1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Father/son has same  birth dates?????
2 CONT
2 CONT Baudouin I De Bailleul (de BELOEIL, SEIGNEUR de BELOEIL)    
2 CONT * Birth:  1100    Bailleul, Orne, Basse-Normandie, France  
2 CONT * Death:  1176  (76)  
2 CONT * Son of Guy de Bailleul  Husband of Plectrude d'Erquinghem
2 CONT * Father of Baudouin de Bailleul
2 CONT
2 CONT Baudouin de Bailleul     
2 CONT * Birth:  1100    Bailleul, Orne, Basse-Normandie, France  
2 CONT * Death:  1146  (46) 
2 CONT * Son of Baudouin I De Bailleul (de BELOEIL, SEIGNEUR de BELOEIL) and Plectrude d'Erquinghem
2 CONT * Husband of Euphémie de Saint-Omer
2 CONT * Father of Baudouin de Bailleul, vicomte d'Ypres and Henri de Bailleul
2 CONT
2 CONT There are two pedigrees of the Flemish family of de Bailleul : one in the collection of genealogical manuscripts in the public library at Douai ; the other, in the sixth volume of ' Bruges et le Franc,' by Gailliard. The latter co
2 CONC mmences with Baudouin deBailleul, who married Euphemie de Saint-Omer; the former begins earlier, and traces the descent of this Baudouin de Bailleul from his great-grandfather, Arnoul de Gramines.
2 CONT
2 CONT This pedigree is erroneous in many particulars; but, is not, perhaps, wholly unworthy of credit. The earlier portion of it is supported in some measure by this, that it includes Albert de Bailleul, whom it states to have been in t
2 CONC he First Crusade ; and the fact that Albert de Bailleul was in the First Crusadeis stated by other authorities.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Douai MS. Arnoul de Gramines, who was living a.d. 980, married Plectrude, daughter of Eripand, Sire de Fauquenberg, by whom he had two sons, 
2 CONT * Hubert and
2 CONT * Simon.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Simon was Chatelainof Bailleul, and was living a.d. 1052. He married the daughter of Geoffroy, Sire de Mervalle, who brought to her husband the lands of Wiersem and Flammertinghem. By her he had two sons,
2 CONT *  Baudouin, Chatelain of Bailleul, and 
2 CONT * Albert ;
2 CONT
2 CONT both of whom went to the Holy Land in 1095, where Albert died in 1096.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Baudouin married Plectrude, daughter of the Seigneur d'Arquenghien, by whom he had two sons, 
2 CONT * Baudry, Chatelain of Bailleul, and 
2 CONT * Baudouin, who married Euphemie, daughter of the Chatelain of Saint-Omer, and was Chatelain of Ardenbourg.
2 CONT
2 CONT A. Arnoul de Gramines.
2 CONT
2 CONT The three generations prior to Baudouin II. in the pedigree rest upon the authority of the Douai manuscript.
2 CONT
2 CONT D. Baudouin II. de Bailleul.
2 CONT
2 CONT The dignity of Chatelain of Bailleul, says Gheldolf, in his ' History of Ypres, Cassel, Bailleul and Warneton,' p. 295, appears to have belonged to a family of that name, whom we find mentioned from the year 1092.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Baudouin de Bailleul married Euphemie, daughter of the Chatelain of Saint-Omer, by whom he had 
2 CONT * Gerard and 
2 CONT * Hoston.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Gerard had two sons, 
2 CONT * Baudouin, who also became Chatelain of Bailleul ; and  
2 CONT * Gerard, who in right of his wife,Virginie, was Chatelain of Oudenbourg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The heirs of Baudouin de Bailleul, son of Gerard and grandson of Baudouin, possessed the two Chatellenies of Ypres and Bailleul until 1295, when Baudouin d'Aubigny and his wife, Agnes, sold, on the 5th May, to Gui de Namur, son of
2 CONC  Count Gui de Dampierre by his second wife, for 3,000 Hvres parisis, the Chatellenie of Bailleul, with all lands, revenues, hommages and other rights appertaining thereto, as also all that they possessed in fief in the territories
2 CONC  of Cassel and Bailleul...
2 CONT
2 CONT Baudouin II. de Bailleul had by his wife, Euphemie de Saint- Omer, two sons and two daughters : viz. 
2 CONT * Gerard,  
2 CONT * Hoston,  
2 CONT * Alix or Adelis and 
2 CONT * Mathilde. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gailliard names another son, Hector, and several other daughters, of whom nothing appears to be known.
2 CONT
2 CONT D. EUPHEMIE DE Saint-Omer
2 CONT
2 CONT was daughter of Guillaume, Chatelain de Saint Omer, Seigneur de Fauquemberge, son of Hoston, Chatelain de Saint-Omer in 1053, ^^^ of Melisende de Picquigny, daughter of Arnould, Vidame of Amiens. Lambin, * Chatelains d'Ypres,' 9.
2 CONT
2 CONT Melisenda de Picquigny, de Nobilissima Regis Francorum, Caroli Magni, stirpe et familia progenita, Arnolphi, vice Domini de Pinkinio filia. 13 Bouquet 429. Ex Lamberti ' Ardensis Historia Ghisnensium Comitum.'
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bailleuls of Flanders, and the Bayleys of Willow Hall (1881) http://archive.org/stream/bailleulsoffland00bayl/bailleulsoffland00bayl_djvu.txt
