2 CONT '''EVERARD [IV] Radou'''l ([1190/1200?]-[8 Jan/Jul] 1226).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis names “Evrardum Raduel” as the son of "Balduinus de Mortania" and his wife "filiam senescalli Flandriæ...Hediardem
2 CONC "[1983].  “Balduinus dominus de Mauritanie et sponsa mea Heldiardis cum filio nostro Radul” donated water adjacent to their church to the abbey du Château by charter dated to [1192][1984].  “Bald. Tornacensis castellanus et Maurit
2 CONC anie dominus” approved donations to Saint-Martin du Château and Saint-Nicolas de Mortagne, made by “Walterus Mausclers miles de Forest”, with the consent of “uxoris nostre Heldiardis et...filii nostri primogeniti Evrardi et alioru
2 CONC m tam filiorum quam filiarum nostrorum”, by charter dated 21 Feb 1208[1985].  Châtelain de Tournai.  Seigneur de Mortagne.  “Evrardus Raddo dominus de Mauritania et castellanus Tornacensis” approved the donation to Tournai Saint-M
2 CONC artin made by “Matheus de Hera” by charter dated 1213[1986].  “Everardus Rodulfus de Mortania castellanus Tornacensis et frater meus Hellinus” confirmed donations to the Templars made by “avus noster bone memorie dominus Everardus
2 CONC  Radolfus...pater etiam noster dominus Balduinus” by charter dated Mar 1215[1987].  “Everardo Radoul domino Mauritanensi castellano Tornacensi” corrected damage done to the church of Tournai by charter dated 1222[1988].  Milon Bis
2 CONC hop of Beauvais notified an agreement concerning various rights between the abbeys of Saint-Amand, Tournai Saint-Martin and Tournai Saint-Nicolas des Prés and “Everardum Radol castellanum Tornacensem” by charter dated 8 Jan 1226[1
2 CONC 989].  He is named as deceased in his brother Hellin’s Aug 1226 charter quoted below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly '''ISABELLE d’Enghien''', daughter of ENGELBERT [III] Seigneur d’Enghien & his wife Ida [Adelaide] d’Avesnes (-1218).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis records that “Evrardum Raduel”, son of "Baldu
2 CONC inus de Mortania" and his wife, married "filiam domini Engelberti de Enghien ex Adelina filia domini Jacobi de Avennes"[1990].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (after 1218) '''ELISABETH [Isabelle] de Courtrai''' Vrouw van Nevele, daughter of ROGER [II] Châtelain de Courtrai & his wife Beatrix van Nevele (-before Mar 1246).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avenn
2 CONC is records that “Evrardum Raduel”, son of "Balduinus de Mortania" and his wife, married secondly "hæredem...terræ de Nevella juxta Gandavum"[1991].  A charter dated Mar 1246 records an arbitration, naming “dame Ysabiaus ki mere fu
2 CONC  mon segneur Mikiel de Niviele mon segneur Evrart Radour et mon segneur Rogier devant dit drois oirs”[1992].  Everard [IV] & his first wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         '''ARNAUD de Mortagne''' (-[Jul 1266/May 1267]).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis records that "alia…soror Sigeri de Einghen una" married "domino Evrardo Radoul domino de Mortania" by whom she ha
2 CONC d "filium Arnulphum"[1993].  Châtelain de Tournai.  Seigneur de Mortagne.  -        see below.  Everard [IV] & his second wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         '''MICHEL de Mortagne''' (-after Mar 1246).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis names “filios [Rodolphum], Michaëlem qui juvenis decessit, et Rogerum” as the sons of “Evrardum Raduel”, son of "Baldu
2 CONC inus de Mortania" and his wife, and his second wife "hæredem...terræ de Nevella juxta Gandavum"[1994].  Heer van Nevele.  A charter dated Mar 1246 records an arbitration, naming “dame Ysabiaus ki mere fu mon segneur Mikiel de Nivi
2 CONC ele [...ki ainnes estoit des freres] mon segneur Evrart Radour et mon segneur Rogier devant dit drois oirs”[1995]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         '''EVERARD Radoul de Mortagne''' (-1276 or after).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis names “filios [Rodolphum], Michaëlem qui juvenis decessit, et Rogerum” as the sons of “Evrardum Raduel”, son of
2 CONC  "Balduinus de Mortania" and his wife, and his second wife "hæredem...terræ de Nevella juxta Gandavum"[1996].   A charter dated Mar 1246 records an arbitration, naming “dame Ysabiaus ki mere fu mon segneur Mikiel de Niviele mon se
2 CONC gneur Evrart Radour et mon segneur Rogier devant dit drois oirs”[1997].  “Ernous sire de Moretaigne et castelains de Tournay” approved the homage by “Rogiers mes frères chevaliers sire d’Espiere” to the bishop of Tournai for “le w
2 CONC ienage d’Espiere”, noting an agreement which had been made between “Radoul men frère...et Huon chevalier chastelain de Gand”, by charter dated Jun 1257[1998].  Heer van Nevele.  m JEANNE de Béthune, daughter of GUILLAUME de Béthun
2 CONC e Seigneur de Pont-Rohard & his wife Elisabeth Dame de Pont-Rohard (-after 1287).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis records that “Evrardi domini de Mortania filii de secundis nuptiis, Rodulphus primogenitus”
2 CONC  married “filiam domini Guilelmi de Betunia domini de Pontroart Joannam” by whom he had "filios...et filias"[1999].   Butkens records that she was living as a widow in 1287[2000].  Everard Radoul & his wife had children:  i)      
2 CONC     [GAUTHIER de Mortagne (-after 1299).  Butkens names Gauthier “mentionné 1287, 1299” as son of “Raoul Châtelain de Courtrai, S. de Nevele” [presumably indicating Everard Radoul], younger son of Everard [IV] Radoul de Tournai wh
2 CONC o is shown above, and his wife “Jenne de Béthune, laquelle estoit veufve 1287”[2001].  Châtelain de Courtrai.  Heer van Nevele.]  -         HEREN van NEVELE.  ii)         [GUILLAUME de Mortagne .  Butkens names “Guillaume de Nevel
2 CONC e Sire de Wervy” as second son of Everard Radoul de Mortagne Châtealin de Courtrai, Heer van Nevele (citing “l’Espinoy, pag. 133”)[2002].  Seigneur de Wervy.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         '''ROGER de Mortagne''' (-after 20 Mar 1272).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis names “filios [Rodolphum], Michaëlem qui juvenis decessit, et Rogerum” as the sons of “Evrardum Raduel” and his seco
2 CONC nd wife "hæredem...terræ de Nevella juxta Gandavum"[2003].   Seigneur d’Espierres [Spiere].  -        SEIGNEURS d’ESPIERRES. 
