1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthold Bathélémy de Nédonchel had married:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 ° Marie d'Ollehain, daughter of Guillaume, Lord of Ollehain, and of Ursule of Colemberg, for whom he founded an obit in the monastery of Saint André;
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 ° Alix , lady of Thiembronne , daughter of Gilbert, lord of Aire .
2 CONT
2 CONT He had two children from the first lady, namely:
2 CONT
2 CONT *A. '''Gilles, 2nd of the name''', which follows, V.
2 CONT *B. Beatrix, died before the month of October 1249, which is proved by the confirmation of '''Alix , Lady of Thiembronne , her mother-in-law,''' in favor of the monks of the monastery of Saint André of the goods of which Béatrix d
2 CONC e Nedonchel was the usufructuary, by virtue of the deed of gift of Barthélemi Nedonchel and his son, Gilles, knight, of the month of June 1246 (3).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * http://racineshistoire.free.fr/LGN/PDF/Nedonchel.pdf
