2 CONT 1.        [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-de-Gavre-Heer-van-Schorisse-Seigneur-d-Escornaix/6000000185362202860 JEAN de Gavre] (-1301).  Goethals confuses him with Jan van Gavre “van den Eyghen”, son of Raso [X] van Gavre Heer va
2 CONC n Liedekerke (see below)[562].  Heer van Schorisse [Seigneur d’Escornaix].  An epitaph at Oudenaarde records the burial of “Jan de Gavre sire d’Escornaij” who died 1301 [?] and “Willemine de Wavrin sa femme”[563].  m [https://www.
2 CONC geni.com/people/Wilhelmine-de-Wavrin/6000000185361590869 WILHELMINE de Wavrin], daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Seigneur-de-Wavrin/6000000185361835865 ROBERT [III] Seigneur de Wavrin] & his wife [https://www.geni.c
2 CONC om/people/Isabelle-de-Croisilles/6000000185362221848 Isabelle de Croisilles].  Guy Count of Flanders granted revenue from “la terre de Wavrin, appartenante à ladite Wilhelmine” to “Jean de Gavre Sire d’Escornay et à madame Willelm
2 CONC ine sa femme” by charter dated 17 Oct 1298[564].  An epitaph at Oudenaarde records the burial of “Jan de Gavre sire d’Escornaij” who died 1301 [?] and “Willemine de Wavrin sa femme”[565].  Jean & his wife had children: https://fmg
2 CONC .ac/Projects/MedLands/FLEMISH%20NOBILITY.htm#ArnaudGavredied1336B
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Arnaud-de-Gavre/6000000185362504831 ARNAUD de Gavre] (-after 31 Mar 1336) son of JEAN de Gavre Seigneur d’Escornaix & his wife Wilhelmine de Wavrin (-after 31 Mar 1336).  Goethals records h
2 CONC is parentage without citing any source which confirms the information [567].  Heer van Schorisse [Seigneur d’Escornaix].  An epitaph at Oudenaarde records the burial of “Arnout de Gavre chlr seigneur d’Escornaij” who died 18 Sep 1
2 CONC 316 [?] and “Cathelijne de Rode dame d’Escornaij et d’Asschove” who died 12 Mar 1314 [?][568]. 
2 CONT m [https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-de-Rodes-dame-d-Escornaij-et-d-Asschove/6000000185361774879 CATHERINE de Rodes], daughter of ---.  Goethals records her family origin and marriage without citing any source which confirms t
2 CONC he information [569].  An epitaph at Oudenaarde records the burial of “Arnout de Gavre chlr seigneur d’Escornaij” who died 18 Sep 1316 [?] and “Cathelijne de Rode dame d’Escornaij et d’Asschove” who died 12 Mar 1314 [?][570]. Arna
2 CONC ud & his wife had children: https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLEMISH%20NOBILITY.htm#ArnaudGavredied1336B
