1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "The House of Humières is an old noble family of feudal origin which takes its name from the seigniory of Humières in Artois and whose main possessions were located in Picardy.
2 CONT This family produced Grand Masters of the Artillery, a Grand Chaplain of France , a Grand Falconer of France, Governors of Picardy and Knights of the Order of the Golden Fleece.
2 CONT Origins 
2 CONT The first mention of this family goes back to Jean d'Humières, lord of Humières and Humereuil in Artois who appears in a title of the year 1150. He had married Richilde de Fosseux with whom he had two sons and a daughter. One of h
2 CONC is sons is cited in 1199 as governor of Artois."
2 CONT [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maison_d%27Humi%C3%A8res#XVe_si%C3%A8cle]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Jean d’Humières ° ~1280 + ~1345
2 CONT seigneur d’Humières et Humeroeuilles
2 CONT ép. ~1302 Jeanne de Nédonchel + ~1338"
2 CONT [http://racineshistoire.free.fr/LGN/PDF/Humieres.pdf]
