2 CONT >>>b)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Roger-de-Gavre/6000000185362744846  ROGER de Gavre] (-21 Oct 1456, bur Gheerdtsberghe).  A charter dated 26 May 1425 records the marriage of “mer Roegier van Schoresse, zoen van wijlen me
2 CONC r Aernout van Gavere, heer in sinen levene van Scoerisse” and “joncvrauwe Johane vanden Bysdome, weduwe Gheraert van de Zijpe”[583].  “Jan van Massemen heer van Kalken” acted as guarantor for “de broers Gerard en Rogier van Gavere
2 CONC -Schorisse” in a charter dated 20 Dec 1433[584].  An epitaph at Gheerdtsberghe records the burial of “Rogier de Gavre d’Escornaij chlr sr de Hoornebeke” who died 21 Oct 1456, a note adding that “hij quarteleert met Ghistelle (gheb
2 CONC roken met Luxrmbourch au premier canton)” (not yet explained)[585].  m ([26 May 1425]) as her second husband, [https://www.geni.com/people/Johanna-de-Gavre/6000000185361748923 JOHANNA vanden Bysdome], widow of [https://www.geni.co
2 CONC m/people/Gerard-van-de-Zijpe/6000000185361330892 GERARD van de Zijpe], daughter of ---.  A charter dated 26 May 1425 records the marriage of “mer Roegier van Schoresse, zoen van wijlen mer Aernout van Gavere, heer in sinen levene 
2 CONC van Scoerisse” and “joncvrauwe Johane vanden Bysdome, weduwe Gheraert van de Zijpe”[586]. https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLEMISH%20NOBILITY.htm#ArnaudGavredied1336B
