2 CONT >>>c)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gerard-de-Gavre/6000000185362481855 GERARD de Gavre] (-1466).  Goethals records his parentage without citing any source which confirms the information[587].  A document dated 3 Apr 1425 n
2 CONC ames “mer Gheraerd van Scoresse here van Mourcourt, Berchem rnfr Ayshove” and “vrouwe Mergriete van Steenhuse vrouwe [van Aishove]”[588].  “Jan van Massemen heer van Kalken” acted as guarantor for “de broers Gerard en Rogier van G
2 CONC avere-Schorisse” in a charter dated 20 Dec 1433[589].  Seigneur de Morcourt-sur-Somme.  Seigneur de Beveren et de Nockere.  Seigneur de Berchem.  The Marquis de Trazegnies records Arnaud’s date of death[590].  m (22 Jun 1408) [htt
2 CONC ps://www.geni.com/people/Margareta-van-Steenhuize-Vrouw-van-Aischove/6000000185361225926 MARGARETA van Steenhuize Vrouw van Aischove], daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Arend-van-Steenhuize-Zwevegem/6000000185362592874 AREN
2 CONC D van Steenhuize-Zwevegem] & his first wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-de-Rochefort-Walcourt/6000000185362807853 Catherine de Rochefort] [Walcourt] (-after 1466).  The Marquis de Trazegnies records her parentage, marri
2 CONC age date, and her husband’s parentage[591].  A document dated 10 Jul 1406 names “Mergriete van Steenhuse...joncvrauwe van Ayshove” and “mer Arend van Steenhuse vader vande vors joncvrauwe”[592].  A document dated 1415 names “Guera
2 CONC rd d’Escournay escuier” and “damoiselle Mergriete de Steenhuse dame de Aeyshove sa femme, bourgeois et bourgeoise de Gand”[593].  A document dated 3 Apr 1425 names “mer Gheraerd van Scoresse here van Mourcourt, Berchem rnfr Ayshov
2 CONC e” and “vrouwe Mergriete van Steenhuse vrouwe [van Aishove]”[594].  “Margareta van Steenhuize en haar echtgenoot Geeraard van Mourcourt, Berchem, Ayshove en Machelen” surrendered Zwevegem to Philippe III Duke of Burgundy by charte
2 CONC r dated 1447[595].  The Marquis de Trazegnies records her husband’s date of death and that Margareta survived him[596]. See-        HEREN van BEVEREN, VICOMTES d’EREBODEGHEM[597]. https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLEMISH%20NOBILIT
2 CONC Y.htm#ArnaudGavredied1336B
