2 CONT 1.         JEAN [I] de Flandre (-after 10 Sep 1439).  Heer van Praet en van der Woestijne.  Espinoy records that “messire Jean de Flandre...avec...sa mere Dame de Zweueghem et de Roosebeke” settled the succession of “messire Louys
2 CONC  son pere en son vivant Seigneur de Praet et de la Woestine” and settled her dower (no date), recorded in a document dated 1431[872].  “Ian van Vlaenderen Heere van Praet ande vander Woestine ende Burghemeesters ende Schepenen van
2 CONC den selven Heerschepe van Praet” issued a charter dated 10 Sep 1439[873].  m JOHANNA van Reigaarsvliet, daughter of HENDRIK van Reigaarsvliet & his wife --- van Schendelbeek.  Père Anselme records her parentage and marriage[874]. 
2 CONC  Vredius quotes a manuscript which records that “Iean de Flandre Seign. de Praet et de la Woestine” married “Ieanne de Reyghersvliet fille de Henry, fils de Gautier”[875].  No primary source has been found which confirms her paren
2 CONC tage and marriage, or her date of death.  Jean & his wife had five children: 
