1 NAME Jean I, de Flandre, Heer van Praet en van der Woestijne
2 GIVN Jean
2 NSFX I, de Flandre, Heer van Praet en van der Woestijne
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 10 SEP 1439
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LOUIS bâtard de Flandre "Friese", illegitimate son of LOUIS II Count of Flanders & his mistress --- de Borre (-killed in battle Nicopolis 28 Sep 1396).  His mother is referred to in the following source: Vredius qu
2 CONC otes a manuscript which records “messire Loys de Frise fils bastard de...Loys de Male conte de Flandre, lequel il eut d’une fille de Monsieur de Borre”[864].  Heer van Praet en van der Woestijne: Espinoy records that Louis II Coun
2 CONC t of Flanders “en avancement de son mariage avec Dame Marie de Guistelles, Dame de Zweueghem et de Rosebeke” granted “les terres et Baronies de Praet et de la Woestine” to his illegitimate son “Messire Louys de Flandres dit le Fri
2 CONC zon” (no source cited)[865].  Vredius quotes a manuscript which records that Louis “eut en partage [la Wostine] par acte du 25 de septembre 1373” [date not confirmed] and died at Nikopolis 28 Sep 1396[866]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m as her first husband, MARIE [Isabelle?] van Gistel Vrouw van Zwevegem, daughter of ROGER van Gistel Heer van Straeten & his wife Elisabeth [Margareta] Vrouw van Dudzele (-after 1431).  Père Anselme records her parentage (naming 
2 CONC her “Marie”) and two marriages (reversing their order) (no sources cited)[867].  As noted above under her husband, Espinoy names her “Dame Marie de Guistelles, Dame de Zweueghem et de Rosebeke”.  Vredius quotes a manuscript which 
2 CONC records that “messire Loys de Frise fils bastard de...Loys de Male conte de Flandre...” married “madame...de Ghistelles...fille de messire --- Seigneur de Dudzeele” who later married “--- de Halewijn”[868].  Vredius quotes another
2 CONC  manuscript which records that Louis married “dame Marie de Guistelles fille de messire Rogier chevalier seign. de Dudzeele, Straten et de Dame Isabeau heretiere de Dudzeele”[869].  Her family origin is confirmed by the arms displ
2 CONC ayed on the epitaph of her granddaughter (by her second marriage) Isabelle.  Some doubt about Marie’s name is introduced by the charter dated 25 Apr 1435 which names “Pierre de Boulers escuier”, married to “Margaretha van Halewijn
2 CONC , de oudste dochter van Jan van Halewijn en Isabella van Gistel”[870].  No “Jean d’Halluin” married to “Isabella van Gistel” has been found.  If Marguerite’s father was Jean d’Halluin Seigneur de Roosebeke (the second husband of “
2 CONC Marie”, see below), maybe his wife was named “Isabelle” not “Marie” (that name being recorded only in secondary sources as noted above).  An indication that this suggestion about Marguerite’s parentage is correct is that “Marie va
2 CONC n Gistel”’s son by her first husband married “Johanna van Reigaarsvliet” (see below), presumably a relative of Marguerite’s husband although the precise family relationship has not been established (see the document FLANDERS NOBIL
2 CONC ITY), as multiple marriages between different members of two noble families are often noted.  She married secondly Jean d’Halluin Seigneur de Roosebeke, Burggraaf van Harelbeke.  Espinoy records that “messire Jean de Flandre...ave
2 CONC c...sa mere Dame de Zweueghem et de Roosebeke” settled the succession of “messire Louys son pere en son vivant Seigneur de Praet et de la Woestine” and settled her dower, recorded in a document dated 1431[871].  This document does
2 CONC  not name “Marie/Isabelle” but it does provide another indication that she was the mother of Marguerite d’Halluin : her second husband died before 1431, indicating the need to settle her dower. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         '''JEAN [I] de Flandre (-after 10 Sep 1439).  Heer van Praet en van der Woestijne.  Espinoy records that “messire Jean de Flandre...avec...sa mere Dame de Zweueghem et de Roosebeke”   settled the succession of “messire 
2 CONC Louys son pere en son vivant Seigneur de Praet et de la Woestine” and settled her dower (no date), recorded in a document dated 1431[872]. [My lord, Jean of Flanders… together with his mother, Lady of Zweueghem and of Roosebeke, s
2 CONC ettled the succession of Sir Louys, his father, in his lifetime Lord of Praet and of la Woestine.” AI TRANSLATION ]   “Ian van Vlaenderen Heere van Praet ande vander Woestine ende Burghemeesters ende Schepenen vanden selven Heersc
2 CONC hepe van Praet” issued a charter dated 10 Sep 1439[873].  m JOHANNA van Reigaarsvliet, daughter of HENDRIK van Reigaarsvliet & his wife --- van Schendelbeek.  Père Anselme records her parentage and marriage[874].  Vredius quotes a
2 CONC  manuscript which records that “Iean de Flandre Seign. de Praet et de la Woestine” married “Ieanne de Reyghersvliet fille de Henry, fils de Gautier”[875].  No primary source has been found which confirms her parentage and marriage
2 CONC , or her date of death.  Jean & his wife had five children:''' 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLANDERS,%20HAINAUT.htm#LouisFlandrePraetdied1396
2 CONT ----
