1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Naam	Jan II van Kuyc 
2 CONT Geboorte	1290  [1] 
2 CONT Occupation	Knape  [1] 
2 CONT Occupation	van 1308 tot 1319  [1]  Heer van Grave 
2 CONT Occupation	van 1308 tot 1319  [2]  Heer van Kuyc 
2 CONT Overlijden	tussen 02-02-1319 en 25-03-1319  [2] 
2 CONT Vader	Hendrik IV van Mierop,   geb. 1260   ovl. 1304, juli (Leeftijd 44 jaar) 
2 CONT Moeder	Aleydis van Diest 
2 CONT Huwelijk	1290  [3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gezin 1	N.N. 
2 CONT Kinderen 	
2 CONT 1. Jan van Kuyc-Mierop   ovl. 1349
2 CONT
2 CONT Gezin 2	N.N. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Internal Sourcing:
2 CONT 1. [S97] J.A. Coldeweij, COLDEWEIJ_1981, (Stichting Zuidelijk Historisch Contact, 1981), 232.
2 CONT 2. [S97] J.A. Coldeweij, COLDEWEIJ_1981, (Stichting Zuidelijk Historisch Contact, 1981), 225, 232.
2 CONT 3. [S97] J.A. Coldeweij, COLDEWEIJ_1981, (Stichting Zuidelijk Historisch Contact, 1981), 231.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: “Jan.” Graafschap-Middeleeuwen.nl, 2025, www.graafschap-middeleeuwen.nl/genealogie/getperson.php?personID=I9195&tree=DGidME_01. Accessed 6 Nov. 2025.
2 CONT …..
2 CONT a)         JAN van Kuyc (-before 10 Oct 1320).  “Johannes dns de Cuyk” established jurisdictional limits in his lands, with the consent of “collateralis nostre...Juthe dne de Cuyk nec non filiorum nostrorum Johannis Sancti Servati
2 CONC i Trajectensis et Lovaniensis ecclesiarum ppti. et Ottonis dni de Zeelehem militis, ac nepotis nostri Johannis de Cuyk”, by charter dated 20 Apr 1308[1309].  Heer van Kuyc.  The testament of “Jutta de Nassau relicta domini Johanni
2 CONC s quondam domini de Kuyc bone memorie”, dated 25 Jan 1312, bequeathed property to “dominum de Kuyc meum nepotem”, sealed by “dominorum Johannis...prepositi et Ottonis militis de Kuyc meorum liberorum, Johannis domini de Kuyc mei n
2 CONC epotis”[1310].  “Johannes dominus de Kuyc” donated property to Marienweerd “per nobilem virum dominum Ottonem de Kuyc nostrum patruum” by charter dated 7 Jul 1318[1311].  The date of his death is ascertained from the charter dated
2 CONC  10 Oct 1320 under which “Otto...dominus de Kuyc” confirmed a donation to Marienweerd contained in a charter issued by himself and “Johanne nostro consanguineo quondam domino de Kuyc”[1312]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Internal Sourcing:
2 CONT [1309] Wap (1858), Oorkonden, p. 245. 
2 CONT [1310] Wap (1858), Oorkonden, p. 257. 
2 CONT [1311] Marienweerd, 191, p. 133. 
2 CONT [1312] Marienweerd, 207, p. 143. 
2 CONT
