1 NAME Simon IV /de Lalaing/ Seigneur de Montigny et de Santes, Chevalier de la Toison d'Or
2 GIVN Simon IV
2 SURN de Lalaing
2 NSFX Seigneur de Montigny et de Santes, Chevalier de la Toison d'Or
2 _MARNM de Lalaing
1 NAME Simon IV de Lalaing, Seigneur de Montigny et de Santes
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC L’église Notre Dame de Deinze
2 ADDR
3 CITY Deinze
3 STAE Vlaanderen
3 CTRY Belgium
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1405
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 MAR 1477
1 OCCU Chevalier de la Toison d'Or,  - Seigneur de Montigny et de Santes,  - Conseiller et chambellan de Philippe le Bon,  - Gouverneur de Beaumont, de Fumay et de Revin,  - bailli d'Amiens,  - admiral et grand-veneur de Flandres,
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT - chevalier de la Toison d'Or, 
2 CONT - seigneur de Montigny et de Hantes, 
2 CONT - conseiller et chambellan de Philippe le Bon, 
2 CONT - gouverneur de Beaumont, de Fumay et de Revin, 
2 CONT - bailli d'Amiens, 
2 CONT - admiral et grand-veneur de Flandres, 
2 CONT - commissaire au renouvellement des magistrats de Flandres, 
2 CONT - capitaine du franc, des deux châteux et ville d'Ecluse dont il soutint le siège en 1435, puis capîtaine de la ville d'Audenarde, qu'il défendit en 1452. 
2 CONT - Il fut ensuite conseiller d'épée au parlement établi à Maline en décembre 1473. Il fut prisonnier de guerre en France en 1531-1532.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000188880045833&size=large}}
2 CONT Armorial équestre Toison d'or - Simon VIII de Lalaing 
2 CONT
2 CONT Available Sources :A van Buchel, 1648, E De Seyn, 1948, L de Herckenrode, 1865, L de Herckenrode, 1868, F Brassart, 1879, FV Goethals, 1862, C Butkens, 1724, A Boterdaele, 1912, de Herckenrode, 1844, J van Helmont, 2005, de Saint 
2 CONC Genois, et al., 1848, FV Goethals, 1849, M Pastoureau et M Popoff, 2001, D Van der Meersch, 1848, P Le Doulx, 1800, Manuscrit H van Heesel, C Sars de Solmont, 1846, B de Ryckman et F de Jonghe, 1956.
2 CONT Birth, Spouse: F Brasssart, 1879.
2 CONT Death: 
2 CONT - E De Seyn, 1948.
2 CONT - L de Herckenrode, 1868.
2 CONT - FV Goethals, 1862.
2 CONT - J de Saint Genois, et al., 184
2 CONT _____
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Simon VI de Lalaing''' ° ~1405 (Lalaing) + 15/03/1477 
2 CONT - knight, lord of Santes and Montigny, 
2 CONT - X the Turks in Cyprus (1426), 
2 CONT - X in France under Jean de Luxembourg, count of Ligny (1429), 
2 CONT - distinguished himself at the Tournament of Arras (02/1430), 
2 CONT - knight of the Golden Fleece (27°, 1431, Chapter of Lille), 
2 CONT - adviser & Chamberlain of Philip II "The Good" then of Charles "The Bold", dukes of Burgundy, 
2 CONT - governor of Beaumont, Fumay and Revin, 
2 CONT - provost (-"Le-Comte") of Valenciennes (1427-1437), 
2 CONT - bailiff of Amiens (1441-1449), 
2 CONT - governor of Luxembourg (1443-1444), 
2 CONT - admiral & Grand-Veneur of Flanders, 
2 CONT - commissioner for the renewal of the magistrates of Flanders, 
2 CONT - captain of the Freehold of Brugge, of the 2 castles & town of L'Ecluse (seat 1435, 1437) & of Oudenarde (seat 1452), 
2 CONT - lieutenant-General of the Great Bastard of Burgundy (crusade, 1464), 
2 CONT adviser of Sword to the parliament (Great Council) of Malines (12/1473) 
2 CONT
2 CONT (breaks his arms of a lion or lionceau of Gules to the 1° rhombus) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ep. 11/06/1441 Jeanne de Gavre-Escornaix, lady of Bracle and Sarladinghe ° ~1425 + 29/05/1478 (daughter of Arnould de Gavre and Marie d'Aumont)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire'' :
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000188858373861&size=large}}
2 CONT Simon was made a knight of the Order of the Golden Fleece in 1431
2 CONT
2 CONT __________
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the most illustrious of the house; for two centuries, the distinguished men it produced shone in the front rank, continuing to make famous the name of Laiaing carried so high by the Good Knight; to write their biography wo
2 CONC uld be to summarize the history of our country under the houses of Burgundy and Austria: for there is not a memorable event in which one of them has not taken part.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SIMON de Lalaing''' 
2 CONT (3rd son of Otte, lord of Lalaing), lord of Montigny (Sint-Christophe), knight of the Golden Fleece in 1431, chamberlain of the duke, provost-count in Valenciennes (1427-1437), bailiff of Amiens (1441-1449), captain or military go
2 CONC vernor of L'Ecluse besieged in 1437 by the rebellious Bruges and in 1452, of Audenarde besieged by the Gantois rebels, having been "cause of the saivation of the aforementioned two cities," lieutenant general of the great bastard 
2 CONC of Burgundy to the crusade of 1464, adviser of sword to the great council of Malines in 1473.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born around 1405, most probably in the castle of Lalaing, he had made his first appearance in 1426, against the Turks, in the kingdom of Cyprus, where he earned his knight's spurs; then in France, in 1429, under the Count of Ligny
2 CONC  (Jean de Luxembourg), a great supporter of the English alliance.
2 CONT
2 CONT The tournament of Arras, in February 1429 (old style), completed to put him in evidence, he "who among a thousand knights was found one of the most beautiful and the biggest, man of very noble house too," says Chastellain, in his 
2 CONC Chronicle (II, page 20).
2 CONT
2 CONT As a cadet, he bore a lion of gules in the first lozenge.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on March 15, 1476 (old style), and lies in the church of the Augustinians of Deynze in Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT From '''Jeanne DE GAVRE-Escornaix''', whom he married around 1436, he had a numerous posterity:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1° '''Josse''', who follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2° '''Arnoul de Lalaing''', doctor in theology and rights, provost of Saint-Sauveur of Harlebeke, in 1459, of Notre-Dame of Bruges (from 1473) and of Saint-Lambert of Liége (67) in 1481 (by market made with Jean de Lalaing, his fi
2 CONC rst cousin), of the private council of Charles the Bold and Maximilian of Austria, professor at the university of Louvain, in whose council he had been admitted in 1473, died in this city, on March 21, 1483, lying in the choir of 
2 CONC the preaching brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT He left a report, written in French, of the meeting of Emperor Frederick III and Duke Charles in Trier in 1473.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3° '''Simon de Lalaing''', knight, mortally wounded before Paris, towards the end of August 1465, buried at the Saints-Innocents, without child of Marie DE SARS, his wife, whom he had married in 1461, daughter of the late Jean, es
2 CONC quire, and of Marguerite de Barbançon dit “de Donstienne” (account of the great bailliage of Hainaut, October 1, 1460 - September 30, 1461, f°s iiij and xlij).
2 CONT
2 CONT "In this time Simon de Lalaing, second (68) son of Mr. Simon de Lalaing, lord of Montigny, was captured and taken to Paris. He died the next day and was buried at the Innocents in Paris. He was still young, so he had seen and trav
2 CONC eled a great deal, such as to the Holy Sepulchre, to Saint James, to Rome, to the Allemaines and to Turkey" (69). So says the lord of Haynin, knight of Hainaut, who also fought in the army of Charles the Bold (Les Mémoires de mess
2 CONC ire Jean, seigneur de Haynin, Mons, 1842, in-8°, I, page 46).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4° '''Philippe de Lalaing''', esquire, who, on March 18, 1453 (v. st.), although being "of the duke's hostel" Philippe le Bon, attended the festival of the Unicorn, given at Cambrai by the count of SaintPol, who was then ill-regar
2 CONC ded at court, so much so that the duke had forbidden his people to appear at these jousts (Mathieu d'Escouchy, Chronique, II, page 239). He died of the plague in Marseille, around Christmas 1464, during the crusade of the great ba
2 CONC stard of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5° '''François de Lalaing''', squire, died of the plague and was buried in Marseille, next to his brother. In such a way that the lieutenant of the great bastard/ "messire Simon de Lalaing, lost two beautiful squires, his children
2 CONC : who was a pity, and to dur carried it" (Chastellain, Chronique, V, page 47).
2 CONT
2 CONT 6° '''Jean de Lalaing''', knight, having been armed by the hand of Duke Charles, at the siege of Neuss in Germany, on May 23, 1475, the day of the battle against the emperor (Molinet, I, page 129). Chamberlain of the duke, captain
2 CONC  of an ordinance company, he was killed at the disaster of Granson, against the Swiss, on March 2, 1476 (old style).
2 CONT
2 CONT 7° '''Philippotte de Lalaing''', canoness of Mons in 1454, married, after 1479, to Jean DE LANNOY, knight, lord of Maingoval, father and mother of the famous Charles de Lannoy, viceroy of Naples, who took the king François I at Pa
2 CONC via.
2 CONT
2 CONT (67) liste des prévôts de Liége est très-défectueuse dans le Gallia christiana, (Paris, 1725, in-f°), III, col. 922; au lieu de de ceux ci : Jean de Lalaing, 1443, 1446 ; Evrard de La Mark, vers 1450; Antoine de Lalaing ; Arnould 
2 CONC de Lalaing prétendu frère du précédent, 1191 ; Hugues de Lalaing élu en 1481, mort en 1483, — il faut mettre ces deux seulement: Jean de Lalaing, 1413-1481, et Arnoul de Lalaing, 1481-1483.
2 CONT Toutefois il est probable que Jean reprit sa prévoté après la mort d'Arnoul, puisqu'en 1484 il aurait assisté à un synode qui se tint dans l'église de Notre-Dame-aux-Fonts à Liége (Annales de l'Académie d'archéologie de Belgique, 
2 CONC Anvers, 1862, in-8°, XIX, p.482).
2 CONT (68) Les généalogies s'accordant pour donner le second rang à Arnoul, « qui fut d'église », nous le lui conservons, malgré le témoignage de Jean de Haynin.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 57-6
2 CONC 0.''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SIMON de Lalaing''', son of OSTE de Lalaing & his wife Yolande de Barbançon Dame de Hantes (-15 Mar 1477, bur Deinze).  Seigneur de Montigny.  “Simon de Lalaing seigneur de Montigny chevalier...Guillaume seigneur de Lalaing aus
2 CONC si chevalier...son frère” made declarations as “curateur aux biens vacants de feu...Jacques de Lalaing” by charter dated 3 Apr 1469[529].  An epitaph at Deinze, near Gent records the burial of “Simon de Lalaing chevalier seigneur 
2 CONC de Montigny et de Santes fondateur de cette église et Jeanne d’Escornaix dame de Bracle et Salardinghe sa femme”, providing brief biographical details, who died 15 Mar 1476 and 29 May 1478 respectively[530]. 
2 CONT m ([1436]) '''JEANNE de Gavre''' Dame d’Escornaix, de Bracle et de Salardinghe, daughter of ARNAUD de Gavre Baron d’Escornaix & his wife Marie d’Aumont Dame de Bracle et de Salardinghe (-29 May 1478, bur Deinze).  Brassart records
2 CONC  her parentage and marriage, without citing the sources on which the information is based[531].  An epitaph at Deinze, near Gent records the burial of “Simon de Lalaing chevalier seigneur de Montigny et de Santes fondateur de cett
2 CONC e église et Jeanne d’Escornaix dame de Bracle et Salardinghe sa femme”, providing brief biographical details, who died 15 Mar 1476 and 29 May 1478 respectively[532]. 
2 CONT Simon & his wife had seven children: 
2 CONT 1.         '''JOSSE de Lalaing''' (-Utrecht 5 Aug 1483, bur Deinze).  Seigneur de Montigny.  Stadhouder of Holland 1480.  An epitaph at Deinze records the burial of “Josse de Lalaing baron et seigneur dudict lieu, seigneur de Mont
2 CONC igny et Santes, Bracle, Salardingue” who married “Bonne de la Vieville fille et héritière de...Louis des Sains, de Berles, d’Orvillers, de Meurepas, en la comté d’Arthois...” and died Aug 1483, and includes some brief biographical
2 CONC  details[533].  In a charter dated 15 Dec 1515, [his son] “Charles baron de Lalaing d’Escorany...” ratified obits at Lalaing in memory of “son feu...pere Monseigneur Josse signeur de Lalaing en son temps gouverneur de Hollande...”
2 CONC  who died 5 Aug 1483 “au siege devant la cite dUtrecq et son corps enterre au cloistre Dainze en Flandre”[534].  m BONNE de la Viesville Dame de Sains, de Tangry et de Maurepas, daughter of LOUIS de la Viesville Seigneur de Sains 
2 CONC et de Tangry et de Maurepas châtelain de Bapaume & his wife Marguerite du Bos Dame de Maurepas et de Villers (-2 Mar 1503).  An epitaph at Deynze records the burial of “Josse de Lalaing baron et seigneur dudict lieu, seigneur de M
2 CONC ontigny et Santes, Bracle, Salardingue” who married “Bonne de la Vieville fille et héritière de...Louis des Sains, de Berles, d’Orvillers, de Meurepas, en la comté d’Arthois...”[535].  In a charter dated 15 Dec 1515, [her son] “Ch
2 CONC arles baron de Lalaing d’Escorany...” ratified obits at Lalaing in memory of “son feu...pere Monseigneur Josse signeur de Lalaing...Bonne de la Viefville son espeuse” who died 2 Mar 1503, and for “Jacqueline de Luxembourg son espe
2 CONC use”[536].  Josse & his wife had children: 
2 CONT a)         '''CHARLES de Lalaing''' ([1466]-Oudenaarde 17 Jul 1525, bur Douai, l’église des Dames de l’Abbaye-des-Prés).  He succeeded his cousin Jean in 1498 as Seigneur de Lalaing.  In a charter dated 15 Dec 1515, “Charles baron
2 CONC  de Lalaing d’Escorany, pers de Haynaut, seigneur Descussigniz, chevalier de lordre de la Thoison dOr...” ratified obits at the church of Lalaing in memory of “son feu...pere Monseigneur Josse signeur de Lalaing en son temps gouve
2 CONC rneur de Hollande...” who died 5 Aug 1483 “au siege devant la cite dUtrecq et son corps enterre au cloistre Dainze en Flandre” and “Bonne de la Viefville son espeuse” who died 2 Mar 1503, and for “Jacqueline de Luxembourg son espe
2 CONC use”[537].  Baron de Lalaing 1508.  Comte de Lalaing 1522.  An epitaph at l’église des Dames de l’Abbaye-des-Prés records the burial of “Charles comte de Lalaing baron d’Escornaix, seigneur de Brakele de saint Aulbin en Douai” who
2 CONC  married “Jacqueline de Luxembourg...” and died 17 Jul 1525 “audit chasteau d’Audenarde”, and includes some brief biographical details[538].  m (before 1494) JACQUELINE de Luxembourg Dame de Ville, daughter of JACQUES de Luxembour
2 CONC g Seigneur de Fiennes et de Gavre & his wife Marie de Berlaimont Dame de Ville, de la Hamaide et de Vasières (-after 1515).  In a charter dated 15 Dec 1515, [her husband] “Charles baron de Lalaing d’Escorany...” ratified obits at 
2 CONC Lalaing for “Jacqueline de Luxembourg son espeuse”[539].  Charles & his wife had children: 
2 CONT i)          JACQUES de Lalaing (-30 Oct 1521, bur Beaumont, Valenciennes).  “Charles baron de Lalaing...” granted property at Valenciennes to “Jacques de Lallaing seigneur Descornetz son fil aisne” by charter dated 1 Jul 1518[540]
2 CONC .  An epitaph at l’église des Dames de Beaumont, Valenciennes records the burial of “Jacques fils aîné de Charles de Lalaing seigneur d’Ecornaix capitaine d’Audenarde...” who died 30 Oct 1521 “en revenant du siège de Maisiere”[541
2 CONC ]. 
2 CONT ii)         CHARLES de Lalaing ([1506]-Brussels 21 Nov 1558, bur Lalaing).  Comte de Lalaing. 
2 CONT -         see below. 
2 CONT iii)        MARGUERITE de Lalaing (Oudenaarde Sep 1508-1602).  The Catalogue des Lalaing records her parentage and marriage[542].  m EVRARD Seigneur de Pallant, son of ---. 
2 CONT iv)       PHILIPPE de Lalaing (-30 Jun 1555, bur Hoogstraten).  “Philippe van Lalaing baron van Schorisse” confirmed receiving property from “Anthonyse van Lalaing ridder...grave van Hooghstraeten heere van Montigny, van Culemborc
2 CONC h, Borsele ende van vrouwe Elizabeth van Culembourg gravine van Hooghstraten zyne...geselline” by charter dated 6 Aug 1534[543]. 
2 CONT -         see below, GRAVEN van HOOGSTRATEN. 
2 CONT v)        ANNE de Lalaing .  The Catalogue des Lalaing records her parentage and marriage[544].  m JOSSE Comte de Montfort, son of ---. 
2 CONT b)         ANTOINE de Lalaing ([1480]-Gent 2 Apr 1540, bur Hoogstraten).  Seigneur de Montignies-Saint-Christophe[545].  Stadhouder of Holland 1522.  Heer van Hoogstraten, de iure uxoris.  Graaf van Hoogstraten 15 Jun 1518.  Epita
2 CONC ph.  m (11 Apr 1509) as her second husband, ELISABETH van Culemborg Vrouwe van Culemborg, Hoogstraten, Borsselen en Zuylen, widow of JEAN de Luxembourg Seigneur de Ville, daughter of GASPAR Heer van Culemborg & his wife Jeanne de 
2 CONC Bourgogne (-9 Dec 1555). 
2 CONT 2.         '''ARNOUL de Lalaing''' (-Louvain 21 Mar 1483, bur Louvain Dominicans).  Prévôt de Harlebeke Saint-Sauveur 1459, of Bruges Notre-Dame 1473, and of Liège Saint-Lambert 1481[546]. 
2 CONT 3.         '''SIMON de Lalaing''' (-Paris end-Aug 1465, bur Paris Saints-Innocents).  Seigneur de Hantes.  The Mémoires of Jean Seigneur de Hénin records that, after being wounded, “Simon de Lalaing, second fils de...Simon de Lala
2 CONC ing seigneur de Montigny” was brought to Paris, died from his wounds the next day, and was buried “aux Innocents audict Paris”[547].  m (1461) MARIE de Sars, daughter of JEAN Seigneur de Sars et du Maisnil & his wife Marguerite de
2 CONC  Barbançon.  The Catalogue des Lalaing records her parentage and marriage[548]. 
2 CONT 4.         '''PHILIPPE de Lalaing''' (-Marseille [25] Dec 1464, bur Marseille). 
2 CONT 5.         '''FRANÇOIS de Lalaing''' (-Marseille [1464], bur Marseille). 
2 CONT 6.         '''JEAN de Lalaing''' (-killed in battle Grandson 2 Mar 1477). 
2 CONT 7.         '''PHILIPPOTTE de Lalaing''' ).  The Catalogue des Lalaing records her parentage and marriage[549].  m (after 1479) JEAN de Lannoy Seigneur de Maingoval, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Cawley, Charles. “NORTHERN FRANCE-CAMBRAI, DOUAI, VALENCIENNES.” Medieval Lands, Foundation for Medieval Genealogy, 24 Mar. 2022, https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfracado.htm#_Toc44147371''
2 CONT __________
