1 OCCU Jean I de Luxembourg, seigneur de Ligny, Count of Ligny, Count of Luxembourg
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} JEAN I (died at the Battle of Cocherel), Lord of Ligny, Roussy & Beauvoir 1354-1364  LUXEMBOURG-LIGNY (de) 1313-1364
2 CONT
2 CONT www.wikipedia.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean I of Luxembourg, born around 1300, died May 17, 1364, was lord of Ligny-en-Barrois, Roussy and Beauvoir from 1354 to 1364. He was son of Waléran II, lord of Ligny, and Guyotte of Lille .
2 CONT
2 CONT Union and posterity 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1330 he married Alix de Dampierre (1322 † 1346), lady of Richebourg and d'Ailly, daughter of Guy de Richebourg, lord of Richebourg, d'Armentières, Ailly and Houdan (younger son of Guillaume), and Béatrice de Putten, Guy de Rich
2 CONC ebourg's second wife (rather than Marie d'Enghien daughter of Gérard II d'Enghien-Zotteghem, said by some sources to be Guy's first wife), and he had: Guy (1340 † 1371) count of Ligny, lord of Roussy, de Beauvoir, Richebourg and d
2 CONC 'Ailly, count of St-Pol by his marriage to the countess Mahaut de Châtillon-St-Pol, sister of Guy below. Jean († 1360), lord of Roussy John (1342 † 1373), archbishop of Mainz (1371-1373) Henri (1344 † 1366) canon in Cologne and Ca
2 CONC mbrai Waléran, cited in 1347 Jacques Jeanne († 1392), countess of Faucquenberghe, married to: 1.Guy de Châtillon († 1360), count of Saint-Pol 2.Guy VIII († 1427), baron of La Rochefoucauld
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie dame de Houdan (1337 † 1376/1382), married to Henri V de Vaudémont (1327 † 1365), sire de Joinville, count of Vaudémont Philippote († 1359), married to Raoul, sire de Reineval Catherine († 1366), married to Daniel de Halewyn
2 CONC  († 1365)
2 CONT
2 CONT Widowed, he remarried again with Jeanne Bacon, lady of Molay Bacon, daughter of Roger VI Bacon, lord of Molay Bacon and baron of Normandy, but they had no descendants
