2 CONC 30-1713). Continuateur Contributor : Simplicien (1683 ?-1759 ; augustin). Éditeur scientifique Contributor : Ange de Sainte-Rosalie (1655-1726 ; augustin déchaussé). Éditeur scientifique -Editable Google book here: https://www.goo
2 CONC gle.com/books/edition/_/B6IcDp-zIUAC?hl=en&gbpv=1.
2 CONT .....
2 CONT Research Notes:
2 CONT verwierf het genot van de heerlijkheid Boelare na het overlijden van heer echtgenoot
2 CONT >She acquired the enjoyment of the estate of Boelare after the death of her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes:
2 CONT 1. There is no historical record of a Robert de Leeuwergem (seigneur de Leeuwergem) marrying a Marie van Halewijn.
2 CONT 2. Robert vs. Ghiselbrecht: The 15th-century Lord of Leeuwergem was Ghiselbrecht (d. c. 1461), not Robert.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Gemini AI
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta van Halewijn (daughter of Wouter van Halewijn and Jacqueline de Wissocq) married Ghiselbrecht van Leeuwergem, the Seigneur (Lord) of Leeuwergem.
2 CONT '''Marriage and Legacy'''
2 CONT The union between Margareta and Ghiselbrecht was a critical genealogical event for the lordship of Leeuwergem. Ghiselbrecht served as the Lord of Leeuwergem until his death around 1461.
2 CONT Sole Heiress: They had a daughter, Isabeau (Isabella) van Leeuwergem, who became the sole heiress of the Leeuwergem estate.
2 CONT Transfer to House of Lannoy: Isabeau married Jan de Lannoy (1410–1493), a prominent Flemish statesman and Knight of the Golden Fleece. Through this marriage, the seigneury of Leeuwergem officially passed from the van Leeuwergem fa
2 CONC mily to the House of Lannoy.
2 CONT '''Genealogical Summary'''
2 CONT Parents: Wouter (Gautier) van Halewijn & Jacqueline de Wissocq.
2 CONT Spouse: Ghiselbrecht van Leeuwergem (Lord of Leeuwergem).
2 CONT Child: Isabeau van Leeuwergem (married Jan de Lannoy).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This specific Margareta should not be confused with her contemporary Margareta van Halewijn (of Comines), who was the daughter of Colard de La Clyte and married Olivier van Halewijn.'''
