2 NOTE The reason this exact shield is what you recognized on the Auteuil alliance keystone for Louis #2 is because of the internal branch inheritance of the Piennes track:
3 CONT The Fief Origin: This specific blue shield with the golden fess and six billets belongs to the Lordship of Piennes.
3 CONT Percival's Rights: Percival de Halewijn carried these exact arms because he held dominion over these parallel family seigneuries (Ascq, Annappes, etc.) tied to the exact same Piennes cadet pool.
3 CONT Louis #2's Rights: When Louis #2 solidified his standing as the Lord of Piennes, he bore this exact same fess-and-billet inescutcheon in abîme on his coat of arms.
3 CONT By finding this clean, un-impaled image of the Piennes-Halewijn shield, you have found the exact graphic asset you need for Louis #2's individual profile page!
