1 NAME Philippe /de Lalaing/
2 GIVN Philippe
2 SURN de Lalaing
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Marseille
3 STAE Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur
3 CTRY France
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT DEC 1464
2 ADDR
3 CITY Marseille
3 STAE Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur
3 CTRY France
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes
2 CONT Ecuyer. Il mourut de la peste à Marseille vers noël 1464.
2 CONT Source : F Brassart, 1879.
2 CONT Death: F Brasssart, 1879.
2 CONT _____
2 CONT '''Philippe de Lalaing''' + late 12/1464 (Marseille) 
2 CONT - squire, 
2 CONT took part in the Crusade of the Grand-Bastard of Burgundy (which targeted Turkey but never got there)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire'' :
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Philippe de Lalaing''', esquire, who, on March 18, 1453 (v. st.), although being "of the duke's hostel" Philippe le Bon, attended the festival of the Unicorn, given at Cambrai by the count of SaintPol, who was then ill-regarded
2 CONC  at court, so much so that the duke had forbidden his people to appear at these jousts (Mathieu d'Escouchy, Chronique, II, page 239). He died of the plague in Marseille, around Christmas 1464, during the crusade of the great basta
2 CONC rd of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 59.'
2 CONC '
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''PHILIPPE de Lalaing''' (-Marseille [25] Dec 1464, bur Marseille).
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Cawley, Charles. “NORTHERN FRANCE-CAMBRAI, DOUAI, VALENCIENNES.” Medieval Lands, Foundation for Medieval Genealogy, 24 Mar. 2022, https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfracado.htm''
