2 CONT '''François de Lalaing''' + end 12/1464 (Marseille, plague)
2 CONT - squire,
2 CONT participates in the Crusade of the Grand Bastard of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire'' :
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''François de Lalaing''', squire, died of the plague and was buried in Marseille, next to his brother. In such a way that the lieutenant of the great bastard/ "messire Simon de Lalaing, lost two beautiful squires, his children: w
2 CONC ho was a pity, and to dur carried it" (Chastellain, Chronique, V, page 47).
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 60.'
