1 NAME Jehan de Lalaing, Bâtard de Lalaing
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} X) '''Jehan, Bâtard de Lalaing'''
2 CONT fl 1456 peut-être Bailli d’Haubourdin
2 CONT (brise ses armes d’une barre de sinople)
2 CONT ép. Péronne Guilbaut (fille de Jehan, d’un lignage lillois dont un, Gui, Trésorier des Finances ducales)
2 CONT (ses armes : «D’argent, au chevron d’azur à l’aigle de gueules au canton dextre»)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT ..1° (bis)." Jehan de Lalaing, b. [bastard; would it not be rather bailli?] of Haubourdin, lived in the year 1456, husband of Peronne GUILBAUT, daughter of the late Jehan"; he broke the shield of Lalaing with a bar of vert, and hi
2 CONC s wife bore: Argent with a chevron of azure with an eagle of gules in the dexter canton (large genealogical table of the Cabinet of titles). The Guilbauts were from Lille. Another Péronne Guilbaut, daughter of Guy, treasurer of th
2 CONC e finances of the duke, died about 1430, was the first wife of Bauduin d' Ongnies, governor of Lille.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 46.'
2 CONC '
