1 NAME Jean /de Lannoy/
2 GIVN Jean
2 SURN de Lannoy
2 _MARNM de Lannoy
1 NAME Jean III, seigneur de Lannoy
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 27 APR 1410
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 MAR 1493
1 OCCU Gouverneur van Holland, ridder van het gouden vlies
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://www.genealogieonline.nl/stamboom-familie-kuipers/I68918.php '''genealogieonline.nl....'''] ; [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_de_Lannoy '''en.wikipedia.org....'''] ; 
2 CONT * Jan III van Lannoy (1410-1493) was a Flemish statesman in the service of the Dukes of Burgundy.
2 CONT * He was the son of Jan II of Lannoy (killed in the Battle of Azincourt) and Jeanne de Croÿ, daughter of Jean I de Croÿ, also killed at Azincourt.
2 CONT * As a young man, Jan III had a military career, fighting against the Prince-Bishopric of Liège (1430), England (1436), Lorraine (1440) and the Electorate of Cologne (1447).
2 CONT * In 1448 he was appointed by Philip the Good as stadtholder of the County of Holland and Zeeland, a function he held until 1462. Between 1459 and 1463, he was also stadtholder of Walloon Flanders.
2 CONT * In 1451 he became a '''Knight in the Order of the Golden Fleece'''. In 1452-53 he participated in the submission of the Revolt of Ghent (1449–1453).
2 CONT * In 1468 he came into conflict with Duke Charles the Bold because of his good contacts with the French Court. He was forced to flee, but later reconciated with Charles.
2 CONT * In 1477 he served Maximilian I of Austria as Chamberlain and conducted several diplomatic missions. He played a very important role in the conclusion of the Treaty of Arras (1482).
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________
2 CONT *'''Sir Jean de Lannoy, Seigneur de Lannoy, Lis, Rumes, & Sebourg, Governor of Lille, Douai, & Orchies, Bailiff of Amiens, Ambassador to England1,2
2 CONT *'''M, #85837, b. 27 April 1410, d. 18 March 1493
2 CONT *Father	Sir Jean de Lannoy, Seigneur de Lannoy, Lys, Mingoval, & Wattignies, Governor of Lille3,2 d. 25 Oct 1415
2 CONT *Mother	Jeanne de Croy3,2
2 CONT *     Sir Jean de Lannoy, Seigneur de Lannoy, Lis, Rumes, & Sebourg, Governor of Lille, Douai, & Orchies, Bailiff of Amiens, Ambassador to England was born on 27 April 1410.4,2 He married Jeanne de Poix''', daughter of Sir Louis d
2 CONC e Poix, Seigneur de Brimeu, St. Maxent, & Huppy and Jeanne de Mélusse, '''before 2 April 1429.1,2 Sir Jean de Lannoy, Seigneur de Lannoy, Lis, Rumes, & Sebourg, Governor of Lille, Douai, & Orchies, Bailiff of Amiens, Ambassador to
2 CONC  England married Jeanne de Ligny''', daughter of Michel III, Seigneur de Florennes, Barbancon, Maulde sur l'Escaut, & Ponthois, Marshal of Hennegau, Sire de Ligny and Bonne d' Abbeville, '''circa 1460.2 Sir Jean de Lannoy, Seigneu
2 CONC r de Lannoy, Lis, Rumes, & Sebourg, Governor of Lille, Douai, & Orchies, Bailiff of Amiens, Ambassador to England died on 18 March 1493 at age 82; Buried at Lannoy.4,5,2
2 CONT *'''Family 1     Jeanne de Poix d. 25 Jun 1459
2 CONT *Child	
2 CONT **Jeanne de Lannoy+1,2 d. b 1475
2 CONT *'''Family 2     Jeanne de Ligny d. 15 Mar 1494
2 CONT *Children	
2 CONT **Bonne de Lannoy+2,6 d. 22 Apr 1543
2 CONT **Marie de Lannoy+7,2 b. c 1465
2 CONT *Citations
