1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Guy of Luxembourg       Born:    c. 1340      Died:    1371	
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: •Jean of Luxembourg (c. 1300-1364)        
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: •Alix of Flanders (Dampierre) (c. 1322-1346)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:  1354 to Mahaut of Chatillon (c. 1335-1378)    
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:  
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe de Luxembourg    
2 CONT
2 CONT  **     Marie of Luxemburg (bef. 1340- ) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:  Jean de Luxembourg (Limburg) (1370-1397)    
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:  Count of Luxembourg, St. Pol, Roussy and Fiennes. Killed in action at Baesweiler.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jgshepherd.net/page84.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT  Guy de Luxembourg   
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy was born in 1337 in Ligny et Barrois, Meuse, France.  Guy's father was Duke Jean de Luxembourg and his mother was Alix de Dampierre-Flandre, dame de Richebourg.  His paternal grandparents were Waleran de Luxembourg II and Guyo
2 CONC tte de Lille.  He was an only child.  He died at the age of 34 on August 22nd, 1371.
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy de Luxembourg, who was born in 1340 and died in 1371, was comte de Saint-Pol from 1360 to 1371 and comte de Ligny, Lord of Roussy de Beauvoir and 1364 to 1371. He was the son of John I, lord of Ligny, and Alix de Dampierre-Fla
2 CONC nders, Lady Richebourg.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in 1354 Mahaut de Chatillon (1335 † 1378), Countess de Saint-Pol, daughter of Jean de Chatillon, Comte de Saint-Pol and Jeanne de Fiennes, and had:
2 CONT
2 CONT      * Waleran III (1356 † 1415), Count of Ligny and Saint-Pol.
2 CONT
2 CONT      * Pierre (1369 † 1387), bishop of Metz and cardinal
2 CONT
2 CONT      * Jean (1370 † 1397), Lord de Beauvoir and marriage Count de Brienne and Conversano. He is the author of the younger branch of Saint-Pol and the father of Pierre de Luxembourg, Comte de Saint-Pol, and Jean de Luxembourg, Comt
2 CONC e de Ligny
2 CONT
2 CONT      * André (1396), bishop of Cambrai
2 CONT
2 CONT      * Mary, married to Jean de Conde († 1391), and then to Simon, Comte de Salm († 1397)
2 CONT
2 CONT      * Jeanne († 1430), Countess of Ligny and Saint-Pol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestor Pedigree Chart
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy's family with Maud de Chatillon
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy and Maud were married in a religious ceremony in 1354 in Lille,Nord, France.  They had a son named Jean.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT   Jean de Luxembourg, Lord of Beauvoir
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean was born in 1370 in Beauvoir, Picardy, France.  He died at the age of 27 in 1397 in Luxembourg.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://gw.geneanet.org/jpduf65?lang=en&iz=4&p=guy&n=de+luxembourg+ligny Geneanet Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 29 2023, 14:08:43 UTC''
