1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katherine_Swynford
2 CONT *Katherine Swynford
2 CONT *Children and descendants
2 CONT *By Hugh Swynford:
2 CONT **Blanche Swynford (born 1 May 1363), named for the Duchess of Lancaster, and also a godchild of John of Gaunt.
2 CONT **Margaret Swynford (born c. 1364), became a nun at the prestigious Barking Abbey in 1377 with help from her future stepfather John of Gaunt, where she lived the religious life with her cousin Elizabeth Chaucer, daughter of the fa
2 CONC mous Geoffrey Chaucer and Katherine's sister Philippa de Roet.
2 CONT **?Dorothy Swynford (born c. 1366). -- It should be noted that there are no contemporary references to any person so named at that time.
2 CONT **''''''Thomas Swynford (24 February 1367–1432), born in Lincoln while his father Sir Hugh Swynford was away on a campaign with John of Gaunt in Castile fighting for Peter of Castile.
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *http://www.thepeerage.com/p10732.htm#i107320
2 CONT *''''''Sir Thomas Swynford1
2 CONT *M, #107320, b. 24 February 1372/73, d. 2 April 1432
2 CONT *Last Edited=3 Jul 2009
2 CONT *     ''''''Sir Thomas Swynford was born on 24 February 1372/73 at Lincoln, Lincolnshire, England.2 He was baptised on 25 February 1372/73 at Lincoln, Lincolnshire, England.2 He was the son of Sir Hugh Swynford and Katherine Roët.
2 CONC 1 He married, firstly, Jane Crophill.1 He married, secondly, Margaret Grey, daughter of Henry Grey, 5th Lord Grey (of Wilton) and Elizabeth Talbot, before 12 July 1421.3 He died on 2 April 1432 at age 59.2
2 CONT *     ''''''Sir Thomas Swynford was invested as a Knight.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 102. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *2.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume IV, page 64. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *3.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1665. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1534.htm#i46092
2 CONT *''''''Sir Thomas Swinford1
2 CONT *M, b. circa 1368, d. 2 April 1432
2 CONT *Father Sir Hugh Swynford1 b. c 1340, d. 13 Nov 1371 
2 CONT *Mother Katherine Roet1 b. 25 Nov 1340, d. 10 May 1403 
2 CONT *     ''''''Sir Thomas Swinford was born circa 1368 at of Kettlethorpe, Lincolnshire, England.1 He married Margaret Grey, daughter of Sir Henry de Grey, 5th Lord Grey of Wilton and Elizabeth Talbot, before 12 July 1421; They had o
2 CONC ne son, William.1 Sir Thomas Swinford died on 2 April 1432.1
2 CONT *Family Margaret Grey b. c 1381, d. 1 Jun 1454 
2 CONT *Child 
2 CONT *◦William Swinford+1 b. a 1421
2 CONT
2 CONT ——
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas Swinford, Sheriff of Lincoln, Governor of Calais was born circa 1368 at of Kettlethorpe, Lincolnshire, England; Age 4 in 1372.1,2,5 He married Joan Crophill before 14 October 1399; They had
2 CONT
2 CONT *1 son (Sir Thomas) and 
2 CONT *1 daughter (Katherine, wife of Sir William Drury, & of Thomas Curzon, Esq.)3,2,5,6 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas Swinford, Sheriff of Lincoln, Governor of Calais married Margaret Grey, daughter of Sir Henry de Grey, 5th Lord Grey of Wilton and Elizabeth Talbot, before 12 July 1421;  They had 
