2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/publications32chauuoft/publications32chauuoft_djvu.txt
2 CONT *in Nocton and Dunston, just outside the city of Lincoln. 1 An Edmund and a Norman do Swynford, who possessed lands in Lincolnshire, are mentioned about the same time. 2 In 1361 Sir Thomas de Swynford was succeeded in various Linc
2 CONC olnshire properties by Hugh, his son and heir, then aged 21 years. ''''''In 1372 Sir Hugh Swynford died seised of the same, leaving Katherine his widow, and Thomas his son and heir, aged four years. 1 This last was the Sir Thomas 
2 CONC before mentioned, who was contemporary with Thomas Chaucer. He died in 1432, leaving another Sir Thomas, his son and heir, aged 26. His widow, Margery, was wife of Sir John Darcy in 1441''''''. 
