2 NOTE This is the double casket for Katherine de Roet Duchess of Lancaster died 1403 and her daughter by John of Gaunt named Joan Beaufort. In 1977 apparently the wooden first casket for Katherine was situated at the High Alter of Linco
3 CONC ln Cathedral, England for all to see. But the wood was crumbling and has probably been removed. Before Joan died a will was written calling for her mother's grave to be enclosed together with Joan's body. That resulted in the doub
3 CONC le tomb which was enclosed in the Choir of Angels at the High Alter behind a wrought iron screen created around 1440. The actual intact graves are probably still under the floor of the tomb. [Weir 2007, pp. 277–278]
