1 NOTE CARDINAL BEAUFORT
1 NOTE Henry Beaufort (1377-1447), English cardinal, natural son of John of Gaunt by Catherine, widow of Sir Hugh Swynford. He was thrice chancellor. In 1431 he conducted the young king, Henry VI, to France, to be crowned in Paris as kin
2 CONC g of France and England. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordained and appointed Dean of Wells in 1397; Bishop of Lincoln in 1398. Promoted to Chancellor of Oxford University and Bishop of Winchester in 1405. Chancellor of England. Cardinal-Priest of Saint Eusebius in 1426. He was also l
2 CONC egat a latere in Hungary, Bohemia and the Empire. He reportedly died unmarried and without issue. {Burke�s Peerage} But recorders of the ancestry of Presidents John Quicy Adams and John Adams have a relationship with Alice FitzAla
2 CONC n and a daughter Jane. {Iain Kerr compiler} [GADD.GED]
1 NOTE Cardinal Henry Beaufort
