1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Research Notes:
2 CONT 1. The union between Margareta and Ghiselbrecht was a critical genealogical event for the lordship of Leeuwergem. Ghiselbrecht served as the Lord of Leeuwergem until his death around 1461.
2 CONT Sole Heiress: They had a daughter, Isabeau (Isabella) van Leeuwergem, who became the sole heiress of the Leeuwergem estate.
2 CONT 2. Transfer to House of Lannoy: Isabeau married Jan de Lannoy (1410–1493), a prominent Flemish statesman and Knight of the Golden Fleece. Through this marriage, the seigneury of Leeuwergem officially passed from the van Leeuwergem
2 CONC  family to the House of Lannoy.
