2 NICK Comte de Beaurieu
1 NAME Charles de Gavre, comte de Beaurieux
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1525
2 PLAC Belgium or northern France
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1610
2 PLAC Belgium or northern France
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Charles de Gavre, comte de Beaurieux=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Louis de Gavre, Heer van Frésin, Ollignies, Mussain, Inchy and Jeanne de Rubempré, Vrouwe van Wavrechin
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (1)  '''Marguerite de La Mark de Lumain''' in 1563, then Honorine de L'Esclatière in 1566. implies that his union with Marguerite (1563) was either short or childless, as no offspring are listed in the genealogical reco
2 CONC rds reviewed. The French Wikipedia entry on Charles and the Cleves genealogy index mention the marriage but provide no descendants from it. After the death of his 1st wife Marguerite de La Mark de Lumain he married again.
2 CONT * Married (2) '''Honorine de L'Esclatière''' in 1566. Charles died in 1611 without documented heirs carrying forward the Beaurieux title in a direct line from either wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_de_Gavre Charles de Gavre, a Belgian Diplomat,by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles de Gavre , 1st Count of Beaurieu and of the Holy Roman Empire, Lord of Frésin, was a military man and diplomat, born around 1525 and died in 1611 .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the grandson of Jacques de Gavre , known as Pinchart. He married Marguerite de La Mark de Lumain in 1563, then Honorine de L'Esclatière in 1566.
2 CONT
2 CONT He began his career in the armies of Charles V and there attained the rank of colonel.
2 CONT
2 CONT On October 18, 1576, he was tasked by the States of Brabant with occupying Waelhem , fortifying it, and blocking communications between Antwerp and Lier . He was taken prisoner there by Julián Romero 's troops and brought to Lier.
2 CONT
2 CONT On December 20, 1576, Charles de Gavre was appointed chief and superintendent of provisions for the royal army in the Netherlands, then a member of the War Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1577, he was a deputy to the Estates of Arlon, then to the Prince of Orange to convince him to go to Brussels to reach an agreement with the States General on the measures that should guarantee independence and national freedom
2 CONC s.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was appointed a member of the Council of State inJanuary 1578.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was sent back with the Baron d'Aubigny by the Estates General to the Duke of Alençon to ascertain his intentions regarding the troops he had pledged to send as reinforcements to the United Provinces , and then again to the Duke
2 CONC  of Alençon, this time with the Duke d'Arschot and the Abbot de Maroilles, to sign the act ofSeptember 30, 1578.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrested in Antwerp in 1579 on the pretext of treason, he was reinstated in 1581, before betraying the Spanish by surrendering the stronghold of the citadel of Breda . He was appointed castellan and governor of Ath .January 28, 15
2 CONC 86after the Spanish regained control of the region.
2 CONT
2 CONT
