1 NAME Pontus 1er /de Lalaing/ seigneur de Bugnicourt, bailiff of Orchies
2 GIVN Pontus 1er
2 SURN de Lalaing
2 NSFX seigneur de Bugnicourt, bailiff of Orchies
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fils bâtard, légitimé ensuite. Seigneur de Bugnicourt.
2 CONT Available Sources : F Brassart, 1879, FV Goethals, 1862.
2 CONT Spouse: Ph de l'Espinoy, 1631.
2 CONT _____
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pontus 1er (Ponce, Ponthus) de Lalaing'''
2 CONT -écuyer puis chevalier (après 1499), 
2 CONT - seigneur de Bugnicourt, Hordain, Noyelles-Vion, 
2 CONT - chevalier de la Toison d’Or (203°, 1546), 
2 CONT - Gouverneur & Capitaine-Général de la Province d’Artois, 
2 CONT - Bailli d’Orchies (1499), 
2 CONT - Capitaine de Douai (réside ordinairement à Douai ou dans son château de Villers-au-Tertre)
2 CONT
2 CONT ép. ~1495 Bonne de Wassenaer (fille de Jean, vicomte de Lieden, + 1496, et de Catherine de Craon + 1477)
2 CONT
2 CONT sans postérité
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Pontus I de Lalaing''', knight, lord of Bugnicourt, bailiff of Orchies in 1499 (then qualified as a squire), several times "captain" of the city of Douai (i.e. military governor in times of war), married, around 1495, Bonne DE 
2 CONC WASSENAERE (61).
2 CONT
2 CONT We see, in an account of the great bailliage of Hainaut (October 1, 1490 - September 30, 1491, f° j v°), that "monsr Jehan, lord of Lalaing, deshireta of his fief, chasteau, city, land, justice and seignoury of Villers or Tertre, 
2 CONC and of another fief named of Bantimont, lying rather prez of Bugnicourt, being included.In ploughable lands, meadows and rents of wheat", because of the "sale that he made to Ponthus de Lalaing, his natural son", for the price of 
2 CONC seven thousand livres. A decree, dated from Malines, on December 8, 1490, remitted half of the rights due to the sovereign, in favor of "Ponius, bastart de Lalaing, escuier" (Id., f°xiiij).
2 CONT
2 CONT By a transaction of March 8, 1504 (v. st.), made with his cousin Charles, lord of Lalaing (second branch, XIII), it was agreed that each of them would have the right to full arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT He usually resided in Douai and in his castle of Villers-au-Tertre; he was the main inhabitant of our town.
2 CONT
2 CONT (61) Pontus Heuterus, p. 63 de ses Genealogioe, l'appelle Catherine: il se trompe encore, quand il ajoute que, mariée au fils du comte de Lalaing, elle mourut en 1476.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 49-5
2 CONC 0''
