1 NAME Arthus /de Lalaing/ seigneur de Hordaing, Bugnicourt, Houdain, Villers, etc
2 GIVN Arthus
2 NSFX seigneur de Hordaing, Bugnicourt, Houdain, Villers, etc
2 _MARNM de Lalaing
2 NICK Artus de Lalaing
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC chapel of Sainte-Aune
2 ADDR
3 ADR1  Basilica of Our Lady of Brebières
3 ADR2 Albert
3 CITY Brebières
3 STAE Hauts-de-France
3 POST 62117
3 CTRY France
1 OCCU of Hordaing, Bugnicourt, Houdain, Villers, Fressin, Aubrecicourt and Brebières,  Sénéchal d’Ostrevant, Bailli de Douai
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes
2 CONT Fils bâtard, légitimé ensuite. 
2 CONT - Seigneur de Hordaing, sénéhal d'Ostrevant.
2 CONT Source : F Brassart, 1879.
2 CONT _____
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Arthus (ou Artus) de Lalaing''' + 01/04/1521 (inh. à Brébières) 
2 CONT - écuyer puis chevalier, 
2 CONT - seigneur de Hordaing, Bugnicourt, Houdain, Villers, Fressin, Aubrecicourt et Brebières, 
2 CONT - Sénéchal d’Ostrevant, 
2 CONT - Bailli de Douai (1499-1504), 
2 CONT
2 CONT X 1483 (siège d’Utrecht), sert la Maison d’Autriche (réside à Douai, dans l’hôtel dit «de Hordaing» puis «de Bugnicourt»)
2 CONT
2 CONT (brise ses armes d’un lambel de trois pendants d’azur)
2 CONT
2 CONT ép. Jeanne de Habarcq, dame de Noyelles-Vion + 12/1540
2 CONT (10 enfants, 3 fils & 7 filles)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''ARTUS de Lalaing''', 
2 CONT knight (reached this dignity towards the end of his career), seneschal of Ostrevant, lord of Hordaing, bailiff of Douai (1499-1504), married Jeanne DE HABART, died on April 1, 1521 and was buried in the church of his lordship of B
2 CONC rebières, under a marble placed in front of the altar of the chapel of Sainte-Aune. His widow died in December 1540.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived in Douai in the hotel that he had inherited from his father and that was then called the hotel of Hordaing, then the hotel of Bugnicourt. In the Douai ceremonies, he occupied the place of honor, immediately after his elde
2 CONC r brother. He was wearing a label of three azure pendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served the House of Austria, and his name, as well as that of his brother Pontus, is mentioned several times in the Chronicles of Molinet.
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of a noblewoman who was in his service, Hulline de Manchicourt, sister of Jean, esquire, living in Gomignies, contains some information regarding Artus de Lallaing and his wife having at least ten children, three sons and
2 CONC  seven daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1° Pontus de Lalaing, who follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2° N....... de Lalaing, Mortes jeunes. Pare 192 de l'Histoire de l'abbaye de Flines.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3° N..... of Lalaing, Mortes jeunes. Pare 192 de l'Histoire de l'abbaye de Flines.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4° Anne de Lalaing, born around 1503, died in 1569, married to Nicolas DE LANNOY, knight, lord of Maingoval; she inherited from her brother Pontus, and her daughter brought into the family of Sainte-Aldegonde the lordships of Bugn
2 CONC icourt, Hordaing and other lands of the elder branch of Lalaing.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5° Bonne de Lalaing, who died in Douai in 1585, married Adam D'ESNE, esquire, sr de Bétencourt. Of which posterity.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6° Yolente de Lalaing, died in Douai, in the first days of the year 1581, lying in the choir of the church of the cordeliers or récollets wal(1) municip., reg. aux testam., 1510-1513, f° 220. ions, widow without child of Jean DE L
2 CONC A PORTE, esquire, sr. de Morselede; benefactress of the university and of the poor of Douai.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7° Antoinette de Lalaing, who died young, named around 1513 in the above-mentioned will of Hulline de Manchicourt, with her sisters: "To me well loved Anne and Bonne, the two golden vgnes, and to Yolen, my golden heart, and to Ant
2 CONC oinette, my little patrenostes of coral."
2 CONT
2 CONT 8° Jacqueline de Lalaing, abbess of Flines, from 1533 to 1561, woman superior, who gave the example of all virtues
2 CONT
2 CONT 9° N..... de Lalaing, Mortes jeunes. Pare 192 de l'Histoire de l'abbaye de Flines.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10° N….. de Lalaing, Mortes jeunes. Pare 192 de l'Histoire de l'abbaye de Flines.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 51-5
2 CONC 3''
