3 CTRY France
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes
2 CONT Ou Sidérac. Fils bâtard, légitimé ensuite. Prévôt de Saint-Pierre. Doyen et chanoine de Saint-Amé à Douai.
2 CONT Available Sources : FV Goethals, 1862, F Brassart, 1879.
2 CONT _____
2 CONT '''Sidrac de Lalaing''' + 28/06/1533 (buried in Saint-Omer)
2 CONT Licenciate in decrees, 
2 CONT - Provost of Saint-Pierre de Douai (1508-1532), 
2 CONT - Dean & Canon of Saint-Omer (1512-1533)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Sidrach de Lalaing''', licentiate in decrees, provost of Saint-Pierre de Douai (1508-1532), dean and canon of Saint-Omer (1512-1533), died on June 28, 1533; lies in the church of Saint-Omer where one still sees his elegant tomb
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000188910193858&size=large}}
2 CONT funerary monument of Sidrach de Lalaing (bas-relief) : Sidrach Misach and Abdenago thrown into the furnace.  cathédrale Notre-Dame, actuellement église Notre-Dame, Saint-Omer.  “ Sidrach de Lalaing, canon of Saint-Omer died in 153
2 CONC 3. The sculptor Georges Monnoyer was paid a sum of 24 livres de gros, the common currency of Artois in the 16th century. The monument was originally placed against the opposite pillar, and a ram's head can still be seen there.” AR
2 CONC CH. PHOT. (MH79735)-Propriété de la commune, MINISTÈRE DE LA CULTURE
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 50.'
2 CONC '
