1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/DRURY.htm
2 CONT *William DRURY of Rougham (Sir)
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1408, Rougham, Suffolk, England
2 CONT *Died: 1450
2 CONT *Buried: Church of the Friars Minor of Babewell (as stated in Will)
2 CONT *Notes: 19 May 1426, Knight of the Bath at Leicester Whitsun. 28 Feb 1446/47, Witnessed Charter of Richard of York at Bury St. Edmund's. Catherine Swynford was first cousin of Henry V
2 CONT *Father: Roger DRURY of Rougham (Sir)
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret NAUNTON
2 CONT *''''''Married: Catherine SWYNFORD (d. 3 Dec 1478 - bur. Lincoln Cathedral) (dau. of Thomas Swynford and Jane Croophill) BET 1404 - 1411
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Mary DRURY
2 CONT **2. Anne DRURY (Nun) (b. 1439)
2 CONT **3. Thomas DRURY of Rougham
2 CONT **4. Roger DRURY of Hepworth (b. 1433)
2 CONT **5. George DRURY (Rector of Woolpit) (b. 1435)
2 CONT **6. Catherine DRURY (Nun) (b. 1431)
2 CONT *__________________________
2 CONT *''''''Katherine Roet Swynford
2 CONT *''''''Daughter of a herald; Duchess of Lancaster
2 CONT *http://katherineswynford.tk/page12/page12.html
2 CONT *Extract from MS. number CCCX, 185--In Thorndon Church... there be the Arms of Dame Katherine Swynford sometime Duchess of Lancaster that by Sir Thomas Swynford [six] had a son and heir--Sir Thomas Swynford, knight, father to Dame
2 CONC  ''''''Katherine wife to Sir Wm. Drury, Kt., the tenth Sir Wm. Drury. Dame Katherine among others had Mary'''''' the wife of Edward Grimston whom God had endowed with great virtue and beauty and is here interred the 6th day of Mar
2 CONC ch 1469. Beneath this epitaph lieth in brass the form of a human body... Upon the very highest part of all was a great Escutcheon quarterly of John of Gaunt as France and England, upon the 4th corner beneath Drury as before empali
2 CONC ng Swynford as before underneath this was written--Orate pro anima Mariae Grimston and over all a Lambeaux of three points ermine impaling Swynford argent upon a chevron sable 3 boars heads or.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/dd/drury02.php
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *Sir William Drury of Rougham (d before 27.06.1450) m. Katherine Swinford (d 1478, dau of Sir Thomas (not Hugh) Swinford)
2 CONT **1.	Thomas Drury of Rougham (b c1430, d 1486)	m. Katharine Whitwell (dau of John Whitwel of Suffolkl)
2 CONT *** 	A.	John Drury of Rougham (b 1456, d 1499) 	m. Margaret Felton or Chapman (dau of William Felton alias Chapman of Playford) ## possibly here ##
2 CONT ****i.	John Drury of Rougham (d 1556) 	m. Elizabeth Goldingham (dau of John Goldingham of Belstead by Thomasine Lisbon)
2 CONT *****	a.	Robert Drury of Rougham (dvp)	m. Elizabeth Tay (dau of Thomas Tay of Layer, m2. Edmund Gooding of Thurston)
2 CONT ******	(1)	Sir Robert Drury of Rougham (b 1543, d before 10.01.1625) 	m. Elizabeth Drury (d 1621, dau of Sir William Drury of Hawstead)
2 CONT *******(A)	Robert Drury of Rougham (dvp 1623) 	m. Elizabeth Crofts (dau of Charles Crofts of Bardwell)
2 CONT ********i. Charles Drury of Rougham (d 1633, 2nd son?) 	m. Sarah Seckford (dau /coheirof Henry Seckford of Woodly, m2. John (son of Dudley, Lord North, Baron Kirtling)
2 CONT *********	(a)	Seckford Drury of Rougham (dsp 29.03.1634)
2 CONT *********	(b)	Dorothy Drury (dsp 1634)
2 CONT ********  	(ii)	Elizabeth Drury m. (1622) William Wells (rector of Rougham)
2 CONT *********  	(a)	Robert Wells of Rougham Hall
2 CONT ********  	(iii)	Ann Drury (b 1614)	m. Charles Alexander (son of the Earl of Stirling)
2 CONT ********  	(iv)	Cecily Drury  	m. George Douglas (rector of Stepney)
2 CONT ******** 	(v)+	other issue - Roger (dsp 11.07.1634), others (d young - William (b 1599), Susan, Robert)
2 CONT
