2 TITL Waterton of Waterton & Methley - Family History (14th & 15th Century Descents)
1 NOTE Unmarried
1 NOTE John Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset, 3rd Earl of Somerset (baptised March 25, 1404 – May 27, 1444), was an English noble and military commander.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the second son of John Beaufort, 1st Earl of Somerset, and succeeded his elder brother Henry to become the 3rd Earl of Somerset in 1418.
2 CONT
2 CONT The young earl fought in Henry V's 1419 campaigns in France. In 1421 he accompanied the king's younger brother Thomas of Lancaster to the fighting in Anjou. Thomas was killed at the Battle of Baugé and Somerset was captured.
2 CONT
2 CONT He remained imprisoned for 17 years, and after being ransomed became one of the leading English commanders in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1443 he was created Duke of Somerset and Earl of Kendal, made a Knight of the Garter, and appointed Captain-General of Guyenne. However he proved a poor commander. He married Margaret Beauchamp of Bletso in 1439. His death in 1
2 CONC 444 may have been due to suicide.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Children
2 CONT Illegitimate children of John Beaufort:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacinda (also called Thomasine) (c. 1434 – after 1469). Married Reginald Grey, 7th Baron Grey de Wilton. 
2 CONT Thomasine Beaufort (before 1444 – c. 1494) 
2 CONT John of Somerset (c. 1444 – 1453) 
2 CONT Child of John Beaufort and Margaret Beauchamp of Bletso:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Margaret Beaufort (May 31, 1443 – June 29, 1509), mother of Henry VII of England 
1 NOTE Unmarried
1 NOTE DUKE OF SOMERSET; KG
1 NOTE 3rd Earl of Somerset and K.G. Created 1st Duke of Somerset and Earl of Kendal in 1443. [GADD.GED]
2 CONT
2 CONT SS: Died at Wimborne after returning to England in disgrace after his French campaign failed. [THELMA.GED]
