2 CONT
2 CONT      Mary Ferrers was born circa 1379.3,1 She was the daughter of Sir Robert de Ferrers, 3rd Lord Ferrers (of Wem) and Lady Joan de Beaufort.1,2 She married Sir Ralph de Neville, 2nd Earl of Westmoreland, son of Sir Ralph de Nevil
2 CONC le, 1st Earl of Westmorland and Lady Margaret de Stafford, circa 1413 in a Oversley, Warwickshire, England marriage.2 She died on 25 January 1458.2
2 CONT
2 CONT      From circa 1413, her married name became de Neville.3
2 CONT
