2 CONT ==Lady Eleanor de Neville1==
2 CONT '''F, #107425, b. circa 1397, d. 1472
2 CONT Last Edited=4 Jul 2015
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.03%
2 CONT '''Lady Eleanor de Neville was born circa 1397 at Raby Castle, Durham, County Durham, England.2 She was the daughter''' of Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland and Lady Joan de Beaufort.1 '''She married, firstly, Sir Richard 
2 CONC le Despenser, 4th Lord Burghersh''', son of Thomas le Despenser, 1st and last Earl of Gloucester and Constance Langley, '''after 23 May 1412.3 She married, secondly, Henry Percy, 1st Earl of Northumberland''', son of Sir Henry Per
2 CONC cy, Lord Percy and Elizabeth de Mortimer, '''after October 1414 at Alnwick, Northumberland, England.3 She died in 1472.'''1
2 CONT '''From after 23 May 1412, her married name became le Despenser.1,3 From after October 1414, her married name became Percy.3 As a result of her marriage, Lady Eleanor de Neville was styled as Countess of Northumberland on 16 March
2 CONC  1416.'''
2 CONT '''Children of Lady Eleanor de Neville and Henry Percy, 1st Earl of Northumberland'''
2 CONT 1. Hon. John Percy4 b. 8 Jul 1418
2 CONT 2. Lady Joan Percy4 b. c 1420
2 CONT 3. Henry Percy, 2nd Earl of Northumberland+ b. 25 Jul 1421, d. 29 Mar 1461
2 CONT 4. Thomas Percy, 1st Baron Egremont+5 b. 29 Nov 1422, d. 10 Jul 1460
2 CONT 5. Lady Catherine Percy+6 b. 28 May 1423, d. a 1475
2 CONT 6. Hon. George Percy4 b. 24 Jul 1424, d. 14 Nov 1474
2 CONT 7. Sir Ralph Percy4 b. 1425, d. 25 Apr 1464
2 CONT 8. Sir Richard Percy4 b. c 1426, d. 29 Mar 1461
2 CONT 9. Hon. William Percy4 b. 7 Apr 1428, d. 26 Apr 1462
2 CONT 10. Hon. Alan Percy4 b. c 1430
