2 CONT One more question and I should have my frustrations in check. In possession, I have a Family Group sheet that shows Eleanor Neville b: 1406, dau. of Ralph Neville b: 1364 and Joan Beaufort b: 1375 (dau of John of Gaunt) married to
2 CONC  a Locke. This "source" shows Eleanor married to John Locke b: 1400, son of William Locke b: 1351 and Joan de Mortimer with Locke issue then to Sommerset. In my search of the Neville's (my surname) I have never seen this marriage.
2 CONC  I show the subject Eleanor married to Henry Percy and Richard le Despencer, but no John Locke. Additionally, I do not show a marriage between a Locke and a Neville. If someone in the group has information on this subject John Loc
2 CONC ke b: 1400, son of William and Joan as to his marriages or girl friends, I would sure appreciate it to either  prove or disprove the subject Family Group Sheet. Thanking you inadvance!...take care....Ren Neville
2 CONT
