2 CONT THIS REFERENCE SO FAR IS THE ONLY ONE I HAVE SEEN WITH JOHN LOCKE'S WIFE MENTIONED AND IT IS LISTED AS JANE. 
2 CONT '''Notes and queries
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=NEsAAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA326&lpg=PA326&dq=Matthew+Michael+Locke+1550&source=bl&ots=cznh3tm61c&sig=Pzzex-_XwXbENEb5E2ZqlfAk4tE&hl=en&ei=V5grTcCDIoOusAOZ9NyeBw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=8&ved=0CE
2 CONC gQ6AEwBw#v=onepage&q=Matthew%20Michael%20Locke%201550&f=false
2 CONT Pg.326
2 CONT John Locke, who was Sheriff of London in 1461, and (wife Jane his wife) was enfeoffed in 1499 with the mansion of Merton Place, co. Surrey, was the father of Thomas Locke, of London, Merchant and Mercer.
2 CONT *This Thomas Locke married Joan, sole daughter and heiress of ___ Wilcotts, of Rotherham, co. York, who bore, Azure, an eagle displayed argent. They had issue: 1. John, died s. p. in 1519. 2. Sir William, Knt., alderman, mercer, a
2 CONC nd Sheriff, in 1548, of London. He married four times, and, by his first and second wives, had a large family; died August 24, 1550. 3. Michael Locke.
2 CONT Thomas Locke died in 1507, and was buried in the Mercers' Chapel. London. 
2 CONT
