1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://www.thepeerage.com/p10743.htm#i107421
2 CONT *''''''Joan Neville was the daughter of Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland and Lady Joan de Beaufort.1
2 CONT *''''''     Joan Neville was a nun at The Minories, London, England.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 108. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/NEVILLE2.htm#Ralph DE NEVILLE (1° E. Westmoreland)
2 CONT *Ralph NEVILLE (1° E. Westmoreland)
2 CONT *Born: 1363, Raby, Durham, England
2 CONT *Died: 21 Oct 1425, Raby Castle, Durham, England
2 CONT *Married 2: Joan BEAUFORT (C. Westmoreland) 29 Nov 1396, Meuse-et-Loire, France
2 CONT **''''''12. Joan NEVILLE (Nun) (b. 1398)
2 CONT *<nowiki>-------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_de_Neville,_1st_Earl_of_Westmorland
2 CONT *Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland
2 CONT *He had fourteen children by Joan Beaufort:
2 CONT **Lady Katherine Neville, married first on 12 January 1411 John Mowbray, 2nd Duke of Norfolk; married second Sir Thomas Strangways; married third John Beaumont, 1st Viscount Beaumont; married fourth Sir John Woodville (d. 12 Augus
2 CONC t 1469).
2 CONT **Lady Eleanor Neville (1398-1472), married first Richard le Despencer, 4th Baron Burghersh, married second Henry Percy, 2nd Earl of Northumberland
2 CONT **Richard Neville, 5th Earl of Salisbury (1400-1460), married Alice Montacute. Had issue. Their descendants include Queen Consort to Henry VIII, Catherine Parr.
2 CONT **Robert Neville (d. 1457), Bishop of Durham
2 CONT **William Neville, 1st Earl of Kent (d. 1463)
2 CONT **Edward Neville, 1st Lord Bergavenny (d. 1476)
2 CONT **Anne Neville (1414-1480), married Humphrey Stafford, 1st Duke of Buckingham
2 CONT **Cecily Neville (1415-1495) ("Proud Cis"), married Richard, 3rd Duke of York; mother of Kings Edward IV of England and Richard III of England
2 CONT **George Neville, 1st Baron Latymer (d. 1469)
2 CONT **John Neville (1387 - 20 March 1420)
2 CONT **Cuthbert Neville, died young
2 CONT **Thomas Neville, died young
2 CONT **Henry Neville, died young
2 CONT **''''''Joan Neville, a nun
