2 TITL Raby Castle - Open to the public
2 NOTE The first castle built on the Raby estate was constructed during the reign on King Cnut in the early 11th century. The castle that stands there now was begun by John, 3rd Baron Nevill in approximately 1360.[1] Cecily Neville, who 
3 CONC was the mother of the Kings Edward IV of England and Richard III of England was born here. The Nevilles lost the castle (and many more of their possessions) after they led the failed Rising of the North in favour of Mary, Queen of
3 CONC  Scots in 1569.
3 CONT
3 CONT Sir Henry Vane the Elder purchased the castle in 1626 and neighbouring Barnard Castle from the Crown, and as the Earls of Darlington and Dukes of Cleveland, a Gothic-style entrance hall and octagon-shaped drawing room were added.
