1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==George Neville, 1st Baron Latimer==
2 CONT '''George Neville, 1st Baron Latimer or (Latymer) (c. 1407 – 30 December 1469) was an English peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Neville was the fifth son''' of Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland, by his second wife Lady Joan Beaufort, daughter of John of Gaunt, 1st Duke of Lancaster. '''He succeeded to the Latymer estates on the death of h
2 CONC is half-uncle''' John Neville, 6th Baron Latimer, '''in 1430 (see Baron Latimer), and on 25 February 1432 he was summoned to Parliament as Baron Latimer.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord Latimer later fought in Scotland in 1436,[1] was a Justice of the Peace for Cumberland in 1437 and admitted to the Privy Council in 1439.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1437, Lord Latimer married Lady Elizabeth (1417–1480), daughter of''' Richard de Beauchamp, 13th Earl of Warwick, by his first wife, Elizabeth Berkeley.[1] '''They had four children:
2 CONT *Katherine Neville, who died childless.
2 CONT *Sir Henry Neville (d. 26 July 1469), who married Joan Bourchier, daughter of John Bourchier, 1st Baron Berners, and Marjorie Berners, and had:
2 CONT **Joan Neville, born ca 1464, Latimer, Buckinghamshire, England; she married Sir James Ratclyffe.[2]
2 CONT **Richard Neville, 2nd Baron Latimer (Latimer, Buckinghamshire / Sinnington, North Riding of Yorkshire, ca. 1468 – Snape, North Yorkshire, December 1530, bur. Well, North Yorkshire), married in Grafton, Worcestershire, in 1490 to 
2 CONC Anne Stafford (Grafton, Worcestershire, ca. 1471 – aft. 1513, bur. Well, North Yorkshire), daughter of Sir Humphrey Stafford of Grafton (Grafton, Worcestershire, ca. 1427 – executed by order of King Henry VII for siding with Richa
2 CONC rd III, Tyburn, 8 July 1486) and Catherine Fray (1437–1482), and had issue which included John Nevill, 3rd Baron Latimer.[3]
2 CONT **Thomas Neville (1468–1546) (Esq.), born in Shenstone, Staffordshire, England. He was Lord of Mathom; married Letitia Harcourt (1494–1520), daughter of Sir Robert Harcourt of Stanton Harcourt and Agnes Lymbrake and had issue.[4]
2 CONT *Thomas Neville, of Shenstone, Staffordshire.[1]
2 CONT *Jane Neville, who married Oliver Dudley.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Neville appears to have suffered from some form of dementia in his later years, as he was described as an "idiot," and the guardianship of his lands was given to his nephew''', Richard Neville, 16th Earl of Warwick, the 
2 CONC Kingmaker.[1] '''George Neville, Lord Latimer, died on 30 December 1469 and was succeeded in the barony by his grandson''' Richard, '''his eldest son''' Sir Henry Neville having predeceased him by several months, dying at the Batt
2 CONC le of Edgecote Moor, 26 July 1469.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Neville,_1st_Baron_Latimer
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________
