2 CONT *'''Lady Anne Neville1
2 CONT *'''F, #107422, d. 20 September 1480
2 CONT *Last Edited=27 Jan 2013
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.03%
2 CONT *'''     Lady Anne Neville was the daughter''' of Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland and Lady Joan de Beaufort.1 '''She married, firstly, Humphrey Stafford, 1st Duke of Buckingham''', son of Edmund Stafford, 5th Earl of Sta
2 CONC fford and Anne of Woodstock, Countess of Buckingham, '''before 18 October 1424.2 She married, secondly, Walter Blount, 1st Lord Mountjoy''', son of Thomas Blount and Margaret Gresley, '''before 25 November 1467.2 She died on 20 Se
2 CONC ptember 1480.2 She was buried at Pleshy, Essex, England.3 Her will was proven (by probate) on 31 October 1480.3
2 CONT *'''     As a result of her marriage, Lady Anne Neville was styled as Duchess of Buckingham on 14 September 1444. From before 25 November 1467, her married name became Blount.1,2
