1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT a short summary from Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Cecily Neville
2 CONT
2 CONT Duchess of York
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:	Richard Plantagenet, 3rd Duke of York
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne of York, Duchess of Exeter
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward IV, King of England
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund, Earl of Rutland
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth of York, Duchess of Suffolk
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, Duchess of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT George Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Clarence
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard III, King of England
2 CONT
2 CONT House: House of York
2 CONT
2 CONT House of Neville
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Ralph Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Joan Beaufort
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 3 May 1415
2 CONT
2 CONT Raby Castle, Durham
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 31 May 1495 (aged 80)
2 CONT
2 CONT Berkhamsted Castle, Hertfordshire
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: St Mary and All Saints Church, Fotheringhay
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT "Cecily Neville, Duchess of York (3 May 1415 – 31 May 1495) was the wife of Richard Plantagenet, 3rd Duke of York, and the mother of two Kings of England, Edward IV and Richard III.
2 CONT Lady Cecily Neville was a daughter of Ralph Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland, and Joan Beaufort, Countess of Westmorland. Her maternal grandparents were John of Gaunt, 1st Duke of Lancaster, and Katherine Swynford. John of Gaunt w
2 CONC as the third surviving son of Edward III of England and Philippa of Hainault.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the aunt of Richard Neville, 16th Earl of Warwick, one of the leading peers and military commanders of his generation, and also the great-great-great-aunt of the queen consort Catherine Parr, sixth wife of her great-grands
2 CONC on, King Henry VIII.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecily was called "the Rose of Raby", because she was born at Raby Castle in Durham, and "Proud Cis", because of her pride and a temper that went with it. Historically she is also known for her piety. She herself signed her name "
2 CONC Cecylle"."
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================================================
