1 OCCU chevalier, seigneur de Rambures, Dompierre, Ecouys et Drucat, conseiller & Chambellan du Roi, Sénéchal & Gouverneur de Ponthieu, Maître des Eaux-&-Forêts de Picardie
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The original tree of GENI identified this person as André III de Rambures, incorrect because...
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From Gemini AI''' (Summary for leads only, please check your sources)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *In the lineage of the House of Rambures, a prominent noble family from Picardy, André III and André V represent two distinct generations with significant historical roles.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''André III de Rambures (c. 1341 – 1405)'''
2 CONT André III lived during the mid-to-late 14th century, a period marked by the early phases of the Hundred Years' War. 
2 CONT Titles: He was the Sire and Châtelain of Rambures.
2 CONT Military Role: Known for his military service during the reign of Charles V and Charles VI, he maintained the family's strategic importance in northern France.
2 CONT Family: He was the son of Jean II de Rambures and Jeanne de Drucat. He is often distinguished in genealogy from the famous David de Rambures (his son or nephew depending on the specific branch), who was immortalized in Shakespeare
2 CONC 's Henry V. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''André V de Rambures (c. 1450 – after 1512)'''
2 CONT André V lived nearly a century later and served during the transition from the Middle Ages to the Renaissance. 
2 CONT Titles: Chevalier, Seigneur de Rambures, and Governor of Ponthieu.
2 CONT Court Influence: He served as a Chamberlain to the King and was the Master of Waters and Forests for Picardy.
2 CONT Marriage: He married Johanna van Halewijn (d'Halluin), daughter of the Governor of Picardy. This marriage connected him to the powerful Halewijn family.
2 CONT Key Accomplishment: He is credited with founding the Couvent des Minimes in Abbeville in 1492
2 CONT
2 CONT André V de Rambures was the great-great-grandson of André III de Rambures. Their lineage is central to the history of the Château de Rambures, a unique 15th-century brick-and-stone fortress in Picardy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Genealogical Tree'''
2 CONT The line of descent through the Lords of Rambures is as follows:
2 CONT André III "Andrieux" de Rambures (d. 1405): Knight, Captain of Boulogne and Gravelines.
2 CONT David de Rambures (1364–1415): Son of André III. Master of Crossbowmen of France. He began construction of the present-day Château de Rambures in 1412 but died at the Battle of Agincourt.
2 CONT André II de Rambures (c. 1395–1449): Son of David. A comrade-in-arms of Joan of Arc at the Siege of Orléans, he was killed at the Siege of Pont-Audemer.
2 CONT Jacques de Rambures (c. 1428–1488): Son of André II. He is credited with completing the castle's construction around 1470.
2 CONT André V de Rambures (d. after 1512): Son of Jacques. He served as Chamberlain to the King and Governor of Ponthieu. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Fortress of Rambures'''
2 CONT The Château de Rambures is a masterpiece of late medieval military architecture, notable for several reasons: 
2 CONT Innovating Material: It was one of the first European castles built almost entirely of brick, chosen for its ability to absorb the impact of early artillery better than stone.
2 CONT Distinctive Shape: The fortress features a unique "four-leaf clover" or square-with-rounded-towers design, intended to eliminate blind spots for defenders.
2 CONT Continuous Ownership: Uniquely, the castle has remained in the same extended family (passing to the La Roche Fontenilles branch via marriage in 1645) for nearly 1,000 years.
2 CONT André V de Rambures ° ~1453 + après 10/03/1512
2 CONT (1513 ; inh. aux Minimes d’Abbeville avec son épouse)
2 CONT chevalier, seigneur de Rambures, Dompierre, Ecouys et Drucat, conseiller & Chambellan du Roi, Sénéchal & Gouverneur de Ponthieu 
2 CONT (nommé le 26/05/1495, simultanément avec François de Créquy, nommé Sénéchal du Boulonnais),
2 CONT Maître des Eaux-&-Forêts de Picardie (fonde le Couvent des Minimes d’Abbeville)
2 CONT .....
2 CONT ép. Johanna (alias Anna) van Halewijn (Halluin) -Piennes
