2 CONT 48. Ordinance on the manor house at Montfordt, "given by Anna of Lalaing, douairière of Montfordt. 1545. 1 piece.
2 CONT
2 CONT 221. Anthonis van Lalaing, count van Hoochstrate, stadholder of Holland, and Charlotte van Brederode, lady dowager of Montfort, enter into an agreement, by which the latter as guardian of her son Josse and her other children, empo
2 CONC wered to do so by her deceased husband's will, accepts the former as her joint guardian over her children, who promises on his part, to assist her in all disputes and in particular to see to it that the promises made to her in 152
2 CONC 7 by her aforementioned son, will be carried out, all this subject to the obligations taken on by the lord of Hoochstrate towards the Emperor, and with the promise of wife Charlotte, that she will not oppose the Emperor. 1528. 1 c
2 CONC harter.
2 CONT
2 CONT 230. Notarial deed, in which Joost, lord of Montfoert, ready to take part in the campaign against the Turks, makes his will, appoints his young son Jan, subject to a few bequests, as his universal heir and his wife Anna van Lalain
2 CONC g as guardian, with authority to accept her uncle the count of Hoichstraten as joint guardian. 1532. 1 charter (canceled)
2 CONT
2 CONT 240. Anne of Lalaing , widow of Joest, lord of Montfoerd, and the guardians of the children of Montfoerd, viz. Reynolt, lord to Brederoede and Vianen, and Henrick van Montfoord, lord to Abbenbrouck, agree, that the former will not
2 CONC  make use of the authority, granted to her by the aforementioned guardians and Anthonis van Lalaing, count of Hoichstraten, to continue the administration of the goods of Montfoerd, but that she will renounce her husband's estate 
2 CONC and keep for herself her dowry and personal goods, while she will receive from the above-mentioned guardians 400 carolus-guldens yearly for the preservation of the house of Montfoert, as long as she continues to live at the house.
2 CONC  1539. 1 charter. B.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Fruin, Robert. Inventaris Van Het Archief Der Heeren Van Montfoort, Berustende in Het Rijks-Archief in Utrecht. Landsdrukkerij, 1894.'' 
2 CONT __________
2 CONT "lord Anthonis van Meerten, lord tot Essesteyn, knight, and his wife Anna van Lalaing, douairière of Montfoort"
2 CONT
2 CONT The data on Lodewijk van Montfoort are in the December 2011 issue of the Dutch Lion Magazine.
2 CONT The journal Genealogische en Heraldische Bladen 1909 states that Anna van Lalaing was a daughter of Charles de Lalaing and Jacqueline van Luxemburg, that she married Joost van Montfoort 1529 and then Anton van Abcoude van Meerten 
2 CONC van Essenstein.
2 CONT From her first marriage:
2 CONT 1) Philippine of Montfoort x 1555 Jan van Merode
2 CONT 2) Jan van Montfoort x1558 Maria von Manderscheid.
2 CONT
2 CONT Website Gelderland Archives:
2 CONT 0470 Family De Cock van Opijnen Inventory
2 CONT 1. Personal section
2 CONT 1.4. Van Abcoude van Meerten van Essesteyn family 
2 CONT N.B. Anthonis van Abcoude van Meerten van Essesteyn was married to Anna van Lalaing, widow of Joost, viscount of Montfoort.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.0 Deed from Joannis Joannis, notary in Utrecht, that lord Anthonis van Meerten, lord tot Essesteyn, knight, and his wife Anna van Lalaing, douairière van Montfoort, have deposited their private will with him, 1559. 1 charter Loc
2 CONC ation: Gelders Archief En Utrechts Archief:
2 CONT
