1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Antoine, Bâtard de Lalaing''' ° (Bruxelles) + 12/08/1541 (inh. à Saint-Sauve) 
2 CONT - (légitimé par Lettres de 03/1523 à Malines moyennant finance à 20 £, enregistrées à la Chambre des Comptes de Lille le 02/04/1524) 
2 CONT - Protonotaire Apostolique, enregistré à l’Université de Louvain (dès 1527), 
2 CONT - Docteur ès-droits (1535), 
2 CONT - Prieur commendataire de Saint-Sauve (près Valenciennes, 
2 CONT - ~1525, par accord avec son cousin Charles), 
2 CONT - Prévôt de Saint-Pierre de Cassel (1535), de Saint-Sauveur d’Harlebeke (1536) et de Saint-Liévin de Deventer (Hollande),  
2 CONT - ecclésiastique au Conseil Privé à Bruxelles (brise ses armes de Lalaing-Hoochstrate d’un filet d’or posé en barre)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Antoine, Bastard of Lalaing''' ° (Brussels) + 12/08/1541 (inh. in Saint-Sauve) 
2 CONT - (legitimized by Letters of 03/1523 in Malines by means of finance at 20 £, registered at the Chamber of Accounts of Lille on 02/04/1524) 
2 CONT - Apostolic Prothonotary, registered at the University of Louvain (from 1527), 
2 CONT - Doctor of Laws (1535), 
2 CONT - Prior commendatory of Saint-Sauve (near Valenciennes, 
2 CONT - (near Valenciennes, ~1525, by agreement with his cousin Charles), 
2 CONT - Provost of Saint-Pierre de Cassel (1535), of Saint-Sauveur d'Harlebeke (1536) and of Saint-Liévin de Deventer (Holland), 
2 CONT - ecclesiastical adviser to the Privy Council in Brussels (breaking his arms of Lalaing-Hoochstrate with a golden fillet in bar)
2 CONT
2 CONT Pattou, Etienne, Famille & Seigneurs de Lalaing, Racines et Histoire 
2 CONT __________
2 CONT A. '''Antoine de Lalaing''', legitimized by letters dated of Malines, in March 1523, by means of finance, taxed at twenty pounds, at the time of the registration in the chamber of accounts in Lille, on April 2, 1524 after Easter (
2 CONC 20th register of the charters, f° vijxxX) Born in Brussels, apostolic prothonotary, matriculated in the university of Louvain in the year 1527, promoted doctor in rights in the year 1535, prior commendatory of Saint-Sauve near Val
2 CONC enciennes around 1525 (by march made with Charles de Lalaing, nephew of his father, quoted hereafter, XIV), provost of Saint-Pierre de Cassel in 1535, of Saint-Sauveur d'Harlebeke in 1536 and of Saint-Liévin de Deventer in Holland
2 CONC , ecclesiastical adviser to the private council in Brussels, he died on August 12, 1541, lying in the middle of the church of Saint-Sauve, under a marble tomb. He broke the shield of Lalaing-Hoochstrate with a golden fillet in bar
2 CONC  (genealogical table of the cabinet of titles).
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 62.'
2 CONC '
