1 NAME Pontus II /de Lalaing/ seigneur de Bugnicourt
2 GIVN Pontus II
2 SURN de Lalaing
2 NSFX seigneur de Bugnicourt
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1508
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 OCT 1558
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Pontus II de Lalaing''' ° ~1508 (Douai) + 13 ou 15/10/1558
2 CONT - seigneur de Bugnicourt, Hordain, Noyelle-Vion, 
2 CONT - capitaine d’une bande d’ordonnance (1545), 
2 CONT - Général impérial (Thérouanne, Saint-Quentin, Gravelines), 
2 CONT - chevalier de la Toison d’Or (203°, 1546), 
2 CONT - Gouverneur & Capitaine-Général de la Province d’Artois puis en Flandres (il commande l’armée impériale après la + du comte du Roeux au siège de Thérouanne 1553)
2 CONT
2 CONT ép. 1542 Eléonore de Montmorency (soeur du comte de Hornes ;
2 CONT …..ép. 2) Antoine de Lalaing, comte deHoogstaeten)
2 CONT
2 CONT X) liaison avec Jacqueline
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire'' :
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''PONTUS II de Lalaing''', 
2 CONT lord of Bugnicourt, knight of the Golden Fleece in 1546, governor of Artois, then of Flanders for a while, before his death in 1558, captain of an ordinance band in 1545, one of the good generals that Charles V and Philip II oppos
2 CONC ed to France, in front of Terouane, in Saint-Quentin, in Grayelines etc. Born around 1508, probably in Douai, he died on October 15, 1558, having married Eléonore DE MONTMORENCY, sister of the count of Hornes, who married Antoine 
2 CONC de Lalaing, count of Hoochstrate (branch of Hoochstrate, XV).
2 CONT By his high qualities, he knew how to reconquer the high rank that the mésalliance of his ancestor had made lose to his branch.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had had a legitimate daughter :
2 CONT
2 CONT A. Marie de Lalaing, who died young, on July 4, 1557, lying next to her father, in the choir of the church of Villers-au-Tertre.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his youth, he had "begotten and procreated to the body" of a certain Jacqueline N..., "a daughter also at the time unmarried," an illegitimate son:
2 CONT
2 CONT ..a. Philippe de Lalaing, bastard of Bugnicourt, for whose benefit the lord of Bugnicourt obtained letters of legitimation, without finance (64), signed by Philippe II, in his camp in Authie, in September 1558, recorded on October
2 CONC  1 in the chamber of accounts in Lille (26th register of the charters, f° vijxxiij). This favor was granted to the supplicant, says the sovereign: "en considéra° des grandz, notables et agreables seruices qu'il a faict à l'empereu
2 CONC r monseignr et pere et à Nous, et faict encoires journellement."
2 CONT
2 CONT The letters of legitimation relate the wartime actions in which the young Philippe de Lalaing had already been involved, "who is of good conduct and honesty, and has followed the arms, since the beginning of the last war, es Ytale
2 CONC s, soubz nre très chier et amé cousin, aussi chlr de nre Ordre, le duc d'Alue, soubz lequel il est encoires à pnt en nre camp lez Dourlens, ayant grand desir et affection de continuer de bien en mieulx. "
2 CONT
2 CONT "Philippe de Lalaing" appears on the list of one hundred and sixteen gentlemen of the house of the king of Spain, drawn up on June 28, 1567 (65),
2 CONT
2 CONT The bastard of Bugnicourt also served during the troubles, notably as captain of the Walloon infantry at the siege of Valenciennes, in 1567, at the head of one hundred Walloon "arquebusiers de pied" under the due d'Albé, in 1568, 
2 CONC and in 1580, at the unfortunate expedition of the Douaisians against Bouchain, an expedition of which he was one of the leaders and where he fell to the rebels. We find him in Douai, his ordinary residence, in 1585 and in 1598, ca
2 CONC ptain of a bourgeois company.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died towards the beginning of March 1603, having made in Douai, on January 26, in the presence of his parish priest, the pastor of Notre-Dame, a will, in the "hold" of which, made in the hall, on March 11, he is called: "noble
2 CONT
2 CONT He was confused with the count of Lalaing, Philippe (second branch, XV); the latter, son and heir of a principal minister of the emperor and the king, could not be a simple, gentleman of the house.
2 CONT
2 CONT The latter, son and heir of a principal minister of the emperor and the king, could not be a simple gentleman of the house of the late Catholic Maté". He speaks in these terms of his wife Marie MARTINS : " And as I feel more estro
2 CONC ciously obliged towards her, for the great affection that she has always carried to me and the sincere friendship that I have received during our conjunction, signamt in that, for my enlargement of prison and to provide for my ran
2 CONC chon, she sold and adenieré her chaisnes, rings, jewels and some parts of rents ". He lies in the chapel of the name of Jesus to the minor brothers, or cordeliers. His widow, of whom he had left no children, made a will on Septemb
2 CONC er 23, 1612 and died at the beginning of October (66).
2 CONT
2 CONT On the large genealogical chart, with colored coat of arms in the cabinet of titles, "Phles de Lalaing, b. de Bugnicourt", whose wife's name is left blank, bears Lalaing broken by a golden fillet in bar.
2 CONT
2 CONT (64) Déjà en novembre 1551, à Bruxelles, Charles-Quint avait accordé des lettres de légitimation, sur la " supplication dé Phelippe, filz naturel de nre chier et feal chlr de nre ordre messire Ponthus de Lalaing, seigneur de Bugni
2 CONC court, à present gouuerneur et cappitaine de ,nre citadelle de Cambray, contenant que ledit suppliant soit engendré de pere et mere hors lestat de mariage... Veu le consentement dudit sr de Bugnicourt... Sera tenu parer certaine f
2 CONC inance et somme de deniers pour une fois, à nre prouffit, selon la faculté et. qualité de ses biens, à larbitraige et taxation de noz amez et feaulx les president et gens de noz comptes à Lille». (Archives départ., registre B 1762
2 CONC , f° 232.)
2 CONT (65) Gachard, Correspond, de Philippe II, I, p. 549.
2 CONT (66) Archives municip., reg. aux testam., 1599-1609, f° 105 v°, et 1608-1616, f° 181 v°.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 54-5
2 CONC 7:''
