1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jeanne de Lalaing'''
2 CONT (breaks her arms with a golden plain)
2 CONT married Maurand de Haussy, esquire, Lord of Remerchicourt, Alderman of Douai (1548, 1552 & 1557), Captain
2 CONT of La Bassecourt ° ~1485 + 04/12/1558 (La Bessecourt) (son of Jean, Receiver of the Domain in Douai (1491-1518), Bailiff of Douai (1504-1513), Captain of La Bassecourt, ennobled (1500) and of Antoine(tte) Le Preudhomme)
2 CONT
2 CONT posterity of which
2 CONT Antoinette & Jeanne de Haussy who married members of the du Hem d'Auby family (Jeanne married Robert du Hem, esquire)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Jeanne de Lalaing''' (who broke a golden plain), wife of Maurand DE HAUSSY, esquire, lord of Remerchicourt, born around 1485, chief of Douai in 1548, 1552 and 1557, died on December 4, 1558 at the palace of Bassecourt of which 
2 CONC he was "concierge"; we would say today: governor; - son of Jean de Haussy, receiver of the domain in Douai (1491-1518), bailiff of that city (1504-1513), "concierge" of Bassecourt, ennobled in 1500, and "demoiselle Anthoine" Le Pr
2 CONC eudhomme. They had two daughters, Antoinette and Jeanne de Haussy, who married into the du Hem d'Auby family.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 42.'
2 CONC '
