2 CONT '''Philippote de Lalaing''', widow in 1530 of Jacques DE TOUVILLE, squire, "familiar domesticq" of the count of Gavre, lying in Ghent, in the church of Saint-Michel. On her husband's tombstone, she bears: Argent with three fess of
2 CONC  Gules, with a full quarter of Lalaing (53); it was undoubtedly a combination of her father's and mother's coats of arms: at that time, the full arms put in a full quarter on any shield were a sign of bastardy. According to the ge
2 CONC nealogical table of the Cabinet des titres, she bore, like her two sisters, a golden plain,
