1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT http://gw.geneanet.org/frebault?lang=fr&pz=henri&nz=frebault&ocz=0&p=jeanne&n=de+ligne&oc=4
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''The royal descent and colonial ancestry of Mrs. Harley Calvin Gage (c1910)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/royaldescentcolo00gage
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/royaldescentcolo00gage#page/13/mode/1up/search/Lannoy
2 CONT *   LADY MAGDELAINE OF BURGUNDY, LADY OF FALAISE, was born 1489, died 1511. She was the granddaughter of Philippe III., the Magnificent, Duke of Burgundy and the Netherlands, and cousin of Marie, Duchess of Burgundy, Empress of Au
2 CONC stria, wife of the Emperor Maximilian I., of the Holy Roman Empire, 1493-1519, born 1459. She married, 1509, Philippe de Lannoy, Lord of Molembais, of Solre-le-Chateau, of Colroy and Lord of Turcoing in Flanders, born 1489, died 1
2 CONC 2th September, 1543. In 1531, he was created a Knight of the Order of the Golden Feece, his official number being CLXXXIII., and, in 1535, a Knight of the Imperial Order of the Golden Cross by the Emperor Charles V. , of Germany a
2 CONC nd the Holy Roman Empire, 1519-1556, to whom he was Councillor and Lord High Chamberlain. Philippe's grandfather was Baudouin de Lannoy, surnamed *'le Begue", Lord of Molembais and Governor of Lille, who, in 1429, was one of the t
2 CONC wenty Founder Knights at the institution of the Order of the Golden Fleece, his official number being XIX. He died 1474. The son of this nobleman, by his wife, Adrienne de Berlaymont, Lady of Solre-le-Chateau (died 29th April, 143
2 CONC 9), daughter of Jacques de Berlaymont, Lord of Solre-le-Chateau, by his wife, Catherine de Robersart, was Baudouin de Lannoy, Lord of Molembais and of Solre-le-Chateau, born 1438, died 7th May, 1501. He was a Knight of the Order o
2 CONC f the Golden Fleece, No. LXXXIX., Lord High Chamberlain and Grand Master of the Palace, 1477-1501, to Maximilian I., Emperor of Austria and of the Holy Roman Empire. He served with the Duke of Burgundy at the Siege of Beauvais in 
2 CONC 1472, and was the Governor of Zutphen. He married Michelle d'Esne, Lady of Colroy (died 22d April, 1511), daughter of Ame, Lord of Esne d'Haullien by his wife Habilan de Manilla, and was knighted by Maximilian I. This Baudouin de 
2 CONC Lannoy, as aforesaid, was the father of Phillipe de Lannoy, Lord of Molembais, &c., who married Lady Magdelaine of Burgundy as aforesaid, and their son ; 
2 CONT ** http://www.archive.org/stream/royaldescentcolo00gage#page/14/mode/1up
2 CONT **   JEAN DE LANNOY, LORD OF MOLEMBAIS, OF SOLRE-LE CHATEAU AND OF COLROY, born 1511, died 25th May, 1560. He was created Knight of the Order of the Golden Fleece in 1546, No. CCVIII., Lord High Chamberlain to Charles V., Emperor 
2 CONC of Germany, and of the Holy Roman Empire, 1519-1556, Governor of Hainault and Captain-General of Flanders in 1559. Jean married in 1534, Jeanne de Ligne, Lady of Barbancon, daughter of Louis de Ligne, Lord of Barbancon, by his wif
2 CONC e, Marie de Berghes, Heiress. Their only son ; 
2 CONT ***    GYSBERT THE HUGUENOT, >orn 1535, at Tourcoing in Flanders, was baptised in the Roman Catholic Church, but became a Protestant after the Siege of Tourcoing by the Huguenots, commonly so-called in derision after 1560, the wor
2 CONC d Huguenot signifying Confederate. Gysbert married, in 1558, the Protestant Heiress, Lady Marguerite de Ligne, and removed to Tournai in Hainault, where the public records show that he and his son Jean were residing in 1599. Gysbe
2 CONC rt' s sister, Marie, married Jean de Glymes, Marquis de Berghes, Count of Valhain and Knight of the Order of the Golden Fleece, a nobleman of Brababr.  He was created Marquis de Berghes, 23d May, 1533, by Charles V., German-Roman 
2 CONC Emperor (H.R.E.) - Gysbert's marriage with the Protestant Heiress and subsequent complete alliance with the Huguenots caused a serious family feud, he being the first Protestant in any branch of his family, and he was disinherited
2 CONC  by his father. The estates passed at the death of the latter, to his sister Marie, in 1560, and upon her death, 22d May, 1567, without issue, to her aunt Marie, who, in turn, left them to another niece. Gysbert used the coat-armo
2 CONC r of Barbancon, inherited from his mother, and the Lannoy armes of his paternal ancestors. His son ; 
2 CONT *________________
2 CONT *''''''Historic homes and institutions and genealogical and personal memoirs of ...   By Ellery Bicknell Crane
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=enUrAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA30&lpg=PA30&dq=Jean+De+Lannoy+May+25,+1560&source=bl&ots=7ZnP1dhxSt&sig=aUWV0fbcRlxvv0RmzF8HYDXIn7I&hl=en&ei=d5kTTvbiOKbViAL2t5yDDg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=9&ved=0C
2 CONC EoQ6AEwCA#v=onepage&q=Jean%20De%20Lannoy%20May%2025%2C%201560&f=false/ Historic homes and institutions and genealogical and personal memoirs of ...   By Ellery Bicknell Crane]
2 CONT *Pg. 30
2 CONT *  DELANO FAMILY. The descendants of the Pilgram ancestor, Philip Delano, of Plymouth, have the satisfaction of tracing their ancestry in the old country for a dozen centuries. They have established the full right to bear the arms
2 CONC  of the Delano family, which could be of no better stock and which embraces a host of distinguished men in its numbers.
2 CONT *   The name is drived from the town of Lannoy, a few miles from Isla, now Lille, France. Away back in A. D., 863, this town was called Alnetum, later L'Annois and Lannoy. The meaning of the word is unknown. It has been spelled L'
2 CONC Annois, L'Annoe, L'Aulmais, L'Aulnoy, but more often Alnetum. Today Lannoy is a small manugacturing town, seven miles from Lille, with a population at the last census 1,904. The first Lord of Lannoy, progenitor of the family, was 
2 CONC Hugues de Lannoy, mentioned as a knight of Tournai d'Auclin in 1096. On the same list was Simon do Alneto. A charte des Chanoines (cannons) de St. Pierre a Lille mentions Gilbert de Lannoy in 1171 and Hugues de Lannoy is mentioned
2 CONC  in 1186. It is impossible to present in this place an extended history of the family in its early days in France. That has been done with remarkable care and apparent accuracy in the genealogy, which is authority for all said her
2 CONC e about the origin and early history of the family. There seems to be no flaw in the following pedigree in the direct male line of the American emigrant, Philip Delano or Delanoy.
2 CONT *   1. Arnulphe de Franchmont. 2. Conrad de Franchmont. 3. Hellin, Marquis de Franchmont, married Agnes, daughter of Othon, Duke of Bavaria. 4. Hellin II de Franchmont, married Agnis de Duras. 5. Jean de Franchmont, married Mahien
2 CONC ne de Lannoy. 6. Hugues de Lannoy. 7. Hugues de Lannoy. 8. Guillebert de Lannoy. 9. Baudoin "Le Begue." 10. Baudouin. 11. Philipe. ''''''12. Jean, born about 1511, died May 25, 1560; was made chevalier de la Toison d'or in 1546; c
2 CONC hamberlain to the emperor Charles V from 1519 to 1556; gouvenor de Haymont and captain general of same province of Flanders in 1559; married Jeanne de Ligne de Barbancon, daughter of Louis de Ligne, seigneur de Barbancon and his w
2 CONC ife, Marie de Berghes''''''. 13. Gysbert de Lannoy, born at Tourcoing, 1545, of Roman Catholic parents, but became a Protestant and was disinherited by his father. 14. Jean of Leyden, was born 1570, died at Leyden, 1604. He marrie
2 CONC d at the Walloon Church (Tornai), January 13, 1596, Marie le Mahieu, of a Brabant family. 15. Philip, the American emigrant, see forward.
2 CONT *_______________
2 CONT *''''''Genealogical and family history of southern New York and the ..., Volume 3    By Cuyler Reynolds
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=iNIUAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1058&lpg=PA1058&dq=Jean+De+Lannoy+May+25,+1560&source=bl&ots=XekYAvtjTi&sig=5u6i628rFhIGpmlzmi6z80F3Dvs&hl=en&ei=PKATTqO1HJTZiAKzgcnpDQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ve
2 CONC d=0CDoQ6AEwBTgU#v=onepage&q=Jean%20De%20Lannoy%20May%2025%2C%201560&f=false/ Genealogical and family history of southern New York and the ..., Volume 3    By Cuyler Reynolds]
2 CONT *Pg. 1058
2 CONT *SAME AS Historic homes and institutions and genealogical and personal memoirs of ...   By Ellery Bicknell Crane
2 CONT *__________
