1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_I,_Count_of_Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles I, Count of Nevers (1414 – May 25, 1464), Count of Nevers and Rethel, was the son of Philip II, Count of Nevers and Bonne of Artois.
2 CONT
2 CONT Towards the end of the life of Philip III, Duke of Burgundy, Charles fell under suspicion of practising witchcraft, in an effort to supplant Charles, Count of Charolais as the heir. He precipitately fled to France and died soon af
2 CONC ter.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marie d'Albret, daughter of Charles II d'Albret on June 11, 1456, but had no legitimate children. He was succeeded by his brother John.
