1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewis_of_Luxembourg]
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis of Luxembourg; (died 1443). Bishop of Therouanne 1415-1436, Archbishop of Rouen, 1436, Bishop of Ely 1437,  Elevated to Cardina 18 December 1439 by Pope Eugenius IV at request of English King Henry VI 
2 CONT
2 CONT Chancellor of the Lancastrian council in Normandy where he was elected bishop and  the leading native administrator/collaborator with the Lancastrian regime in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT In September 1422 Louis, as the English Chancellor in France, was named along with with Lancastrian, Richard, Duke of York to a commission to attempt to negotiate a treaty with France and was empowered to select a suitable place f
2 CONC or a meeting.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis visited England in 1437 and became an English subject (citizen).   Henry VI granted him the bishopric of Ely in 1437 / 38
2 CONT
2 CONT  The Hundred Year's War would not unofficially end until ten years after Louis' death as result of the Battle of Castellon (1453)
