1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Thomas DRURY of Rougham
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1430, Rougham, Suffolk, England
2 CONT *'''Died: 12 Dec 1486, Rougham, Suffolk, England
2 CONT *'''Notes: 2nd cousin of Henry VI. 3 Feb 1461/62 Commissioned to arrest any persons guilty of unlawful gatherings/ congregations
2 CONT *Father: William DRURY of Rougham (Sir)
2 CONT *Mother: Catherine SWYNFORD
2 CONT *'''Married: Catherine WHITEWELL (dau. of John Whitewell) ABT 1455, Rougham, Suffolk, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. John DRURY of Rougham (Esq.)
2 CONT **2. Catherine DRURY
2 CONT **3. Elizabeth DRURY
2 CONT **4. Clement DRURY
2 CONT **5. Dorothy DRURY
2 CONT **6. Francis DRURY
2 CONT **7. Anne DRURY
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/DRURY.htm#Thomas DRURY of Rougham1
2 CONT *_________________________
2 CONT *'''from "Suffolk manorial Families", Vol. 1, pt. 9, 1899 by Joseph James Muskett. 
2 CONT *http://www.genealogysource.com/muskett346.htm
2 CONT *Pg.346
2 CONT **     Drury of Thurston
2 CONT *John Drury of Thurston, in Com. Suffolke, Esquier, sonne and heire tempre Kinge Edward first, 19, 1291. = Amabell daugh. of Thomas Newton, Esquier. Sables, too shanke bones in Salter argente.; ch: Sr Roger, Nicholas (m. Agnes Sax
2 CONC ham) Drury.
2 CONT *Nicholas Drury of Thurston in Com. Suffolke, esquier, sonne & heire, died 3rd 13 of Kinge Edw. 3d ao 1339; Will 7 Rich. 2, 1381, Cullum. = Agnes, sole daughter and heire of Sr Symond Saxham, Kt.Joane??, Joan in his will. Oullum.;
2 CONC  ch: Sr Roger (m. Margarett Naunton), Nicholas (m. Joanne Heathe), John Drury.
2 CONT * *Nicholas Drury of Saxham's in Thurston in Suffolke, 2d sonne, & of Hawsted, buried with his wife. Will, Gage, p. 428, Arch. Sudh., 4 Jan. 1454, proved 2 Sept. 1456. See note above. = Joanne, daugh. to Thomas Heathe, esquier, of
2 CONC  Mildenhall. ch: DRURY OF HAWSTEAD.
2 CONT ** *This Nicholas and Thom Heathe for love of John a Gaunte theire Captayne they tooke their voyage wt him into Spayne and theye have assumed to them Sellefs the Crosse Tawe in the Cheffe of there Armes ever since that tyme for th
2 CONC e Howse of Hawsted. Whilste he Florished at Thurston in the Auweiente house of Saxhams, which lande wt others Came by his Mother beinge heire to her father to him allso did desende the Mannor of Hawsted wt others: he lyeth Buryed 
2 CONC wt his wyfe in Thurston Church in a Chapell over aganst his fathers chap: where his Armes doeth appeare wt his Crosse Tuny. See below, Nicholas Drury.
2 CONT *Sr Roger Drury of Chauente in Rough. in Com. Suffolke, Knight in Right of his wyfe, sonne and heire, obijt 8th of K. Henry 5, ao 1419. Fines Div. Come. 6 H. 4. Will, Cur. Ep. Norw., Harl. MS. 10, fo. 226, proved 24 Oct. 1420. = M
2 CONC argarett, daugh. and sole heire of Sr Thomas Maunton of Chauente in Rougham, Kt, 4 II. 6, 1425. Gent. Mag. 1813.; ch: Margery, Joan, Elizabeth (m. John Baret), George (d. bef. father), Roger, Nicholas, Thomas, Margarett (m. Willia
2 CONC m Clopton), Sr William (m. Katherin Swynforde) Drury.
2 CONT *Sr William Drury of Rougham in Com. Suffolke, Knight, sonne & heire, lived in 14 yeare of K. Henry 6; ao d'ni 1435; obijt 28; of H; 6, 1449, Will, Cur. Ep. Norw., 10 June 1450, proved 27 June 1450, Harl. MS. 10, fo. 112. = Kather
2 CONC in, Daughter of Sr Hughe (Otes) Swynforde, Knight, and of Catherin, his wyfe, dau. of Payne Rowett als. Gugan Kinge of Armes; she after mar. to John Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster. This false.; ch: DRURY OF ROUGHAM.
2 CONT *http://www.genealogysource.com/muskett347.htm
2 CONT *Pg.347
2 CONT **     Drury of Rougham.
2 CONT *Sir William Drury of Rougham in Suffolk, son and heir of Sir Roger Drury and Margaret Naunton )see page 346). Will, Cur. Ep. Norw., 10 June 1450 (Harl. MS. 10) prob. 27 June 1450 and 24 Dec. 1476. = Catherine, dau. of Sir Thomas 
2 CONC Swynford, son of Sir Otes Swynford and of Catherine, his wife, dau. of Sir Payn Roet, Guyeene King of Arms, who after mar. in 1396 John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster. The Inq. p.m. of Catherine Drury was taken 19 K. 4, anno 1479.; c
2 CONC h: '''Thomas (m. Catherine Whitwell)''', Roger, George, Catherine, Anne, Mary (m. Edward Grimstone) Drury.
2 CONT *'''Thomas Drury of Rougham, Esq., son and heir to his mother; aged 50 in 1479. Inq. p.m., 3 H. 7, anno 1487. = Catherine, dau. and coh. of John Whitwell of Suffolk.; ch: John (m. Margaret Felton als. Chapman), Catherine (m. Rober
2 CONC t Rokewood), Elizabeth (m. Thomas Traas), Anne, Clement (m. Sarah Rowton) Drury.
2 CONT
