2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.theartnewspaper.com/news/a-wife-replaced-in-a-medieval-prayer-book
2 CONT
2 CONT *Isabella Stewart, Princess of Scotland
2 CONT *By Marriage Duchess Consort of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT ==biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella was born between 1425 and 1427, the daughter of James I, king of Scots, and Joan Beaufort. It was said she was more beautiful than her elder sister Margaret, and Jean VI, duc de Bretagne, proposed to marry her to his son 
2 CONC François I; thus he sent ambassadors to Scotland to take a description of her. They reported that she was handsome, upright and graceful, but that she also seemed simple. The Duke's reply was: 'My friends, return to Scotland and b
2 CONC ring her here, she is all I desire, and I will have no other; your clever women do more harm than good'. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella became the second wife of François I, duc de Bretagne, at the Château d'Auray on 30 October 1442, after which the whole court went to Rennes for eight days of festivities. She and François had two daughters, Marguerite an
2 CONC d Marie, who would both have progeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon the death of her sister Margaret, married to the future King Louis XI, Isabella penned an illuminated prayer book of hours, _Livre d'Isabeau d'Escosse,_ which is preserved to this day. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon her husband's death in 1450, there was talk of marriage between Isabella and the prince of Navarre, but this fell through due to the disapproval of Charles VII of France. Isabella died in 1494.BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Isabella was born between 1425 and 1427, the daughter of James I, king of Scots, and Joan Beaufort. It was said she was more beautiful than her elder sister Margaret, and Jean VI, duc de Bretagne, proposed to marry her to his son 
2 CONC François I; thus he sent ambassadors to Scotland to take a description of her. They reported that she was handsome, upright and graceful, but that she also seemed simple. The Duke's reply was: 'My friends, return to Scotland and b
2 CONC ring her here, she is all I desire, and I will have no other; your clever women do more harm than good'. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella became the second wife of François I, duc de Bretagne, at the Château d'Auray on 30 October 1442, after which the whole court went to Rennes for eight days of festivities. She and François had two daughters, Marguerite an
2 CONC d Marie, who would both have progeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon the death of her sister Margaret, married to the future King Louis XI, Isabella penned an illuminated prayer book of hours, _Livre d'Isabeau d'Escosse,_ which is preserved to this day. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon her husband's death in 1450, there was talk of marriage between Isabella and the prince of Navarre, but this fell through due to the disapproval of Charles VII of France. Isabella died in 1494.
2 CONT
