2 CONT *'''Joanna (Jean) Stewart1,2,3,4,5,6
2 CONT *'''F, #2934, b. circa 1428, d. between 16 October 1486 and 1490
2 CONT *Father      James I Stewart, King of Scotland7,8 b. c 25 Jul 1394, d. 21 Feb 1437
2 CONT *Mother     Joan Beaufort7,8 b. 1398, d. 15 Jul 1445
2 CONT *'''     Joanna (Jean) Stewart was born circa 1428 at of Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland.6 She married James Douglas, 1st Earl Morton, 3rd Lord Dalkeith, Ambassador to France & Castile, son of James Douglas, 2nd Lord Dalkeith and 
2 CONC Elizabeth Giffard, before 15 May 1459; They had 2 sons (Sir John, 2nd Earl of Morton; & James) and 2 daughters (Janet, wife of Patrick Hepburn, Earl of Bothwell; & Elizabeth).5,6 Joanna (Jean) Stewart and James Douglas, 1st Earl M
2 CONC orton, 3rd Lord Dalkeith, Ambassador to France & Castile obtained a marriage license on 7 January 1464; Date of Dispensation, being related in the 2nd and 3rd degrees. Joanna (Jean) Stewart died between 16 October 1486 and 1490.5,
2 CONC 6
2 CONT *'''Family      James Douglas, 1st Earl Morton, 3rd Lord Dalkeith, Ambassador to France & Castile b. c 1425, d. bt 22 Jun 1493 - 22 Oct 1493
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Janet Douglas+ d. b 21 Feb 1491
2 CONT **James Douglas3
2 CONT **Sir John Douglas, 2nd Earl Morton, 4th Lord Dalkeith+5,6 b. b 1466, d. bt 19 Jul 1511 - Sep 1515
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. IV, p. 40.
2 CONT * 2.[S11572] The Lineage and Ancestry of H.R.H. Prince Charles, Prince of Wales, by Gerald Paget, Vol. II, p. 395.
2 CONT * 3.[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 1788.
2 CONT * 4.[S11563] The Scots Peerage, Vol. I, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 19.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 579-580.
2 CONT * 6.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 658.
2 CONT * 7.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 577-578.
2 CONT * 8.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 655-656.
