1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eleanor Beaufort (1431–16 Aug 1501) was the daughter of Edmund Beaufort, 2nd Duke of Somerset and his second wife, Lady Eleanor Beauchamp, Duchess of Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor married Sir Robert Spencer in about 1470. They had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Catherine Spence'''r (1477–1542), who married Henry Percy, 5th Earl of Northumberland.
2 CONT # Margaret Spencer (c 1472) who married Thomas Carey.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor Beaufort (1431–16 Aug 1501) was the daughter of Edmund Beaufort, 2nd Duke of Somerset and his second wife, Lady Eleanor Beauchamp, Duchess of Somerset. She was a sister of the 3rd and 4th Dukes of Somerset.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1453, Eleanor's husband was Lieutenant of Ireland. When conflict broke out, the lieutenant fought on the Lancastrian side. He was present at the first battle of St. Albans in 1455, Mortimer's Cross in 1461 and at the battle of 
2 CONC Towton. Ormond also held the post of councillor to the Lancastrian Prince of Wales. After Towton, he was a proscribed traitor and was captured the same year at Cockermouth and executed there in 1461.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor married James Butler, 1st Earl of Wiltshire and 4th Earl of Ormond, K.G., on or around April 1458.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor next married Sir Robert Spencer in about 1470. They had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Catherine Spencer (1477–1542), who married Henry Percy, 5th Earl of Northumberland.
2 CONT     * Margaret Spencer (c 1472) who married Thomas Carey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor Beaufort
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #10454, d. 16 August 1501
2 CONT
2 CONT      Eleanor Beaufort was the daughter of Sir Edmund Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset and Lady Eleanor Beauchamp.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 She married, firstly, James Butler, 5th Earl of Ormonde, son of James Butler, 4th Earl of Ormonde and Elizabeth Beauchamp, circa April 1458 at Woodsford, Dorset, England.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Sir Robert Spencer circa 1470.2 She died on 16 August 1501.2
2 CONT
2 CONT      From circa April 1458, her married name became Butler.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 From circa 1470, her married name became Spencer.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Eleanor Beaufort and Sir Robert Spencer
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Catherine Spencer+ b. c 1480, d. c Oct 1542
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Margaret Spencer+2 b. c 1480
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund Beaufort, 2nd Duke of Somerset married before 1436, Lady Eleanor Beauchamp, widow of Thomas, 8th Lord Ros, daughter of Richard de Beauchamp, 13th Earl of Warwick and his first wife, Elizabeth, daughter and heir of Thomas, L
2 CONC ord Berkeley. Eleanor was an older half-sister of Henry de Beauchamp, 1st Duke of Warwick and Anne Neville, Countess of Warwick.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their unlicensed marriage was later pardoned on 7 March 1438, and they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor – married first James Butler, 5th Earl of Ormonde and second Sir Robert Spencer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (d. before 1472) – married Sir Henry Fitz Lewis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Beaufort, 2nd Duke of Somerset (1436–1464)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Beaufort, Countess of Stafford (bef. 1439–1474) – married first Humphrey, Earl of Stafford and second Sir Richard Darell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund Beaufort, styled 3rd Duke of Somerset (c. 1439– 4 May 1471)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Beaufort (c. 1453 – c. 1496) – married William Paston, Esq.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Beaufort, styled Marquess of Dorset (c. 1455– 4 May 1471)
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan Beaufort (d. 11 August 1518) – married first Sir Robert St. Lawrence and second Sir Richard Fry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Beaufort (c. 1455–c. 1463)
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Percy, 5th Earl of Northumberland
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Catherine Spencer, daughter of Sir Robert Spencer of Spencer Court and Lady Eleanor Beaufort. Her maternal grandparents were Edmund Beaufort, 2nd Duke of Somerset and Eleanor Beauchamp.
