2 CONT https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&pg=RA3-PA47&lpg=RA3-PA47&dq=Lady+Joan+St.+Lawrence+%28Beaufort%29&source=bl&ots=kvkINTGNd4&sig=lFAyDbPxpOlsvSJiEuhP3z1mVFc&hl=en&sa=X&ei=25uiVba5M4bxoASMypdw&ved=0CDcQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage
2 CONC &q=Lady%20Joan%20St.%20Lawrence%20%28Beaufort%29&f=false
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Daughter of Edward and Eleanor.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&pg=RA3-PA47&lpg=RA3-PA47&dq=Lady+Joan+St.+Lawrence+%28Beaufort%29&source=bl&ots=kvkINTGNd4&sig=lFAyDbPxpOlsvSJiEuhP3z1mVFc&hl=en&sa=X&ei=25uiVba5M4bxoASMypdw&ved=0CDcQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage
2 CONC &q=Lady%20Joan%20St.%20Lawrence%20%28Beaufort%29&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Frye being a close trustee of Henry 7, one could wonder if he didn't marry a woman from France, as henry was exiled many years before coming back to England. As war was raging in France, I will take some time trying to fin
2 CONC d out.  Henry came back in 1485, so if Richard Frye was Esq to the king's body, he must have proved himself in France, to the family of the future king, as he ended up marrying a Beaufort.
2 CONT
2 CONT Logic takes me to France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of the men who ended up in Henry 7's close circle after return did indeed go to france..
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.fr/books?id=ca87AwAAQBAJ&pg=PT43&lpg=PT43&dq=entourage+of+henry+tudor+in+france&source=bl&ots=gKzNVduviT&sig=ACfU3U3XEUwotvx_s0_c1wyHhGaJFFfO9A&hl=fr&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwia786DgYfqAhUGaBoKHfiVCxoQ6AEwAHoECA0QAQ#v=
2 CONC onepage&q=entourage%20of%20henry%20tudor%20in%20france&f=false
