2 CONT Notes about "Tacinda Tudor"
2 CONT * Not shown by Weir.
2 CONT * from [http://www.berkshirehistory.com/bios/otudor.html RBH Biography: Owen Tudor (1400-1461)] "They certainly had a daughter who died young, but suggestions that Thomasina, the wife of Reynold, Lord Grey of Wilton, was their dau
2 CONC ghter are incorrect." (Heavily Edited from Sidney Lee's 'Dictionary of National Biography' (1899))
2 CONT * from [http://www.tudor-queens.co.uk/1/post/2013/06/catherine-of-valois-children.html Catherine of Valois' Children] 06/29/2013  "Tacinda Tudor was born sometime around the end of 1432 or the beginning of 1433. She married Regina
2 CONC ld Grey, Baron Grey of Wilton. Unfortunately, that is about as much as we known of Tacinda. Her husband died in 1492." [incorrect]
2 CONT * from [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=timmychew&id=I127638&style=TEXT  "The Large Version of the Chew Family Tree"] The only evidence as to her parentage is in William's funeral ceremonial, which says (
2 CONC in part) that, of the gentlemen holding banners, "the iiij th Henrye Brereton, bearing the banneroll of the armes of the greate-graun dfather and greate-graundmother to the defunct in pale, Reygnolde lorde Grey, and Thomasyn or Th
2 CONC asyna base Unknown to John duke of Somersett." Vincent's Baronage, in the College of Arms, calls her Thaceta, Unknown of Owen Unknown of Tudor, but Vincent's source for this isn't known. See the second edition of Cokayne's *Comple
2 CONC te Peerage*, vol. VI, pp. 180-187, paying special attention to the footnotes.
