2 CONT * '''Children of Ralph Greystoke, Knt.. by Elizabeth Fitz Hugh.'''
2 CONT ** i. ROBERT GREYSTOKE, Knt. [See next].
2 CONT ** ii. MARGERY GREYSTOKE, married Thomas Gray, Knt. of Heaton (in Norham), Northumberland [see GRAY 11].[Ancestors of John Fenwick]
2 CONT ** iii. ELIZABETH GREYSTOKE, married (1st) THOMAS SCROPE, Knt., 5th Lord Scrope of Masham [see SCROPE 8]; [Ancestors of Anne Mauleverer] (2nd) GILBERT TALBOT, K.G., of Grafton, Worcestershire [see TALBOT 11].[Ancestors of Thomas R
2 CONC udyard]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====BOOKS
2 CONT * '''Surtees Society. 1865.''' ''Testamenta Eboracensia: A Selection of Wills from the Registry at York: Illustrative of the History, Manners...'' Edited by James Raine and John William Clay. Vol. 3. Durham, England, UK: Andrews &
2 CONC  Company. [https://archive.org/details/testamentaebora04claygoog?view=theater#page/n340/mode/2up Archive.org].
2 CONT ** “1435, July 1. Dispensation from Eugenius IV., issued at Florence, allowing Ralph, sone of John lord Greystock, and ELIZABETH, DAUGHTER OF WILLIAM LORD FITZHUGH, to marry, although related iii the 4th degree:— 
2 CONT ** “On Nov. sand, 1434, William Ayscough, lawyer and gentleman, Richard Burgh, domicelius, and Richard Sedgwick are examined before the archbishop in the hospital of St, James near Westminster, find testify us follows. Sir Henry F
2 CONC izherry, knt., was the father of Henry and Joan Fitzhugh; Henry was the father of another Henry, and the grandfather of William, now lord Fltzhugh, the sire of Elizabeth, one of the petitioners who appears in tbe person of her pro
2 CONC ctor, John Catterick. Or other side, it is shown that Joan daughter of Sir Henry Fizherry knt, married William baron of Grey stock, the father of Ralph, the father of John, the father of Ralph the petitioner. The claim was allowed
2 CONC , Ibid. 168-9.”
2 CONT * '''Surtees Society. 1868.''' ''Testamenta Eboracensia: A Selection of Wills from the Registry at York: Illustrative of the History, Manners...'' Vol. 4 (orig. v.53). Edited by James Raine and John William Clay. Vol. 3. Durham, E
