1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Greystoke-36
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor was the daughter of John, 4th Baron Greystoke and Elizabeth Ferrers.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor is named in her father's 1436 will.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Ralph de Eure (d. 1461 Battle of Towton).[1][2] The Grey Friars Research Team (set up in 2012 under the auspices of the University of Leicester) give a marriage date of 1440[4] but it is not clear what the basis for that is and
2 CONC  some of the information they give is unreliable (see for instance the [Research Notes] on the profile of her son William). They had twelve children (dates given by the Gery Friars Research team need to be checked against other so
2 CONC urces):
2 CONT
2 CONT # William,[1][2] c.1440-c.1500 (see his profile),
2 CONT # John,[1][2] said by the Grey Friars Research team to be born in about 1452 ; his will was proved in 1493 said by the Grey Friars Research Team to be born in about 1446 and a twin of Henry[4]
2 CONT # Hugh, a priest,[1][2] said by the Grey Friars Research team to have been born in about 1456; his will was proved in 1523[4]
2 CONT # Ralph,[1][2] for whom the Grey Friars Research team gives dates of c.1442 to before 9 June 1484[4]
2 CONT # Henry,[1][2] said by the Grey Friars Research Team to be born about 1446 and to be a twin of John/Joan[4]
2 CONT # Robert,[1][2] said by the Grey Friars Research Team to be born in about 1450[4]
2 CONT # Elizabeth, who married John Ellerker[1][2] and whose dates are given by the Grey Friars Research Team as c.1441 to before 1484[4]
2 CONT # Joan[1][2] said by the Grey Friars Research Team to be born about 1438 and to have died single[4]
2 CONT # Margaret, who became a nun[1][2] and was said by the Grey Friars Research team to be born in about 1448[4]
2 CONT # another Joan[1][2] or John (whether the child was called Joan or John depends on whether a record should be transcribed as "Johanni" (masculine genitive) or "Johanna" (feminine), said by the Grey Friars Research Team to be born 
2 CONC in about 1446 and a twin of Henry[4][4]
2 CONT # Maud (according to Richardson[1][2]), possibly the same as the Mary said by the Grey Friars Research team to be born in about 1458 and to have married someone with the last name Hilton[4]
2 CONT # Anne, who married Thomas Rokeby[1][2] and is said by the Grey Friars Research Team to have been born in about 1454[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Eleanor Greystoke1,2,3,4,5,6,7
2 CONT *F, #34859
2 CONT *Father	Sir John Greystoke, 4th Baron Greystoke, Governor of Roxburgh Castle2,3,4,5,6,7 b. c 1390, d. 8 Aug 1436
2 CONT *Mother	Elizabeth Ferrers2,3,4,5,6,7 b. c 1393, d. 1434
2 CONT *'''     Eleanor Greystoke married Sir Ralph Eure''', son of Sir William Eure, Sheriff of Yorkshire & Northumberland, Steward of Holderness and Matilda (Maud) FitzHugh, '''circa 1438 at of Greystoke, Cumberland, England; They had 
2 CONC 6 sons''' (Sir William; John; Hugh, LL.D; Ralph; Henry; & Sir Robert) '''& 6 daughters''' (Elizabeth, wife of John Ellerker; Joan; Margaret, nun at Watton; Joan; Maud; & Anne, wife of Thomas Rokeby).2,3,4,5,6,7
2 CONT *'''Family     Sir Ralph Eure''' b. c 1415, d. 9 Mar 1462
2 CONT *'''Child	
2 CONT **Sir William Eure, Sheriff of Yorkshire+2,4,6 b. 18 Feb 1440, d. a 3 Jul 1497
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S10789] Unknown author, The Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles, by Gerald Paget, Vol. II, p. 408.
2 CONT *[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 296.
