2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/GREYSTOKE.htm#Eleanor GREYSTOKE1 __________________________
2 CONT *John [de Greystock], 4th Baron Greystock
2 CONT *born     c. 1390
2 CONT *mar.     after 28 Oct 1407 Elizabeth Ferrers (b. c. 1393; d. 1434), 1st dau. and cohrss. of Robert [Ferrers], 2nd Baron Ferrers of Wemme, by his wife Lady Joan Beaufort, legitimated dau. of John [Plantagenet], 1st Duke of Lancast
2 CONC er (by his mistress and later third wife Katharine Swynford, widow of Sir Hugh Swynford, of Kettlethorpe, co. Lincoln, and 2nd dau. and cohrss. of Sir Payne de Roet, Guienne King of Arms), 4th son of King Edward III
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **1. Ralph de Greystock, later 5th Baron Greystock
2 CONT **2. Thomas de Greystock (dsp.)
2 CONT **3. Richard de Greystock (dsp.)
2 CONT **4. William de Greystock (dsp.)
2 CONT **5. John de Greystock (dsp.)
2 CONT **6. Henry de Greystock (dsp.)
2 CONT **'''1. Eleanor de Greystock, mar. Sir Ralph Eure, of Stokesley, Malton, etc., co .York''' (d. at the Battle of Towton 1461), '''and had issue
2 CONT **2. Katherine de Greystock, a nun at Barking
2 CONT **3. Joan de Greystock, mar. (1) Sir John Darcy (d. 1455/6), 2nd son of John [Darcy], 5th Baron Darcy de Knayth, by his wife Margaret de Grey, only dau. of Henry [de Grey], 5th Baron Grey of Wilton, and (2) 1458 William Stoke, and
2 CONC  had issue by her first husband
2 CONT **4. Elizabeth de Greystock, mar. Roger Thornton, of Newcastle, merchant and landowner, and had issue
2 CONT **5. Anne de Greystock (d. betw. 6 Dec 1476 and 12 May 1478), mar. 18 Feb 1432 Sir Ralph Bigod, of Settrington, co. York (d. at the Battle of Towton 1461), and had issue
2 CONT *died     8 Aug 1436
2 CONT *suc. by     son
2 CONT *note     Keeper of Roxburgh Castle 1420/1
