2 CONT ==Sir Henry Percy==
2 CONT '''Birth	25 Jul 1421'''
2 CONT '''Alnwick, Northumberland Unitary Authority, Northumberland, England'''
2 CONT '''Death	29 Mar 1461 (aged 39)'''
2 CONT '''Towton, Selby District, North Yorkshire, England'''
2 CONT '''Burial	St Dennis Churchyard'''
2 CONT '''York, York Unitary Authority, North Yorkshire, England'''
2 CONT Find a Grave Memorial ID: 104698815
2 CONT '''Knight, 3rd Earl of Northumberland, 6th Lord Percy. King's Knight, Warden of the east March, Captain of Berwick, Constable of Scarborough Castle.'''
2 CONT '''Son and heir''' to Sir Henry Percy, 5th Lord Percy and Eleanor de Neville. '''Grandson of''' Sir Henry Hotspur Percy and Elizabeth de Mortimer, Sir Ralph de Neville and Joan de Beaufort, daughter of John of Gaunt. '''First cous
2 CONC in of''' Edward IV of England, Margaret of York, George, Duke of Clarence and Richard III of England.
2 CONT '''Husband of Lady Eleanor de Poynings''', daughter and heiress of Sir Richard Poynings, descendant of King Edward I and his second wife, Countess of Arundel, Eleanor de Berkeley, daughter of Sir John of Beverstone, descendant of 
2 CONC King John. '''They married before 25 June 1435 and had one son and three daughters''':
2 CONT Sir Henry Percy, 4th Earl of Northumberland, Knight of the Garter
2 CONT Eleanor, wife of Sir Thomas West, Lord West, Lord la Warre
2 CONT Margaret, wife of Sir William Gascoigne of Gawthorpe, Yorkshire
2 CONT Elizabeth, wife of Sir Henry Scrope, Lord Scrope of Bolton
2 CONT '''As a result of this marriage, he was summoned to Parliament from Dec 1446 to May 1455 as Henrico de Percy, chivaler, domino de Ponynges. Henry was taken prisoner at the Battle of Sark in 1448 where his father was defeated, at t
2 CONC he Battle of Wakefield 30 Dec 1460 and was slain fighting for King Henry VI at the Battle of Towden 29 March 1461, buried at St Dionis (St Denys) at Yorkshire.''' Eleanor died 11 Feb 1484.
2 CONT The picture placed by Sharon Lee Fisher Martin is evidently one of Henry Wriothesley, 3rd Earl of Southampton (1573-1624), NOT Sir Henry Percy.
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT '''Parents'''
