1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Ralph Percy==
2 CONT '''Sir Ralph Percy (died 1464) was a knight, a Governor of Bamburgh Castle and a supporter of the Lancastrian side in the Wars of the Roses. Percy was the grandson of Sir Harry (Hotspur) Percy.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Percy married, firstly, Eleanor Acton and they had six children:
2 CONT *1.Sir Ralph Percy
2 CONT * 2.Peter Percy
2 CONT * 3.Sir Henry Percy
2 CONT * 4.George Percy
2 CONT * 5.John Percy
2 CONT * 6.Margaret Percy
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Ralph married, secondly Jane Teye. They had a child''', Catherine Percy.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During 1462 and 1463, the Lancastrians attempted to destabilise the kingdom, ruled by their Yorkist enemy, Edward IV. These attempts were concentrated in the north of England and directed by the Lancastrian Queen, Margaret of A
2 CONC njou (Henry VI's queen).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Earl of Warwick led campaigns to neutralise the Lancastrians in the north in the early 1460s. As a result Sir Ralph Percy surrendered Bamburgh Castle to Edward IV, on Christmas Eve 1462 in return for a free pardon. Sir Ralp
2 CONC h swore allegiance to Edward IV and, as part of Edward IV’s policy of conciliation, Percy’s lands were then returned to him. Sir Ralph took control of both Bamburgh and Dunstanburgh Castles, under his surrender agreement with Edwa
2 CONC rd.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fighting in the north continued, exacerbated by a Scottish invasion. When the Scots sued for peace, Lord Montague was sent to arrange terms. On 25 April 1464, Montague was on his way to Norham. The Duke of Somerset (who had sur
2 CONC rendered and sworn allegiance with Percy) and Percy, forswearing their oaths, attacked Montague with 5,000 men. The site of that battle was Hedgeley Moor, seven miles south of Wooler. Percy led Somerset's vanguard and was killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT *1 England families, genealogical and memorial By William Richard Cutter, p. 775
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Percy
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________
