1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir Richard Percy (1426/7–29 March 1461, Battle of Towton)
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations 
2 CONT #  "The Extinct and Dormant Peerages of the Northern Counties of England" by J.W. Clay. "Percy, Lords Percy, Earls of Northumberland."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Towton The Battle of Towton] was fought during the English Wars of the Roses on 29 March 1461, near the village of the same name in Yorkshire. It was "probably the largest and bloodiest batt
2 CONC le ever fought on English soil".[2] According to chroniclers, more than 50,000 soldiers from the Houses of York and Lancaster fought for hours amidst a snowstorm on that day, which was Palm Sunday. A newsletter circulated a week a
2 CONC fter the battle reported that 28,000 died on the battlefield. The engagement brought about a monarchical change in England—Edward IV displaced Henry VI as King of England, driving the head of the Lancastrians and his key supporter
2 CONC s out of the country.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://histfam.familysearch.org/getperson.php?personID=I3463&tree=EuropeRoyalNobleHous
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p10743.htm#i107425
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=allerton%5Fmanor&id=I25476
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Percy,_2nd_Earl_of_Northumberland
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________
