2 CONT * “Complete Peerage Addition: Marriage of Edward Hastings and Mary Hungerford.”  Soc.Gen.medieval, post by Douglas Richardson, August 26, 2004.  < [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/4OWvWgCenPA/m/nZXCSuqEVmoJ li
2 CONC nk] > Complete Peerage 6 (1926): 622-623 (sub Hungerford) has a useful account of the lives of Edward Hastings, Lord Hastings (died 1506) and his wife, Mary Hungerford, Lady Botreaux. Regarding their marriage, the editor states: "
2 CONC m[arried], between this date [8 June 1478] and 18 Feb. 1480/1" [when Mary and her husband had license of entry into her great-grandmother's inheritance].
2 CONT * https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p914.htm#i27442
2 CONT * https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00109530&tree=LEO cites 
2 CONT # [S00120] Cahiers de Saint Louis , Dupont, Jacques and Saillot, Jacques. 826 
2 CONT # [S00010] A Genealogical History of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited and extinct peerages of the British Empire, London, 1866, Burke, Sir Bernard. 292 
2 CONT # [S00119] The Lineage and Ancestry of H.R.H. Prince Charles, Prince of Wales, Edinburgh, 1977, Paget, Gerald. Q 115388 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LR31-7VB/anne-percy-1436-1522
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Percy-43
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/82559542/ann-raynsford_vaughan
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Percy Hungerford Raynsford Vaughan
2 CONT
2 CONT Youngest child of Sir Henry Percy, 2nd Earl of Northumberland, Lord Percy, Descendant pf King Edward III by Eleanor de Neville, daughter of Sir Ralph de Neville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Thomas Hungerford, married before 16 Oct 1460, the date of the marriage charter. They had two daughters, Elizabeth and Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Hungerford sided with the Lancastrians, was attained and put to death near Salisbury as a traitor 18 Jan 1469.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne married again, before 06 June 1476 to Sir Laurence Raynsford, Knight of Colchester and Bradfield, Essex, of Alpheton and Great Whelnetham, Suffolk, son of Sir William Raynsford by Eleanor, daughter and heiress of Edmund de Br
2 CONC oxbourne. Laurence had been previously married to Elizabeth de Fiennes, widow of William Cromer of Tunstall, Kent then Alexander Iden of Kent. She was the daughter of Sir James de Fiennes, Lord Say. Anne and Laurence had children.
2 CONC  Laurnce died testate 18 Sept 1490.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne married a third time to Sir Hugh Vaughan of Littleton and St Peter, Westminster, Middlesex, Captain of Jersey who died testate in 1536.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne died 05 July 1522 and was buried at Long Melford, Suffolk.
