1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William FitzAlan, 16th Earl of Arundel
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT The new Earl married Joan Neville. Joan was a daughter of Richard Neville, 5th Earl of Salisbury and Alice Montagu, Countess of Salisbury. Alice was a daughter of Thomas Montacute, 4th Earl of Salisbury and Eleanor Holland. Eleano
2 CONC r was a daughter of Thomas Holland, 2nd Earl of Kent and Alice FitzAlan. Alice was a daughter of Richard FitzAlan, 10th Earl of Arundel and Eleanor of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Joan had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas FitzAlan, 17th Earl of Arundel (1450 – 1524).
2 CONT
2 CONT William FitzAlan.
2 CONT
2 CONT George FitzAlan.
2 CONT
2 CONT John FitzAlan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary FitzAlan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas FitzAlan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan NEVILLE (C. Arundel)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 3 Feb 1423, Salisbury, Wiltshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: BEF 9 Sep 1462
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Richard NEVILLE (1° E. Salisbury)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Alice MONTAGUE (C. Salisbury)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: William FITZALAN (15° E. Arundel) AFT 17 Aug 1438, Salisbury, Wiltshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. William FITZALAN
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. George FITZALAN
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. John FITZALAN
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Mary FITZALAN
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Thomas FITZALAN (16° E. Arundel)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p1422.htm#i14212
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan Neville1 
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #14212, d. before 9 September 1462
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=11 Apr 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.3%
2 CONT
2 CONT      Joan Neville was the daughter of Sir Richard de Neville, 5th Earl of Salisbury and Alice Montagu, Countess of Salisbury.1 She married Sir William Fitzalan, 16th Earl of Arundel, son of Sir John d'Arundel, 13th Earl of Arundel
2 CONC  and Eleanor Betteshorne, after 17 August 1438.1 She died before 9 September 1462.1 She was buried at Arundel Castle, Arundel, Sussex, England.2
2 CONT
2 CONT      From after 17 August 1438, her married name became Fitzalan.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Joan Neville and Sir William Fitzalan, 16th Earl of Arundel
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas FitzAlan, 17th Earl of Arundel+ b. c 1450, d. 25 Oct 15242
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 17. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 10
2 CONC 6th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct 
2 CONC or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 248. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
