1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Cecily Neville, Duchess of Warwick==
2 CONT '''Cecily Neville, 1st Duchess of Warwick, 1st Countess of Worcester (c.1425 – 26 July 1450) was a daughter''' of Richard Neville, 5th Earl of Salisbury and Alice Montacute, 5th Countess of Salisbury. '''Her siblings included''' R
2 CONC ichard Neville, 16th Earl of Warwick; John Neville, 1st Marquess of Montagu; George Neville, (Archbishop of York and Chancellor of England); Katherine Neville, Baroness Hastings; and Alice Neville, Baroness FitzHugh.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was most likely named after her paternal aunt''', Cecily Neville, Duchess of York.[2] '''Her first cousins included''' Anne of York, Duchess of Exeter; Edmund, Earl of Rutland; Elizabeth of York, Duchess of Suffolk; Margare
2 CONC t of York; George Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Clarence; and Kings Edward IV and Richard III.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She first married Henry de Beauchamp, 1st Duke of Warwick and the only King of the Isle of Wight (as well as of Jersey and Guernsey). Their only daughter''' was Lady Anne Beauchamp, who was allowed to succeed as suo jure 15th C
2 CONC ountess of Warwick. Upon the death of the 15th Countess, the title was inherited by her paternal aunt, also named Lady Anne. Lady Anne married '''Cecily's brother''', Richard Neville, who would become jure uxoris 16th Earl of Warw
2 CONC ick.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Her second husband was John Tiptoft, 1st Earl of Worcester. They had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She is buried with her first husband, the Duke of Warwick, in Tewkesbury Abbey.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cecily_Neville,_Duchess_of_Warwick
2 CONT
