2 CONT *'''     Cicely Neville was the daughter''' of Richard de Neville, 5th Earl of Salisbury and Alice Montagu, Countess of Salisbury.1 '''She married, firstly, Henry de Beauchamp, 1st Duke of Beauchamp''', son of Richard Beauchamp, 1
2 CONC 3th Earl of Warwick and Isabel le Despenser, '''in 1434.2 She and John Tiptoft, 1st Earl of Worcester obtained a marriage license on 3 April 1449.2 She died on 28 July 1450.2 She was buried on 31 July 1450 at Tewkesbury Abbey, Tew
2 CONC kesbury, Gloucestershire, England.1
2 CONT *'''      From 1434, her married name became de Beauchamp.2 She held the office of Sheriff of Worcestershire in 1449.2 From 3 April 1449, her married name became Tiptoft.2 As a result of her marriage, Cicely Neville was styled as 
2 CONC Countess of Worcester on 16 July 1449.
2 CONT *'''Child of Cicely Neville and Henry de Beauchamp, 1st Duke of Beauchamp
