1 OCCU 1st Marquis Montague
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00058021&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT John Neville, 1st Marquess of Montagu, alias John Mortimer, called the Captain of Kent (c. 1431 – 14 April 1471) was a Yorkist leader in the Wars of the Roses, best-known for eliminating Lancastrian resistance in the north of Engl
2 CONC and during the early part of the reign of Edward IV of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Montagu was a younger son of Richard Neville, 5th Earl of Salisbury and Alice Montagu, Countess of Salisbury, and a brother of Warwick the Kingmaker.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought at the Battle of Blore Heath and was captured and imprisoned by the Lancastrians. After the Yorkist victory at Northampton he was released, but was captured again at the Second Battle of St Albans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following his second release from imprisonment, he led the Yorkist forces in the north of England, defeating the Lancastrians at Hedgeley Moor and again at Hexham (both 1464).
2 CONT
2 CONT In reward for driving out the Lancastrians, Montagu was created Earl of Northumberland. This title had long been held by the Percy family, but they were in disgrace. However, when Henry Percy was rehabilitated in 1470, Montagu was
2 CONC  forced to give up the earldom and many important offices in favour of his former foe.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was in compensation created Marquess of Montagu, but without suitable estates to support such a dignity. Now set against Edward IV, he joined his brother Warwick the Kingmaker in the restoration of Henry VI. Montagu returned to
2 CONC  high office in the north, but was killed at the Battle of Barnet.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Isabel Ingoldsthorpe (1441-1476) and had seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anne Neville, married Sir William Stonor
2 CONT     * Isabelle Neville, married Sir William Huddleston, then Sir William Smythe
2 CONT     * Elizabeth Neville, married Sir Henry Wentworth
2 CONT     * John Neville, died sp bef. 1483(dead at birth)
2 CONT     * Margaret Neville, married Sir John Mortimer, then Charles Brandon, 1st Duke of Suffolk
2 CONT     * George Neville, Duke of Bedford (c. 1457–1483), died sp
2 CONT     * Lucy Neville, married Sir Anthony Browne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy Neville was the Ancestor of President Franklin Roosevelt and Sir Winston Churchill.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel married a year after his death, to Sir William Norreys.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Neville,_1st_Marquess_of_Montagu
2 CONT --------------------
