2 CONC ville Earl of Salisbury", dated 10 May 1458, bequeathed property to “my eldest son Richard Earl of Warwick...my son George...my daughter Alice...my daughter Eleanor...my daughter Katherine...my daughter Margaret...my daughter the 
2 CONC Countess of Arundel...my brother Lord William Fauconberg...Alice my wife Countess of Salisbury”[1920]. 
2 CONT **	10.      RALPH (-young, bur Sheriff Hooton).  A mid-15th century manuscript names "Johanna comitissa Arundelie, Alienora comitissa Warwici, Ricardus filius prim, ---, Johannes de Neuille, Georgius de Neuille clericus, Alesia…Al
2 CONC ienora, Radulphus mortuus apud Shirefhoton sepultus, Katherina…Robertus mortuus apud Midelham sepultus" as the children of "Ricardum Neuille comitem Sarum" and his wife "Alesia comitissa Sarum et heres"[1921]. 
2 CONT **	11.      CATHERINE (-[22 Nov 1503/25 Mar 1504]).  A mid-15th century manuscript names "Johanna comitissa Arundelie, Alienora comitissa Warwici, Ricardus filius prim, ---, Johannes de Neuille, Georgius de Neuille clericus, Alesi
2 CONC a…Alienora, Radulphus mortuus apud Shirefhoton sepultus, Katherina…Robertus mortuus apud Midelham sepultus" as the children of "Ricardum Neuille comitem Sarum" and his wife "Alesia comitissa Sarum et heres"[1922].  The will of "Ri
2 CONC chard Neville Earl of Salisbury", dated 10 May 1458, required “that the marriage covenants made for the marriage of Catherine my daughter with the son and heir apparent of William Lord Harrington, the son of William Lord Bonville”
2 CONC , names “my mother Joan late Countess of Westmoreland, and my father Ralph late Earl of Westmoreland”, bequeathed property to “my eldest son Richard Earl of Warwick...my son George...my daughter Alice...my daughter Eleanor...my da
2 CONC ughter Katherine...my daughter Margaret...my daughter the Countess of Arundel...my brother Lord William Fauconberg...Alice my wife Countess of Salisbury”[1923].  m firstly (1458) WILLIAM Bonville Baron Harington, son of WILLIAM Bo
2 CONC nville & his wife Elizabeth Harington (1443-killed in battle Wakefield 31 Dec 1460).  m secondly (before 6 Feb 1462) WILLIAM Hastinges of Kirby, Leicestershire Lord Hastings, son of LEONARD Hastinges & his wife Alice de Camoys ([1
2 CONC 430/31]-executed Tower of London 13 Jun 1483, bur Windsor, St George’s Chapel). 
2 CONT **	12.      ROBERT (-young, bur Middleton).  A mid-15th century manuscript names "Johanna comitissa Arundelie, Alienora comitissa Warwici, Ricardus filius prim, ---, Johannes de Neuille, Georgius de Neuille clericus, Alesia…Alieno
2 CONC ra, Radulphus mortuus apud Shirefhoton sepultus, Katherina…Robertus mortuus apud Midelham sepultus" as the children of "Ricardum Neuille comitem Sarum" and his wife "Alesia comitissa Sarum et heres"[1924]. 
2 CONT **	13.      MARGARET (-after 20 Nov 1506, bur Colne Priory).  A manuscript pedigree dated to [1500] names "Countess of Oxford" as daughter of "Richard Earl of Salisbury"[1925].  The will of "Richard Neville Earl of Salisbury", dat
2 CONC ed 10 May 1458, bequeathed property to “my eldest son Richard Earl of Warwick...my son George...my daughter Alice...my daughter Eleanor...my daughter Katherine...my daughter Margaret...my daughter the Countess of Arundel...my brot
2 CONC her Lord William Fauconberg...Alice my wife Countess of Salisbury”[1926].  m as his first wife, JOHN de Vere Earl of Oxford, son of JOHN de Vere Earl of Oxford & his wife Elizabeth Howard (8 Sep 1442-Hedingham Castle 10 Mar 1513, 
2 CONC bur Colne Priory). 
2 CONT *From: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#RichardNevilleSalisburydied1460B _____________________
