2 CONT
2 CONT George Neville held the office of Prebendary of York in 1446.
2 CONT
2 CONT He graduated from Balliol College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, in 1450 with a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.).
2 CONT
2 CONT He graduated from Balliol College, Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, in 1452 with a Master of Arts (M.A.).
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Chancellor of Oxford University between 1453 and 1457.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Prebendary of Lincoln in 1454.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Prebendary of Ripon in 1454.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Archdeacon of Northampton in 1454.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 21 December 1454 he was ordained.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Bishop of Exeter in 1458.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Lord Chancellor between 1460 and 1467.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Archdeacon of Carlisle before May 1463.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Archbishop of York between 1464 and 1476. He held the office of Lord Chancellor in 1470.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the Abbot in 1475 at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.
2 CONT
