2 CONT *'''Catherine NEVILLE (B. Ashby-Zouche)
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1435, Salisbury, Wiltshire, England
2 CONT *'''Died: 22 Nov 1503 / AFT 25 Mar 1504
2 CONT *'''Buried: Ashby de la Zouche
2 CONT *'''Notes: left a widow at the age of eighteen. She did not, however, remain a widow for long; shortly before 6 Feb 1462 her brother Richard Neville, Earl of Warwick, arranged a marriage between her and William Hastings, 1st Baron
2 CONC  Hastings, a close friend of Edward IV. On 9 Apr 1483, King Edward died; his son Edward V and kingdom were placed under the guardianship of his youngest brother Richard, Duke of Gloucester. It was Catherine's husband William Hasti
2 CONC ngs who advised Richard to take the young King Edward V into protective custody immediately following the death of Edward IV. It was about this time that Catherine's husband became the lover of Jane Shore, a former mistress of bot
2 CONC h the late King Edward IV and her son-in-law, Thomas Grey, Marquess of Dorset. She encouraged him to enter into a conspiracy with the Woodville family against Gloucester. Richard, upon discovering Hastings' treachery ordered his i
2 CONC mmediate execution, which took place on 13 Jun 1483 at the Tower of London. Several weeks later, Richard sealed an indenture, swearing to take Catherine directly under his protection and to "secure for her the enjoyment of her hus
2 CONC band's lands, goods, privileges, and the custody not only of their heir until the boy came of age but also the wardship of the young Earl of Shrewsbury who was married to their daughter, Anne". Richard assured Catherine that Hasti
2 CONC ngs would never be attainted, and that she would be defended against any attempt by intimidation or fraud to deprive her of her rights. Shortly after Hastings' death, on 22 Jun, Richard proclaimed himself King of England. Catherin
2 CONC e never remarried.
2 CONT *Father: Richard NEVILLE (1° E. Salisbury)
2 CONT *Mother: Alice MONTAGUE (C. Salisbury)
2 CONT *'''Married 1: William BONVILLE (2° B. Bonville and 6° Harrington)''' (b. ABT 1442 - d. 30 Dec 1460) (son of William Bonville, 1° B. Bonville, and Elizabeth Harrington) '''BEF 1458
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Cecily BONVILLE (M. Dorset) (b. 30 Jun 1460 - d. 12 May 1529) (m.1 Thomas Grey, 1° M. Dorset - m.2 Henry Stafford, 3º E. Wiltshire) (See her Biography)
2 CONT *'''Married 2: William HASTINGS (1° B. Ashby-Zouche) 6 Feb 1461, Salisbury, Wiltshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **2. Ralph HASTINGS (b. ABT 1463)
2 CONT **3. Elizabeth HASTINGS
2 CONT **4. Edward HASTINGS (2º B. Ashby-Zouche)
2 CONT **5. Richard HASTINGS (b. ABT 1468)
2 CONT **5. William HASTINGS
2 CONT **7. Anne HASTINGS (C. Shrewsbury)
2 CONT **8. George HASTINGS (b.  ABT 1472)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/NEVILLE2.htm#Catherine NEVILLE (B. Ashby-Zouche) __________________
2 CONT *'''Katherine de Neville Hastings
2 CONT *'''Birth: 	1442  Salisbury, Wiltshire, England
2 CONT *'''Death: 	1504, England
2 CONT *'''Katherine de Neville Bonville Hastings
2 CONT *'''Fifth daughter and one of ten children''' of Richard de Neville, 5th Earl of Salisbury and Alice Montagu. '''Granddaughter of''' Sir Ralph de Neville and Lady Joan de Beaufort (the daughter of John of Gaunt and Katherine de Ro
2 CONC et), Thomas Montagu, 4th Earl of Salisbury and Eleanor de Holland. '''Katherine was born in 1442 at Salisbury.
2 CONT *'''Wife of Sir William Bonville, 6th Lord Harington''', son of Sir William Bonville and Elizabeth Harington. '''They were married in 1458 and had one daughter''', Cecily, who married Sir Thomas Grey. Sir William was a Yorkist, ca
2 CONC ptured and beheaded on the battlefield at the Battle of Wakefield along with his father 31 Dec 1460, making '''Katherine one of the wealthiest heiresses of all England at age eighteen.
2 CONT *'''Her brother''', Richard 'the Kingmaker' '''arranged her next marriage to Sir William Hastings''', the son of Sir Leonard Hastings and Alice de Camoys. '''They were married by 1462 and had six children:
2 CONT **Richard Hastings (1464 - 1465)
2 CONT **William Hastings (1466 - 1466)
2 CONT **Sir Edward Hastings, 2nd Baron Hastings (1466 - 1506)
2 CONT **Richard Hastings (born 1468)
2 CONT **William Hastings (a470 - after 1540)
2 CONT **Anne Hastings (c.1471 - 1520) married George Talbot, 4th Earl of Shrewsbury
2 CONT *Sir William was charged with treason and beheaded 13 June 1483. '''Katherine was taken under the protection of Richard II, but lost many of her properties despite his promises.
2 CONT *'''Katherine did not remarry and left a will dated 22 Nov 1503, proven 25 March 1504, but her exact death is unknown.
2 CONT *Thank you Anne Shurtleff Stevens for all this information.
2 CONT *Family links: 
2 CONT * Parents:
2 CONT *  Richard Neville (1400 - 1460)
2 CONT *  Alice Montagu Neville (1406 - 1462)
2 CONT * Spouses:
2 CONT *'''  William Hastings (1431 - 1483)
2 CONT *'''  William Bonville (____ - 1460)*
2 CONT * Children:
2 CONT **  Cecily Bonville de Grey (1460 - 1530)*
2 CONT **  Edward Hastings (1466 - 1506)*
2 CONT **  Anne Hastings Talbot (1471 - 1520)*
2 CONT * Siblings:
2 CONT *  Thomas Neville (____ - 1460)*
2 CONT *  Joan Nevill Fitzalan (____ - 1462)*
2 CONT *  Cicely de Neville Beauchamp Tiptoft (1424 - 1450)*
2 CONT *  Richard Neville (1428 - 1471)**
2 CONT *  John De Neville (1431 - 1471)*
2 CONT *  Eleanor de Neville Stanley (1438 - 1464)*
2 CONT *  Katherine de Neville Hastings (1442 - 1504)
2 CONT * *Calculated relationship
2 CONT * **Half-sibling
