2 CONT *THE DAU. JANE NEVILLE WIFE OF SIR HENRY POLE IS LISTED IN OTHER REFERENCES AS THE DAU. OF HER SON SIR GEORGE NEVILLE & JOAN FITZALAN
2 CONT *'''Sir George Neville, 2nd Lord Abergavenny1
2 CONT *'''M, #14221, b. circa 1440, d. 20 September 1492
2 CONT *Last Edited=18 Jan 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=1.23%
2 CONT *'''     Sir George Neville, 2nd Lord Abergavenny was born circa 1440.1 He was the son of Sir Edward Neville, 1st Lord Abergavenny and Elizabeth Beauchamp, Lady Bergavenny.1 He married, firstly, Margaret Fenne, daughter of Sir Hug
2 CONC h Fenne, before 1469.1 He married, secondly, Elizabeth (?) after 1485.2 He died on 20 September 1492.
2 CONT *'''     He was invested as a Knight on 4 May 1471 at Tewkesbury, Gloucestershire, England, by King Edward IV.1 He succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Abergavenny [E., 1450] on 18 October 1476.1 On 12 January 1476/77 he had livery 
2 CONC of the lands of his parents, but he never had seizin of Abergavenny.1
2 CONT *'''Children of Sir George Neville, 2nd Lord Abergavenny and Margaret Fenne
