2 CONT *Edward NEVILLE (1° B. Abergavenny)
2 CONT *Born: ABT 1412/1417, Raby, Durham, England
2 CONT *Died: 18 Oct 1476
2 CONT *Buried: Priory Church, Abergavenny, Monmouth, England
2 CONT *Notes: he inherited her first wife family title. He cohabited with his second wife, Catherine, during the lifetime of his first, Elizabeth. He was created 1st Lord Abergavenny on 5 Sep 1450.
2 CONT *Father: Ralph NEVILLE (1° E. Westmoreland)
2 CONT *Mother: Joan BEAUFORT (C. Westmoreland)
2 CONT *Married 1: Elizabeth BEAUCHAMP (b. 1415 - d. 18 Jun 1447) (descendant of Edward III) BEF 18 Oct 1424
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Alice NEVILLE
2 CONT **2. Richard NEVILLE
2 CONT **3. Elizabeth NEVILLE
2 CONT **4. George NEVILLE (2° B. Abergavenny)
2 CONT **5. Henry NEVILLE (b. ABT 1444)
2 CONT *Married 2: Catherine HOWARD 15 Oct 1448 in Dispensation
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **6. Margaret NEVILLE (B. Cobham)
2 CONT **7. Catherine NEVILLE
2 CONT **8. Anne NEVILLE (B. Strange of Knockin)
2 CONT **9. Henry NEVILLE (Sir Knight)
2 CONT **10. William NEVILLE
2 CONT **'''11. Edward NEVILLE
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/NEVILLE4.htm#Edward NEVILLE (1° B. Abergavenny) ____________
2 CONT *'''Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900, Volume 40
2 CONT *Neville, Edward (d.1476)     by James Tait
2 CONT *NEVILLE, EDWARD (d. 1476), Baron of Bergavenny or Abergavenny (a form which appeared in the sixteenth century and was not definitely adopted until 1730), was the sixth and youngest son of Ralph Neville, first earl of Westmoreland
2 CONC  [q. v.], by his second wife, Joan Beaufort, daughter of John of Gaunt, duke of Lancaster. His father had arranged, before his death in 1425, the match which made his youngest son the founder of the house which alone among the Nev
2 CONC ille branches has been continued in the male line to our own day, and is now represented by the Marquis of Abergavenny (Wills and Inventories, Surtees Soc. i. 71). The lady was Elizabeth Beauchamp, only child and heiress of Richar
2 CONC d, earl of Worcester, who died in April 1422 of wounds received at the siege of Meaux. Worcester's father, William Beauchamp, fourth son of Thomas Beauchamp, earl of Warwick (d. 1369), by Catherine, daughter of Roger Mortimer, fir
2 CONC st earl of March [q. v.], inherited the castle and lands of Bergavenny or Abergavenny on Usk on the death of the last Hastings, earl of Pembroke, whose father, being on the maternal side a nephew of William Beauchamp's mother, had
2 CONC  (15 April 1372) placed his cousin next in the entail (Nicolas, Historic Peerage, ed. Courthope; Complete Peerage, ed. G. E. C. p. 14). .... etc.
2 CONT *Abergavenny's second wife was Catherine Howard, daughter of Sir Robert Howard, and sister of John Howard, first duke of Norfolk. His first wife is said to have died on 18 June 1448 (Doyle; Swallow, p. 231), and he then married Ca
2 CONC therine Howard. But he was excommunicated for doing so on the ground that they had had illicit relations during his wife's lifetime, and were within the third degree of consanguinity. Pope Nicholas V was, however, persuaded to gra
2 CONC nt a dispensation for the marriage. Dugdale gives 15 Oct. 1448 as the date of the bull, which, supposing the date of Elizabeth Beauchamp's death to be correct, does not leave much time for the intermediate proceedings. Both dates 
2 CONC are irreconcileable with the age (twenty-six) which Dugdale (from the Escheat Roll) gives to her second son at his father's death in 1476. Sir Harris Nicolas gives thirty-six as his age, and, if this is a correction and not an err
2 CONC or, it will remove the worst difficulty. It is certainly most unlikely that George Neville should have been born at Raby Castle in 1450 (cf. Paston Letters, i. 397).
2 CONT *'''The children of the second marriage were two sons''', Ralph and '''Edward, who died without issue''', and three daughters: Margaret, who married John Brooke, baron Cobham (d. 1506); Anne, who married Lord Strange (d. 1497), fa
2 CONC ther of the second Earl of Derby; and Catherine, who married Robert Tanfield.  .... etc.
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Neville,_Edward_(d.1476)_(DNB00) _____________
