1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The family include the Nevilles of Abergavenny, Wellingore, Auborn, Kewland Hall, Skelbrooke, Chevet, Thorney, Tasburgh Hall and the Nevilles of Raby Castle. Each bore similar Coat of Arms with the Motto "NeVile Ve
2 CONC lis" meaning "Form no Vile wish or thought."
2 CONT
2 CONT On the spelling of the surname Neville, the Abergavenny branch reject the final "e", while the Braybroooke branch retain it. For the sake of further distinction, the Grove, Chevet, Holbeck, Skelbrooke and Wellingore baranchs omit 
2 CONC one "L". In the old manuscripts, from "De Nova Villa", we get Neuville, Nevylle, Nevyll, Nevyl, Nevill and Nevil while the Latimers are frequently styled Nevell, but the prevailing form is Nevyll or Nevill.
2 CONT *__________
2 CONT *http://www.thepeerage.com/p1181.htm#i11809
2 CONT *''''''Margaret Neville1
2 CONT *''''''F, #11809, b. after 1448, d. 30 September 1506
