2 CONT *[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1027. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pee
2 CONC rage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p18919.htm#i189187 __________________
2 CONT *'''Alice NEVILLE
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1437, Roxborough Castle, Tyrone, Ireland
2 CONT *Father: William NEVILLE (1° E. Kent)
2 CONT *Mother: Joan FAUCONBERGE (B. Fauconberge)
2 CONT *'''Married: John CONYERS (Sir Knight)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. William CONYERS (1º B. Conyers of Hornby)
2 CONT **2. Margery CONYERS
2 CONT **3. Anne CONYERS
2 CONT **4. John CONYERS
2 CONT **5. Eleanor CONYERS
2 CONT **6. Reginald CONYERS
2 CONT **7. Elizabeth CONYERS
2 CONT **8. Jane CONYERS
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/NEVILLE2.htm#Alice NEVILLE2 _____________
2 CONT *William Conyers, 1st Baron Conyers (21 December 1468 – 14 April 1524), also known as William Conyers of Hornby, was an English baron and aristocrat.
2 CONT *Conyers was a '''son of Sir John Conyers of Hornby and Lady Alice Neville''',[1] daughter of William Neville, 1st Earl of Kent. His first wife was Hon. Mary le Scrope, daughter of Sir John Scrope, 5th Baron Scrope of Bolton. His 
2 CONC second wife was Lady Anne Neville, daughter of Ralph Neville, 3rd Earl of Westmorland. He rebuilt Hornby Castle in Swaledale, Yorkshire, which the Conyers had inherited.
2 CONT *He served the king on several military expeditions to Scotland and also fought at the Battle of Flodden in 1513.
2 CONT *Conyers was created 1st Baron Conyers on 17 October 1509.[2] He was succeeded by Christopher Conyers, one of his sons by Anne. His daughter Katherine (d. 1566) married Sir Francis Bigod.[3]
2 CONT *From:  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Conyers,_1st_Baron_Conyers HAS WRONG LINK TO FATHER _________________________
2 CONT *'''Alice Neville was born about 1437 and died 11 Dec 1490.
2 CONT *Parents:  William Neville, Earl of Kent,   b. Abt 1405, of, Alnwick, Northumberland, England ,   d. 9 Jan 1462-1463, Alnwick, Northumberland, England   and Joan de Faucomberge,   b. 18 Oct 1406, Skelton, Yorkshire, England ,   d.
2 CONC  11 Dec 1490 
2 CONT *Married:
2 CONT *'''# bef 28 Apr 1422 to John Conyers, of Hornby,Yorkshire, England.  d. 26 Jul 1469, Danesmoor, Edgcote, Northamptonshire, England. He was the son of Sir John Conyers (d. abt 1489) and Margaret Darcy (b. 1418 in Ravensworth)
2 CONT *4 children include:
2 CONT **# John Conyers,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT **# William Conyers, Lord Conyers,   b. 21 Dec 1468,   d. 1524
2 CONT **# Margery Conyers,   d. 10 May 1524
2 CONT **# Anne Conyers,   d. 1530
2 CONT *==Notes==
2 CONT *CONDITION: 2 sons and 2 daughters of this marriage. 	
2 CONT *KINSHIP: 3rd daughter and coheiress.
2 CONT *BIRTH: Date Approximated> Age being 26+ years in 1463.
2 CONT *DEATH: Date> Sometime prior to 11 Dec 1490 (death date of her mother).
2 CONT *==MedLands Pedigree==
2 CONT *-        EARLS of SALISBURY. 
2 CONT *11.      WILLIAM (-[Alnwick] 9 Jan 1463, bur Guisborough Priory).  He was created Earl of Kent in 1461.  m (before 28 Apr 1422) as her first husband, JOAN Baroness Fauconberge, daughter of Sir THOMAS de Faucomberge of Skelton Lor
2 CONC d Fauconberge & his second wife Joan Brounflete of Londesborough, Yorkshire (Skelton, Yorkshire 18 Oct 1406-11 Dec 1490).  According to the Complete Peerage, she was “a fool and idiot from birth”[598].  She married secondly (Pardo
2 CONC n for marrying without royal licence 14 Mar 1463) John Berwyke.  William & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT **a)         JOAN ([1435]-after 22 Feb 1472).  m (before 1463) Sir EDWARD Bethum of Beetham, Westmoreland (-22 Feb 1472). 
2 CONT **b)         ELIZABETH ([1435]-before 1488).  m (before 1463) as his first wife, RICHARD Strangways of West Harlsey, Yorkshire (-13 Apr 1488).  
2 CONT **'''c)         ALICE (1437-before 1490).  m (before 1463) JOHN Conyers, son of Sir JOHN Conyers of Hornby, Yorkshire & his wife --- (-killed in battle Edgecote Field 26 Jul 1469).''' 
2 CONT *William had two illegitimate children by an unknown mistress: 
2 CONT **d)         THOMAS Fauconbridge (-executed [Sep] 1471). 
2 CONT **e)         WILLIAM (-after 1482). 
2 CONT *==Links==
