3 CONT Richard III of England is Walter G. Ashworth's first cousin 15 times removed!
2 NOTE Richard III King of England
3 CONT
3 CONT The burial site of Richard III either York or Leicester.  Even though York the York Minster holds services and they are sometimes regarded as on the High Church or Anglo-Catholic end of the Anglican continuum. It is still not a Ca
3 CONC tholic church, nor is the Leicester Cathedral.  That said either way he would not entombed in a Catholic Church.  So here is the important point. He was a King. Now what matters no matter what you conjure up, Kings for the most pa
3 CONC rt want to be recognized. In his case he definitely wanted to be KING. 
3 CONT Lets look at a little history: Richard was a royal prince until the death of his brother Edward IV in 1483. Appointed as protector of his nephew, Edward V, Richard instead assumed the reins of power.
3 CONT Edward and his brother Richard, known as the Princes in the Tower, disappeared soon after. Rumors circulated they had been murdered on the orders of their uncle.
3 CONT
3 CONT Where would the most amounts of people pay tribute to see his tomb?
3 CONT
3 CONT York is located 211 miles from London, three and half to four hours away on a good day.
3 CONT Long trip unless you stay over. Less people likely to visit. Less recognition. 
3 CONT
3 CONT Leicester is located 100 miles north of London, two, two and half-hours away. 
3 CONT A very nice days outing. 
3 CONT REMEMDER: Richard III wanted to be King and this King wanted recognition. 
3 CONT He did not die in battle while hiding. He wanted to lead and be seen. He was out there on the battlefield. Bury his remains in Leicester where he will be visited the most, get the recognition he craved for and this the site where 
3 CONC the Battle of Bosworth took place in 1485 and infamous as the place where King Richard III lost his life and crown to Henry Tudor and thus where the Tudor dynasty was born. Richard III King of England, died defending this ground. 
3 CONC Bury him there. 
3 CONT
3 CONT Walter G. Ashworth 16th Great Nephew of Richard III King of England
3 CONT Great Grandson of:
3 CONT • Uther Pendragon "The Head Dragon" ap Custennyn, King of Britons • c. 430 – 476
