2 CONT ________
2 CONT '''Maurice Denys''' (c. 1410–1466), Esquire, of Siston, Gloucestershire, was twice Sheriff of Gloucestershire in 1460 and 1461.[1] The Denys family were stated by Sir Robert Atkyns, the 18th-century historian of Gloucestershire, t
2 CONC o have provided more sheriffs for that county than any other family.[2]
2 CONT Family background
2 CONT He was the eldest son and heir of Sir Gilbert Denys (d. 1422) of Siston, Glos., by his 3rd wife Margaret Russell (d. 1460), eldest daughter of Sir Maurice Russell of Dyrham, Glos.
2 CONT Birth and baptism
2 CONT etc
2 CONT '''First marriage'''
2 CONT '''Sir Edward Stradling had obtained not only the wardship of Maurice but also his marriage. He exercised this right by marrying him off to his daughter, Katherine Stradling, who was thus provided with a husband of ample means. Ye
2 CONC t Katherine it appears died very soon after giving birth in about 1437 to the couple's first son''', Sir Walter Denys (c. 1437–1505).
2 CONT Second marriage
2 CONT '''Maurice married secondly''', before 1 November 1437, Alice Poyntz, daughter of Nicholas Poyntz of Iron Acton, Glos. By his second wife Elizabeth Hussey, daughter of Henry Hussey of Sussex.[7] The family of Poyntz was prominent 
2 CONC in the Gloucestershire gentry, of ancient lineage, and their principal manor of Iron Acton lay between the Denys manors of Siston and Alveston. '''Maurice''' had 8 children by Alice Poyntz, including Hugh Denys (d. 1511), groom of
2 CONC  the stool to King Henry VII (1485–1509).
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT Death and burial
2 CONT '''Maurice died in 1466 and was buried in the chancel of Olveston Church as the Denys brass of 1505 in that church states.'''
2 CONT Denys monumental brass, 1505, Olveston Church
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maurice_Denys_(sheriff)
2 CONT _____
2 CONT '''Maurice Denys'''
2 CONT Birth	1410
2 CONT Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT Death	1 Sep 1466 (aged 55–56)
2 CONT Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT Burial	St. Mary the Virgin Churchyard
2 CONT Olveston, South Gloucestershire Unitary Authority, Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT Find a Grave Memorial ID: 102021506
2 CONT Esquire, of Olverston and Earthcott, Gloucestershire. Sheriff of Gloucestershire, son and heir of Sir Gilbert Dennis of Siston, Knight of the Shire and Sheriff by his second wife, Margaret Russell.
2 CONT '''Maurice was a ward''' of Sir Edward Stradling, as his father died when he was twelve, and a full record of his birth and baptism is included in a 1431 inquisition at Tetbury. '''Maurice was born into the Denys''' family who "pr
2 CONC ovided more sheriffs for Gloucester than any other."
2 CONT '''Maurice married Katherine Stradling and they had two sons when she was only 14,''' Sir Walter and John, '''before she died at a young age. Maurice would remarry''' to Alice Poyntz, the daughter of Nicholas from Iron Acton, Glou
2 CONC cestershire, about 1437. They had three sons and four daughters; Hugh, Maurice, Francis, Isabel, Jane, Emme and Alice.
2 CONT Due to his mother remarrying a younger man, Stradling's nephew, after his father's death, due to Stradling's insistence, '''Maurice was never able to enjoy his inheritance.'''
2 CONT '''Maurice was buried in the chancel of Olverston parish church, St Mary's.'''
