0 @N6000000002188579681@ NOTE George Nevill, 1st Baron Latymer
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT George Nevill, 1st Baron Latymer (died 30 December 1469), was an English peer.
1 CONT
1 CONT Nevill was the fifth son of Ralph de Nevill, 1st Earl of Westmorland, by his second wife Lady Joan de Beaufort, daughter of John of Gaunt, 1st Duke of Lancaster. He succeeded to the Latymer estates on the death of his uncle John N
1 CONC evill, 6th Baron Latimer, in 1430 (see the Baron Latimer), and in 1432 he was summoned to Parliament as Lord Latymer. He later fought in Scotland in 1436, was a Justice of the Peace for Cumberland in 1437 and admitted to the Privy
1 CONC  Council in 1439.
1 CONT
1 CONT Lord Latymer married Lady Elizabeth, daughter of Richard de Beauchamp, 13th Earl of Warwick, in 1437. He died in December 1469 and was succeeded in the barony by his grandson Richard, his eldest son Sir Henry Neville having predec
1 CONC eased him.
1 CONT Peerage of England
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT New Creation Baron Latymer
1 CONT 1432–1469 Succeeded by
1 CONT Richard Nevill
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Kidd, Charles, Williamson, David (editors). Debrett's Peerage and Baronetage (1990 edition). New York: St Martin's Press, 1990.
