1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT
1 CONT Her children with Richard Plantagenet, 3rd Duke of York include:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Joan of York (1438).
1 CONT    2. Anne of York (August 10, 1439 – January 14, 1476), consort to Henry Holland, 3rd Duke of Exeter.
1 CONT    3. Henry of York (b. February 10, 1441).
1 CONT    4. Edward IV of England (April 28, 1442 – April 9, 1483).
1 CONT    5. Edmund, Earl of Rutland (May 17, 1443 – December 31, 1460).
1 CONT    6. Elizabeth of York (April 22, 1444 – after January, 1503), consort to John de la Pole, 2nd Duke of Suffolk.
1 CONT    7. Margaret of York (May 3, 1446 – November 23, 1503). Married Charles I, Duke of Burgundy.
1 CONT    8. William of York (b. July 7, 1447).
1 CONT    9. John of York (b. November 7, 1448).
1 CONT   10. George Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Clarence (October 21, 1449 – February 18, 1478).
1 CONT   11. Thomas of York (born c. 1451).
1 CONT   12. Richard III of England (October 2, 1452 – August 22, 1485).
1 CONT   13. Ursula of York (born 22 July 1455).
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Namesake Niece
1 CONT
1 CONT While the mother of two English kings was the most notable woman named Cecily Neville, she was not the only historical figure to bear that name.
1 CONT
1 CONT Cecily Neville (1424 - 28 July 1450) was a namesake niece of the above. She was a daughter of Richard Neville, 5th Earl of Salisbury and Alice Montagu, Countess of Salisbury. She was also an older sister of Richard Neville, 16th E
1 CONC arl of Warwick, John Neville, 1st Marquess of Montagu and George Neville (Archbishop of York and Chancellor of England).
1 CONT
1 CONT She first married Henry de Beauchamp, 1st Duke of Warwick and the only King of the Isle of Wight (as well as of Jersey and Guernsey). Their only daughter was Anne Beauchamp, 15th Countess of Warwick.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her second husband was John Tiptoft, 1st Earl of Worcester. They had no children.
1 CONT
1 CONT Little more is known of her.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Fictional Portrayls
1 CONT
1 CONT Cecily Neville as the Duchess of York has been portrayed by many noted actresses in various films and television programs. Actresses who have played the role include: Elinor Aickin, Eleanor Bron,Annette Crosbie, Helen Haye, Mary H
1 CONC inton, Anne Jeffreys, Janet May, and Maggie Smith.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Joanna Laynesmith - The King's Mother (History Today March 2006)
1 CONT
