0 @N6000000003658776136@ NOTE He and his wife Marguerite des Baux were 6th cousins (both descendants of King John, he from Henry III and she from John's daughter Eleanore)
1 CONT
1 CONT From Plantagenet Ancestry:
1 CONT
1 CONT PIERRE DE LUXEMBORUG, Count of Conversano (in Apulia) and Brienne (in Champagne), seigneur of Enghien (in Hainault) and Fiennes, Knight of the Golden Fleece, son and heir, born at Naples, Italy in 1390.  He married 8 May 1405 MARG
1 CONC UERITE DES BAUX .... They had six sons ... and three daughters ....  He was heir in 1430 to his cousin, Philippe, Duke of Lorraine, Brabant, and Limburg, by which he succeeded to title Count of Saint-Pol (in Artois).  PIERRE DE LU
1 CONC XEMBOURG, Count of Saint-Pol, Conversano, and Brienne, died at Rambures 31 August 1433 and was buried at the Abbey of Cercamp (in Artois).  His widow, Marguerite, died 15 Nov. 1469, and was buried at Cercamp.
