0 @N6000000002187742527@ NOTE John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl (born c. 1440– September 19, 1512), also known as Sir John Stewart of Balveny, was created the 1st Earl of Atholl in around 1457.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the oldest child of Joan Beaufort, widowed Queen of James I of Scotland, and Sir James Stewart, the Black Knight of Lorn.
1 CONT
1 CONT He having married twice, first to Margaret (Beatrix) Douglas also known as the 'fair Maid of Gallowy' with whom he had 2 daughters:
1 CONT
1 CONT Janet Stewart 
1 CONT Elizabeth Stewart. 
1 CONT From his second marriage to Eleanor St Clair, nine children were born:
1 CONT
1 CONT John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Atholl 
1 CONT Andrew Stewart. the Bishop of Caithness 
1 CONT Lady Jean Stewart 
1 CONT Catherine Stewart 
1 CONT Elspeth Stewart (who married Sir Robert Innes of Innermarky) 
1 CONT Marjory Steart 
1 CONT Margaret Steart 
1 CONT Isabel Steart 
1 CONT Lady Anne Stewart 
1 CONT He is believed to have had a hand in suppressing the rebellion of the John, Earl of Ross, the last of the Lord of the Isles, and it is reported that it from this that his nephew King James III took these words as his motto.
