0 @N6000000000604975381@ NOTE Margaret Beaufort1 (F) b. 31 May 1443, d. 29 June 1504, #101897d. 29 Jun 1504|p10190.htm#i101897|Sir John Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset|b. b 25 Mar 1404d. 27 May 1444|p10198.htm#i101976|Margaret Beauchamp|b. b 1412d. 8 Aug 1482|p
1 CONC 10198.htm#i101978|Sir John de Beaufort, 1st Earl of Somerset|b. bt 1371 - 1373d. 16 Mar 1409/10|p10198.htm#i101971|Lady Margaret de Holand|b. bt 1381 - 1385d. 31 Dec 1439|p10224.htm#i102237|John Beauchamp|b. b 1396d. Apr 1412|p107
1 CONC 33.htm#i107328|Edith Stourton|b. b 1405d. 13 Jun 1441|p10733.htm#i107329|');"Pedigree <JavaScript:pup('Margaret Beaufort|b. 31 May 1443<BR> Last Edited=22 May 2004
1 CONT Margaret Beaufort was the daughter of Sir John Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset <p10198.htm> and Margaret Beauchamp <p10198.htm>.1 She was born on 31 May 1443 at Bletsoe Castle, Bedfordshire, England.2 She married, firstly, John de 
1 CONC la Pole, 2nd Duke of Suffolk <p10499.htm> between 28 January 1450 and 7 February 1450.2,3 She married, secondly, Sir Edmund Tudor, 1st Earl of Richmond, son of Sir Owen Tudor <p10200.htm> and Catherine de France <p10187.htm>, on 1
1 CONC  November 1455 at Bletsoe Castle, Bedfordshire.2 She married, thirdly, Sir Henry Stafford <p10200.htm>, son of Humphrey de Stafford, 1st Duke of Buckingham <p10743.htm> and Lady Anne Neville <p10743.htm>, circa 1462.3 She married,
1 CONC  fourthly, Thomas Stanley, 1st Earl of Derby <p10500.htm>, son of Thomas Stanley, 1st Baron Stanley <p1385.htm> and Jean Goushill <p1385.htm>, before October 1473.3 She died on 29 June 1504 at age 61 at Abbot's House, Cheyney Gate
1 CONC s, Westminster, London, England.4,3 She was buried at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.2  Her marriage to John de la Pole, 2nd Duke of Suffolk was annulled before 24 March 1453.2 Through her marriage, Margaret Beauf
1 CONC ort gained the title of Countess of Richmond on 1 November 1455. She was invested as a Lady Companion, Order of the Garter (L.G.) in 1488.2 Margaret founded both Christ's College and St. John's College at Cambridge.
1 CONT Child of Margaret Beaufort and Sir Edmund Tudor, 1st Earl of Richmond:
1 CONT Henry VII Tudor, King of England <p10142.htm>+ b. 28 Jan 1457, d. 21 Apr 1509
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S6 <s1.htm>] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant,
1 CONC  Extinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 45. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
1 CONT [S11 <s1.htm>] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 148. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
1 CONT [S8 <s1.htm>] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 220. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baro
1 CONC netage, 106th edition.
1 CONT [S11 <s1.htm>] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family, page 148, says 29 June 1509.
