1 CONT Indian origin, it was cut as a double rose with 126 facets. Once owned by
1 CONT Charles the Bold who lost it when he fell in battle in 1477. The stone came
1 CONT into the possession of Pope Julius II & the Medici family in the 16th century.
1 CONT Maria Theresa of Austria acquired it through her marriage & it became part of
1 CONT the Austrian crown jewels. Seized by the Germans prior to World War II, it was
1 CONT recovered & returned by the U.S. 3rd Army to the Viennese by Gen. Mark Clark.
