0 @N6000000007329648746@ NOTE [Kopi av ROYALS.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Reign: 1483-85;  Although Richard, the last king of the house of York, did
1 CONT usurp the throne, little doubt exists that his unscrupulousness has been
1 CONT overemphasizedby his enemies and by Tudor historians seeking to strengthen the
1 CONT Lancastrian position.  His baseness is strongly exaggerated in Shakepeare's
1 CONT play, Richard III.  He is said to have murdered his nephews, Edward V, and
1 CONT Richard, Duke of York in 1483 (called the Princes in the Tower).  Richard III
1 CONT met his death at the Battle of Bosworth.
0 @N6000000002906274152@ NOTE !SOURCE:  Gary Boyd Roberts, The Royal Descents of 500 Immigrants to the
1 CONT American Colonies or the United States, at 204 (1992).
0 @N6000000000640046577@ NOTE Sir Harry was once taken prisoner by a Breton pirate, and the ransom cost his father three manors and the lordship of Sutton-in-St. Bride's. 
1 CONT     Following in the footsteps of his father and his grandfather, he left for Jerusalem in 1476/77.  By the end of March of the year, he had reached Rome, where he wrote his wife a letter describing his journey so far.  He managed
1 CONC  to leave the Holy City with his knighthood of the Holy Sepulchre, but on his return to England, he died on Cyprus, and was buried at Famagusta.
0 @N6000000001877534346@ NOTE Sir
1 CONT Source GWH
1 CONT www.thepeerage.com
1 CONT www.stirnet.com
1 CONT rootsweb turner-thomas
0 @N6000000006444278768@ NOTE [ken connect 2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [Brøderbund WFT Vol. 14, Ed. 1, Tree #1463, Date of Import: Mar 3, 2004]
1 CONT
1 CONT In passing from St. Donats to his seat in Somersetshire, Sir Henry was
1 CONT imprisoned by Colin Dolphin, a pirate of Britany.  His ransom was rated so
1 CONT high -- 2200 marks -- that he was compelled to sell for its liquidation
1 CONT his two manors in Oxforshire, the castle and manor of Rogerstown, calle in
1 CONT Welsh Re-Gwilyn, together with the lordship of Setton, in Monmothshire.
1 CONT Later he visited the Holy Sepulchre; in returning, he died in the Isle of
1 CONT Cyprus at the age of 25, and was buried in the city of Famagusta.
